Dialogue: 0,0:01:22.71,0:01:24.75,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}非常感谢，先生。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Thank you very much, sir.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:24.92,0:01:26.80,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}干得漂亮，太漂亮了。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You did a wonderful job. Wonderful.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:28.59,0:01:30.84,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我们办到了，皮特。我们办到了。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}- We did it, Pete. We did it.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:32.76,0:01:34.55,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}有那么一会儿，我们还担心来着。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}- For a moment, we had our doubts.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:34.72,0:01:38.26,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}接下来，你们已听取了一桩漫长而复杂的案件，\N{\rEN\blur0.8}To continue, you've listened to a long and complex case,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:38.43,0:01:39.68,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}一级谋杀。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}murder in the first degree.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:40.27,0:01:45.19,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}预谋谋杀是我们刑事法庭审理的最严重指控。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}A premeditated murder is the most serious charge tried in our criminal courts.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:45.36,0:01:46.73,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你们听取了证词。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You've listened to the testimony.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:46.90,0:01:48.02,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}已经向你们宣读了法律\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You've had the law read to you
Dialogue: 0,0:01:48.19,0:01:50.03,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}并解释了其在本案中的适用。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}and interpreted as it applies in this case.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:50.19,0:01:54.07,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}现在你们的职责是坐下来，努力分清事实与臆想。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}It's now your duty to sit down and try and separate the facts from the fancy.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:54.99,0:01:58.37,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}一个人死了，另一个人的生命危在旦夕。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}One man is dead. Another man's life is at stake.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:59.33,0:02:00.95,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}如果你们心中存在合理怀疑\N{\rEN\blur0.8}If there's a reasonable doubt in your minds
Dialogue: 0,0:02:01.12,0:02:03.08,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}对被告是否有罪存有合理怀疑，\N{\rEN\blur0.8}as to the guilt of the accused,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:03.25,0:02:04.58,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}合理怀疑，\N{\rEN\blur0.8}a reasonable doubt,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:05.42,0:02:07.63,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那你们就必须给我一个无罪判决。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}then you must bring me a verdict of not guilty.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:08.21,0:02:10.17,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}但如果不存在合理怀疑，\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Now if, however, there's no reasonable doubt,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:10.34,0:02:14.13,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那你们就必须凭良心判定被告有罪。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}then you must in good conscience find the accused guilty.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:15.43,0:02:19.18,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}无论你们如何决定，裁决必须一致。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}However you decide, your verdict must be unanimous.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:19.35,0:02:22.14,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}如果你们判定被告有罪，\N{\rEN\blur0.8}In the event that you find the accused guilty,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:22.93,0:02:25.69,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}法庭不会考虑从宽处理的建议。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}the bench will not entertain a recommendation for mercy.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:26.35,0:02:29.27,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}本案必须判处死刑。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}The death sentence is mandatory in this case.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:30.02,0:02:33.32,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你们肩负着重大责任。谢谢各位。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You're faced with a grave responsibility. Thank you, gentlemen.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:35.32,0:02:37.37,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}候补陪审员可以退席。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}The alternate jurors are excused.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:43.37,0:02:45.12,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}陪审团现在退庭商议。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}The jury will now retire.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:03.10,0:03:05.69,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I
Dialogue: 0,0:04:43.53,0:04:45.20,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}试试这扇。看我能打开不。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Try this one. See if I can get it.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:46.45,0:04:47.62,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}今天真闷热。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}It's a muggy day.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:51.58,0:04:54.17,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-嘿。哦，哦。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Hey. Oh, oh.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:06.01,0:05:08.31,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-来片口香糖？  -不了，谢谢。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Piece of gum?   -No, thanks.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:08.48,0:05:10.35,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}这玩意儿...\N{\rEN\blur0.8}This thing is...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:10.52,0:05:11.98,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-嗯？  -...挪一下。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Huh?   -...move it.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:13.56,0:05:15.61,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-来，我帮你一把。  -帮我弄一下那个。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Come on, I'll give you a hand.   -Give me a hand with that.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:15.77,0:05:17.15,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}一、二、三……好了。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}One, two three... that's it.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:18.90,0:05:21.36,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}呼。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Phew.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:22.99,0:05:24.57,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-你知道吗？  -什么？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-You know something?   -Yeah?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:24.74,0:05:26.37,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我早上打电话问过气象局。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I called the weather bureau this morning.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:26.54,0:05:28.29,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}今天会是今年最热的一天。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}This is gonna be the hottest day of the year.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:28.45,0:05:29.45,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}也许吧。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Could be.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:30.04,0:05:32.00,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}天哪，他们至少该给这种地方装空调。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Boy, you'd think they'd at least air-condition these places.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:32.16,0:05:35.17,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-先生，你叫什么名字？  -哦，是...是那个，对。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-What is your name, sir?   -Oh, it's... that one, yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:35.34,0:05:36.71,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}非常感谢。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Thank you very much.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:36.88,0:05:39.21,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}好了，各位，人都到齐了。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Okay, gentlemen, everybody's here.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:39.96,0:05:42.72,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}如果你们需要什么，我就在门外。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Now, if there's anything you want, I'll be right outside the door.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:42.88,0:05:44.89,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-敲门就行。  -好，谢谢，我们会的。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Just knock.   -Okay, thanks. We will.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:57.65,0:06:00.32,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}早上好。我都不知道他们会锁门。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Good morning. I never knew they locked the door.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:00.48,0:06:02.44,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}当然锁门。你以为呢？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Sure they lock the door. What'd you think?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:03.49,0:06:05.95,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}不知道，我就是没想到。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I don't know. It just never occurred to me.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:07.53,0:06:08.62,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那是干什么用的？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}What's that for?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:09.62,0:06:11.54,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}哦，我想我们也许想用选票表决。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Oh, I thought we might want to vote by ballot.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:11.70,0:06:14.16,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}好主意。说不定还能把他选进参议院。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Great idea. Maybe we can get him elected senator.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:16.54,0:06:17.54,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}以防万一，你懂的。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Just in case, you know.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:21.76,0:06:24.05,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-你觉得怎么样？  -哦，我不知道。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-How''d you like it?   -Oh, I don't know.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:24.22,0:06:25.51,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}挺有意思的。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}It was pretty interesting.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:25.68,0:06:28.18,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-是吗？我差点睡着了。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Yeah? I almost fell asleep.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:28.35,0:06:30.39,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我是说，我以前从没当过陪审员。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I mean, I've never been on a jury before.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:30.56,0:06:33.10,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}是吗？我当过很多次陪审员。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}No? I've sat on many juries.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:34.35,0:06:37.23,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}让我受不了的是那些律师说啊说啊说个没完\N{\rEN\blur0.8}What gets me is the way those lawyers talk and talk and talk
Dialogue: 0,0:06:37.40,0:06:39.48,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}哪怕是像这样一目了然的案子。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}even when it's an open-and-shut case like this one.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:39.65,0:06:41.28,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我是说，你听过这么多废话吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I mean, did you ever hear so much talk about nothing?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:41.44,0:06:42.99,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}嗯，我想他们有这个权利。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Well, I guess they're entitled.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:43.15,0:06:45.53,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}是啊，他们有权利。制度就是这样，可是...\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Yeah, they're entitled. It's the system, but...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:46.78,0:06:49.16,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}要我说，就该把那些小混混狠狠收拾一顿\N{\rEN\blur0.8}If you ask me, I'd slap those tough kids down
Dialogue: 0,0:06:49.33,0:06:50.83,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}在他们惹事之前。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}before they start any trouble.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:51.33,0:06:53.00,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}能省我们很多时间和钱。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}It would save us a lot of time and money.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:53.16,0:06:54.87,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-嘿，我们开始吧？  -好主意。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Hey, let's get started, huh?   -That's a good idea.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:55.04,0:06:57.46,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}对，开始吧？我们大概都有事要办。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Yeah, let's get goin', huh? We probably all got things to do here.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:57.63,0:06:59.46,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我想我们先休息五分钟。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I figured we'd start out with a five-minute break.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:59.63,0:07:01.30,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}还有一位先生在洗手间，陪审长先生。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}There's one gentleman in the bathroom, Mr. Foreman
Dialogue: 0,0:07:01.46,0:07:04.55,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-我们...我们要按顺序坐吗？  -哎呀，我不知道。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Are... are we gonna sit in order?   -Gee, I don't know.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:04.72,0:07:06.22,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我...嗯，应该是吧。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I... Well, I guess so.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:11.47,0:07:12.85,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你坐了我的位子。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You're in my seat.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:13.02,0:07:14.77,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-哦，抱歉。  -没关系。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Oh, excuse me.   -That's all right.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:17.44,0:07:19.19,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}嘿，这景色不错嘛？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Hey, that's not a bad view, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:22.82,0:07:24.28,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你觉得这个案子怎么样？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}What did you think of the case?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:25.36,0:07:27.07,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我是说，我觉得挺有意思。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I mean, it had a lot of interest for me.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:27.57,0:07:30.45,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}没有真正...冷场的地方。你懂我意思吧？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}No real... dead spots. You know what I mean?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:31.49,0:07:33.58,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}跟你说，能摊上谋杀案算我们走运。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I tell you, we were lucky to get a murder case.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:34.24,0:07:36.21,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我还以为会是个袭击或盗窃案。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I figured us for an assault or burglary.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:36.37,0:07:39.21,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}天哪，那种案子最无聊了。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Boy, they can be the dullest.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:39.88,0:07:42.50,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}嘿，那是伍尔沃斯大楼吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Hey. That the Woolworth Building?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:43.13,0:07:44.21,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}没错。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}That's right.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:45.05,0:07:46.72,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}是不是很好笑？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Isn't that funny?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:46.88,0:07:49.09,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你知道吗，我在这儿住了一辈子，从没进去过。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You know, I've lived here all my life. I've never been inside that.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:49.26,0:07:51.22,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}要是你得整理那些破烂。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}If you had to sort out all that junk.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:51.39,0:07:53.47,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}就像电影那件事。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Like that thing with the movies.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:53.64,0:07:55.89,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}是啊，说得太对了。那把刀的事怎么说？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Yeah, you can say that again. What about that business with the knife?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:56.64,0:07:59.44,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我是说，让成年人相信那种鬼话，啊？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I mean, asking grown-up people to believe that kind of jazz, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:59.60,0:08:02.02,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}嗯，我早料到了。你知道我们面对的是什么人。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Well, I expected that. You know what we're dealing with.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:02.19,0:08:03.86,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-是啊，大概吧。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Yeah, I guess so.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:04.65,0:08:06.28,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}看来你的喇叭没问题，再试试车灯吧。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Well, your horn works. Now try your lights.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:07.99,0:08:09.61,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-你怎么了，感冒了？  -可不是嘛。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-What do you got, a cold?   -And how.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:09.78,0:08:11.49,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}这种热天感冒能要人命。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}These hot-weather colds can kill you.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:11.66,0:08:14.04,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我连鼻子都几乎碰不得。你懂我意思吧？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I can hardly touch my nose. You know what I mean?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:14.54,0:08:16.96,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}当然懂。我刚得过一次。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I sure do. I just got over one.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:18.08,0:08:20.75,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}哦，得了。陪审长先生，我们开始吧？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Oh, come on. Mr. Foreman, let's go here, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:20.92,0:08:22.08,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}嗯，那家伙还在洗手间。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Well, that guy's still in the bathroom.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:22.58,0:08:25.38,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}嘿，有什么新闻？我早上没机会看报。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Hey, what's new? I didn't get a chance to see a paper this morning.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:25.55,0:08:28.76,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}嗯？我只是想知道股市收盘怎么样。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Hmm? I was only wondering how the market closed.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:28.92,0:08:30.88,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你在交易所有席位？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You got a seat on the Exchange?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:31.93,0:08:33.01,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我是股票经纪人。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I'm a broker.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:33.76,0:08:37.56,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我经营一家跑腿服务公司，叫“随叫随到公司”。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I run a messenger service, the Beck and Call Company.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:38.27,0:08:39.98,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}这名字是我老婆起的。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}The name was my wife's idea.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:40.48,0:08:43.52,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}手下有37个人。白手起家。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Got 37 men working. Started with nothing.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:44.23,0:08:46.82,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}好了，各位，请就座吧。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Okay, men, let's take our seats, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:50.57,0:08:52.36,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}对，咱们都能快点离开这儿，对吧？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Yeah, we can all get outta here pretty quick, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:52.53,0:08:53.95,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}不知道你们怎么样，反正我\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I don't know about the rest of you, but I happen
Dialogue: 0,0:08:54.12,0:08:55.62,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}刚好有今晚球赛的票。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}to have tickets to that ball game tonight.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:55.78,0:08:56.91,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}洋基对克利夫兰。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Yanks and Cleveland.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:57.54,0:08:59.46,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}对，我们有个小子莫杰莱夫斯基上场。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Yeah, we got this kid, Modjelewski, in there.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:59.62,0:09:01.17,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}哦，这小子壮得像头牛。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Ooh, he's a real bull, this kid.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:01.33,0:09:03.21,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你知道吗……砰！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You know... Phoom!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:03.38,0:09:05.46,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}接球真稳。懂吧？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}A real jug handler. You know?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:05.63,0:09:07.30,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}砰！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Phoom!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:08.17,0:09:10.67,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你真是铁杆棒球迷，对吧？嗯。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You're a real baseball fan, aren't you? Huh? Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:10.84,0:09:11.88,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}咱们坐哪儿？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Where do we sit here?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:12.05,0:09:15.01,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我想……咱们按陪审员编号顺序坐吧。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Well, I... thought we'd sit in order, you know, by jury numbers.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:15.18,0:09:18.06,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}一号、二号、三号……依次围着桌子坐。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}One, two, three, four, five... so on, around the table.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:18.22,0:09:20.23,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-各位没意见吧。  -有什么差别？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-If that's okay with you, gentlemen.   -What's the difference?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:20.39,0:09:23.15,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-按顺序坐挺合理。  -就这么办。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-I think it's reasonable to sit in order.   -Let it be.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:23.31,0:09:25.52,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-12号坐这儿吗？  -对，那是12号。我们按圈来。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Number 12. Do I sit down here?   -Yeah. That's 12. We go around.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:25.69,0:09:29.11,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-从你开始。1号，对吧？  -1号，对。2、3、4、5、6。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-We start with you. One, right?   -One, yeah. Two, three, four, five, six.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:29.28,0:09:31.32,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你对检察官印象如何？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}What was your impression of the prosecuting attorney?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:31.49,0:09:34.12,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-好。2号。你是2号。  -什么？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Okay. Two. You're two.   -I beg pardon?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:34.62,0:09:35.99,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我觉得他非常精明，\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I thought he was really sharp,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:36.16,0:09:38.33,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}把那些要点一条条处理得很清楚。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}the way he handled all those points one by one.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:38.91,0:09:41.29,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}逻辑严密。我印象很深。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Logical sequence. I was very impressed.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:42.08,0:09:44.63,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我觉得他……干得很专业。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I think he... he did an expert job.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:45.13,0:09:48.17,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}还很有干劲，懂吧？真有冲劲。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}A lot of drive too, you Know? Real drive.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:48.34,0:09:49.67,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}好了，伙计们，能安静一下吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Okay, fellas, can we hold it down a minute?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:49.84,0:09:51.26,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-当然。  -各位。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Sure.   -Fellas.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:51.97,0:09:53.34,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}喂，我们想开始了。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Say, we'd like to get started.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:54.30,0:09:55.39,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}窗边那位先生。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Gentleman at the window.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:56.76,0:09:59.18,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-我们想开始了。  -哦，抱歉。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-We'd like to get started.   -Oh, I'm sorry.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:59.35,0:10:01.98,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}真难理解，对吧？小子杀了亲爹，\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Pretty tough to figure, isn't it? Kid kills his father,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:02.14,0:10:04.48,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-砰，就这么一下。  -哎，你分析下数据，\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-bing, just like that.   -Aw, listen, you analyze the figures,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:04.65,0:10:05.52,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}就知道这种事天天都有。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}you'll see it happens all the time.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:05.69,0:10:07.73,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他们让那些孩子在那地方撒野。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}They let those kids run wild up there.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:07.90,0:10:10.74,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}也许他们活该。懂我意思吧？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Well, maybe it serves 'em right. You know what I mean?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:10.90,0:10:12.15,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}人……人都到齐了吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Is... is everyone here?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:12.32,0:10:14.07,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}老人在里面。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}The old man is inside.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:14.24,0:10:16.32,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}哦。你……能帮他敲下门吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Oh. Would you... knock on the door for him?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:16.49,0:10:18.78,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-好。  -你是洋基球迷吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Yeah.   -You a Yankee fan?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:18.95,0:10:20.08,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}不是。巴尔的摩。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}No. Baltimore.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:21.45,0:10:22.50,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-巴尔的摩？  -对。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Baltimore?   -Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:24.37,0:10:26.88,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那就像每天脑袋被撬棍敲一下。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}That's like being hit in the head with a crowbar once a day.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:27.38,0:10:29.29,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他们有什么好球员？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Who have they got?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:29.80,0:10:31.84,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}不，我是说，除了好场地工，他们还有谁？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}No, I mean, who have they got besides good groundskeepers?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:32.42,0:10:33.97,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}喂，我们想开始了。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Say, we'd like to get started.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:34.13,0:10:36.97,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}哦，抱歉，各位。我……不是故意让你们等的。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Oh, forgive me, gentlemen. I... I didn't mean to keep you waiting.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:37.85,0:10:38.89,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}巴尔的摩？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Baltimore?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:39.72,0:10:42.43,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}好了，各位，请听我说。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Okay, gentlemen, if I can have your attention.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:43.02,0:10:45.60,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}各位想怎么处理都行。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You fellas can handle this thing any way that you want to.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:45.77,0:10:48.19,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我……我不打算定什么规矩。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I'm... You know, I'm not gonna make any rules.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:48.36,0:10:51.78,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}咱们可以先讨论……再表决。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}We can, well, discuss it first and... then vote on it.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:51.94,0:10:54.28,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}这当然……也是一种办法。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}That's, of course... that's... one way.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:54.45,0:10:57.32,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}或者，咱们现在就表决，然后……\N{\rEN\blur0.8}And, well, we can vote on it right now, and...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:57.49,0:10:59.62,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我觉得按惯例应该先初步表决。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I think it's customary to take a preliminary vote.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:00.24,0:11:04.00,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}对，咱们……表决吧。谁知道呢？也许咱们都能快点走。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Yeah, let's... let's vote. Who knows? Maybe we can all get outta here, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:04.16,0:11:05.04,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}嗯。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Uh-huh.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:05.62,0:11:08.54,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}好，那么……我觉得……\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Okay, then... I think that...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:08.71,0:11:09.96,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}当然，你们知道我们……\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Of course, you know that we...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:10.13,0:11:13.67,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}这儿是一级谋杀指控，如果我们裁定被告有罪，\N{\rEN\blur0.8}have a first-degree murder charge here and if we vote the accused guilty,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:13.84,0:11:16.93,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}就得送他上电椅。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}we've got to send him to the chair.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:17.09,0:11:20.60,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-嗯……这是强制规定。  -我想我们都知道。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Um... That's mandatory.   -I think we know that.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:20.76,0:11:22.60,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-看看谁是什么立场吧。  -也好。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Let's see who's where.   -We might as well.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:22.76,0:11:25.85,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-好。有人不想表决吗？  -我没意见。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Okay. Anyone doesn't want to vote?   -All right with me.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:27.81,0:11:29.15,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}好。那么，\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Okay. Then,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:29.31,0:11:32.52,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}记住，无论哪边，都必须12票一致。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}just remember that this has to be 12 to nothing either way.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:32.69,0:11:35.32,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}这是法律规定。好，准备好了吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}That's the law. Okay, are we ready?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:36.24,0:11:38.99,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}现在，认为有罪的请举手。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Now, all those voting guilty, please raise your hands.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:43.16,0:11:46.58,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}一、二、三、四、五、六、七……\N{\rEN\blur0.8}One, two, three, four, five, six, seven...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:48.08,0:11:50.25,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}八、九、十、十一。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}eight, nine, ten, eleven.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:50.96,0:11:53.05,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}好。11票有罪。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Okay. That's 11 guilty.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:53.76,0:11:55.01,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}认为无罪的。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Those voting not guilty.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:56.30,0:11:57.88,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}一票。对。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}One. Right.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:58.55,0:12:00.76,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}11票有罪，1票无罪。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}That's 11 guilty. One not guilty.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:01.68,0:12:03.56,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}好了，现在知道情况了。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Well, now we know where we are.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:03.72,0:12:06.39,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}天哪。总有一个这样的。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Boy, oh, boy. There's always one.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:08.10,0:12:09.60,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那现在怎么办？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}So, what do we do now?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:10.60,0:12:13.61,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-我想咱们得谈谈。  -天哪。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-I guess we talk.   -Boy, oh, boy.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:13.78,0:12:15.19,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你真觉得他无罪？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You really think he's innocent?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:19.45,0:12:20.57,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我不知道。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I don't know.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:20.74,0:12:22.91,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我是说，你和我们一样坐在法庭里。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I mean, you sat in court with the rest of us.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:23.08,0:12:24.83,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你也听到那些证词了。那小子是个危险的杀人犯。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You heard what we did. The kid's a dangerous killer.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:24.99,0:12:27.50,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-这明摆着。  -他才18岁。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-You could see it.   -He's 18 years old.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:27.66,0:12:29.00,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那也够大了。他……\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Well, that's old enough. He...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:29.50,0:12:32.29,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他把亲爹捅进胸口四英寸深。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}He stabbed his own father four inches into the chest.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:32.46,0:12:35.05,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}法庭上用十几种方式证明了。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}They proved it a dozen different ways in court.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:35.21,0:12:36.80,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}要我给你一一列出来吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Would you like me to list them for you?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:37.59,0:12:38.42,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}不用。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}No.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:39.13,0:12:40.34,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那你想怎样？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Then what do you want?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:41.09,0:12:43.72,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-我只想谈谈。  -有什么好谈的？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-I just want to talk.   -What's there to talk about?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:43.89,0:12:45.52,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}这里十一个人都认为他有罪。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Eleven men in here think he's guilty.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:45.68,0:12:47.64,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}除了你，谁都不用多想。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}No one had to think about it twice except you.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:47.81,0:12:50.40,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我想问你，你信他的说法吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I want to ask you something. Do you believe his story?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:51.02,0:12:53.44,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我不知道信不信。也许不信。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I don't know whether I believe it or not. Maybe I don't.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:53.61,0:12:54.82,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那你为什么投无罪？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}So how come you vote not guilty?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:55.52,0:12:57.40,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}刚才有11票赞成有罪。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Well, there were 11 votes for guilty.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:57.57,0:13:00.32,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}要举手把一个孩子送去死，没那么容易\N{\rEN\blur0.8}It's not easy to raise my hand and send a boy off to die
Dialogue: 0,0:13:00.49,0:13:02.32,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}事先都不讨论一下。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}without talking about it first.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:02.49,0:13:04.78,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-谁说这容易了？  -没人说。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Well, now, who says it's easy?   -No one.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:06.24,0:13:07.87,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}怎么，就因为投票投得快？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}What, just because I voted fast?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:08.58,0:13:10.29,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我真心觉得这小子有罪。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I honestly think the guy's guilty.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:11.08,0:13:13.63,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}就算你说上一百年也改变不了我的想法。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You couldn't change my mind if you talked for 100 years.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:13.79,0:13:15.71,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我不是想改变你的想法。只是……\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I'm not trying to change your mind. It's just that...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:16.67,0:13:18.59,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我们这儿谈的是一条人命。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}We're talking about somebody's life here.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:18.76,0:13:20.97,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我们不能五分钟就定下来。万一我们错了呢。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}We can't decide it in five minutes. Supposing we're wrong.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:21.13,0:13:22.43,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}“万一我们错了。”\N{\rEN\blur0.8}"Supposing we're wrong."
Dialogue: 0,0:13:22.59,0:13:24.39,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那万一这整栋楼塌下来砸我头上呢。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Supposing this whole building should fall down on my head.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:24.55,0:13:26.35,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-什么都能假设。  -没错。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-You can suppose anything.   -That's right.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:27.39,0:13:29.43,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}听着，花多长时间有什么区别？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Look, what's the difference how long it takes?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:29.60,0:13:32.14,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}就算我们五分钟就决定，那又怎样？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Suppose we do it in five minutes. So what?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:32.31,0:13:35.86,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}咱们就花一个小时。球赛八点才开始。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Let's take an hour. The ball game doesn't start till eight o'clock.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:38.07,0:13:39.24,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}嗯？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Hmm?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:40.78,0:13:43.24,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}谁有话说？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Who's got something to say?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:43.74,0:13:45.45,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我愿意坐一个小时。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I'm willing to sit for an hour.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:45.62,0:13:48.04,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}太好了。我昨晚听到个挺不错的故事——\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Great. I heard a pretty good story last night--
Dialogue: 0,0:13:48.20,0:13:49.91,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我们坐在这儿不是为了这个。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}That's not why we're sitting here.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:51.12,0:13:54.54,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那好，你告诉我。我们坐在这儿是为了什么？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}All right, then you tell me. What are we sitting here for?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:56.00,0:13:57.54,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我不知道。也许没什么理由。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I don't know. Maybe no reason.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:58.76,0:14:02.26,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}听着，这孩子一辈子都被人踢来踢去，\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Look, this kid's been kicked around all of his life
Dialogue: 0,0:14:02.42,0:14:06.18,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}生在贫民窟，九岁就没了妈。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}you know, born in a slum, mother dead since he was nine.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:06.35,0:14:08.43,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他在孤儿院住了一年半，那时他……\N{\rEN\blur0.8}He lived for a year and a half in an orphanage when his...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:08.60,0:14:10.98,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他父亲因伪造罪在坐牢。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}his father was serving a jail term for forgery.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:11.89,0:14:13.69,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}这可不是什么幸福的开始。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}It's not a very happy beginning.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:14.19,0:14:16.15,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他是个……野性、愤怒的孩子。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}He's a... a wild, angry kid.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:16.31,0:14:17.65,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他一直都是这样。你知道为什么吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}That's all he's ever been. And you know why?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:17.82,0:14:21.19,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}因为他每天都要被人往头上打一下。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}'Cause he's been hit on the head by somebody once a day, every day.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:22.03,0:14:24.11,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他过了……过了很悲惨的十八年。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}He's had a... he's had a pretty miserable 18 years.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:24.28,0:14:27.16,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我……我只是觉得我们该跟他说几句话。就这样。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I... I just think we owe him a few words. That's all.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:27.32,0:14:30.62,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我不妨告诉你，先生。我们什么都不欠他。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I don't mind telling you this, mister. We don't owe him a thing.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:30.79,0:14:33.75,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他得到了公正的审判，不是吗？你觉得那场审判花了多少钱？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}He got a fair trial, didn't he? What do you think that trial cost?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:33.92,0:14:36.12,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他能得到审判就算走运了。你懂我意思吧？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}He's lucky he got it. You know what I mean?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:36.29,0:14:39.30,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-你知道的。  -听着，我们这儿都是成年人。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-You know it.   -Now, look, we're all grown-ups in here.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:39.46,0:14:41.34,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我们听了证词，不是吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}We heard the facts, didn't we?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:41.51,0:14:43.88,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你不会是想告诉我，我们该相信这小子吧，\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You're not gonna tell me that we're supposed to believe this kid,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:44.05,0:14:45.30,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}明知他是什么货色。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}knowing what he is.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:45.47,0:14:47.76,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}听着，我一辈子都跟他们住在一起。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Listen, I've lived among them all my life.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:47.93,0:14:51.02,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他们说的话一个字都不能信。你知道的。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You can't believe a word they say. You know that.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:51.18,0:14:53.06,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我是说，他们天生就是骗子。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I mean, they're born liars.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:53.23,0:14:55.77,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}只有无知的人才会相信这种话。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Only an ignorant man can believe that.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:55.94,0:14:57.60,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-你给我听着——-你以为你是生来\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Now listen-- -Do you think you were born
Dialogue: 0,0:14:57.77,0:14:59.02,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}就垄断了真理吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}with a monopoly on the truth?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:59.52,0:15:02.11,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我觉得有些事该向这位先生指出来。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I think certain things should be pointed out to this man.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:02.28,0:15:04.28,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}得了吧，今天又不是礼拜天。我们用不着听布道。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Come on, this isn't Sunday. We don't need a sermon.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:04.44,0:15:06.45,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}好了，我们现在有正事要做。开始吧。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Come on, we have a job to do now. Let's do it.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:07.62,0:15:10.62,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}米花脆。是我在广告公司做的产品。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Rice Pops. It's a product I work on at the agency.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:11.54,0:15:13.41,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}“自带活力的早餐。”\N{\rEN\blur0.8}"The breakfast with a built-in bounce."
Dialogue: 0,0:15:14.16,0:15:16.00,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-这句是我写的。  -挺上口的。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-I wrote that line.   -Very catchy.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:16.16,0:15:17.79,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-是啊。  -喂，你能不能别这样？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Yeah.   -Say, do you mind?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:17.96,0:15:19.54,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}哦，抱歉。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Oh, I'm sorry.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:19.71,0:15:22.55,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我有个乱涂乱画的习惯。能让我思路清晰。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I have this habit of doodling. Keeps me thinking clearly.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:22.71,0:15:24.30,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}是啊，我们还有这么多事要做。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Yeah, we have all this work to do.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:24.46,0:15:26.13,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-在这儿耗一辈子没意义。  -抱歉。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-There's no point staying here forever.   -Sorry.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:26.30,0:15:27.09,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}好。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Okay.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:28.05,0:15:32.31,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}也许那位坐在下面、不同意我们的先生，\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Now perhaps if the gentleman down there who's disagreeing with us,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:32.47,0:15:33.60,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}也许你能告诉我们为什么。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}well, perhaps you could tell us why.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:33.77,0:15:35.39,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}让我们知道你在想什么。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You know, let us know what you're thinking.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:35.56,0:15:38.06,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我们也许能指出你哪里搞错了。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}And we might be able to show you where you're mixed up.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:38.23,0:15:39.90,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}听着，也许……也许这是个好主意。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Well, look, maybe... maybe this is an idea.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:40.06,0:15:42.36,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我没怎么多想，不过在我看来\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Now, I haven't given it much thought, but it seems to me
Dialogue: 0,0:15:42.52,0:15:45.19,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}该由我们大家来说服这位先生\N{\rEN\blur0.8}that it's up to the group of us to convince this gentleman
Dialogue: 0,0:15:45.36,0:15:46.86,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}让他知道是他错了、我们是对的。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}that he's wrong and we're right.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:47.03,0:15:49.24,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}也许我们每个人花几分钟，就……\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Now, maybe if we each took a couple of minutes just to...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:50.91,0:15:53.91,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-这只是我随口一说。  -不不不。这主意不错。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Well, it was just a quick idea.   -No, no, no. That's a good one.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:54.83,0:15:56.58,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}咱们就绕着桌子轮流说一遍。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Suppose we go once around the table.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:57.29,0:15:59.08,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-我想从你先开始。  -哦。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-I guess you're first.   -Oh.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:00.08,0:16:01.42,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}这个……\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Well...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:02.96,0:16:05.38,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}这……这很难用言语表达。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Well, it... it's hard to put into words.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:06.42,0:16:08.26,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我就是觉得他有罪。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I just think he's guilty.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:08.43,0:16:10.55,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我觉得从一开始就明摆着。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I thought it was obvious from the word "go."
Dialogue: 0,0:16:11.47,0:16:14.26,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-我是说，没人证明不是他干的。  -没人需要证明别的。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-I mean, nobody proved otherwise.   -Nobody has to prove otherwise.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:14.43,0:16:16.18,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}举证责任在控方。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}The burden of proof's on the prosecution.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:16.89,0:16:18.90,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}被告甚至不用开口。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}The defendant doesn't even have to open his mouth.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:19.06,0:16:22.32,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-这是宪法规定的。  -哦，当然，我知道。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-That's in the Constitution.   -Oh, well, sure, I Know that.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:22.94,0:16:24.36,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我的意思是……\N{\rEN\blur0.8}What I meant was, is...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:26.15,0:16:28.15,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我就是觉得他有罪。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Well, I just think he's guilty.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:28.32,0:16:29.95,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我……我是说，有人看见他干的。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I... I mean, somebody saw him do it.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:30.11,0:16:32.95,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}好……我是这么想的，\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Okay... Here's what I think,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:33.12,0:16:35.08,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我对此没有个人感情。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}and I have no personal feelings about this.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:35.24,0:16:37.16,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我只想谈事实。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I just want to talk about facts.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:38.33,0:16:40.00,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-第一。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Number one.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:40.96,0:16:44.88,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}老人住在凶案发生房间的楼下。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}The old man lived downstairs under the room where the killing took place.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:45.05,0:16:47.30,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}凶案当晚十二点十分，\N{\rEN\blur0.8}At ten minutes after 12:00 on the night of the killing,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:47.46,0:16:50.43,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他听到很大的响声，说听起来像在打架。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}he heard loud noises, said it sounded like a fight.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:51.09,0:16:53.60,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他听到那孩子大喊：“我要杀了你。”\N{\rEN\blur0.8}And he heard the kid yell out, "I'm gonna kill ya."
Dialogue: 0,0:16:54.10,0:16:56.31,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}一秒钟后，他听到有身体倒在地板上。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}A second later, he heard a body hit the floor.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:56.47,0:16:58.10,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他跑到门口，打开门，\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Ran to the door, opened it up,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:58.27,0:17:00.44,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}看见那孩子跑下楼梯，冲出房子。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}saw the kid running down the stairs and out of the house.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:01.06,0:17:03.23,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他报了警。警察来了，发现老人\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Called the police. They came in, found the old man
Dialogue: 0,0:17:03.40,0:17:04.82,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}胸口插着一把刀。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}with a knife in his chest.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:04.98,0:17:07.98,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}验尸官判定死亡时间在午夜左右。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}The coroner fixed the time of death around midnight.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:08.15,0:17:11.40,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}这些都是事实。事实是无法反驳的。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Now these are facts. You can't refute facts.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:11.57,0:17:12.66,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}这孩子有罪。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}The kid is guilty.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:13.66,0:17:15.58,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我跟别人一样也讲感情。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I'm just as sentimental as the next fella.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:15.74,0:17:19.62,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我知道他才十八岁，但他还是得为自己的所作所为付出代价。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I know he's only 18, but he's still gotta pay for what he did.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:19.79,0:17:21.04,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我同意你。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I'm with you.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:21.21,0:17:23.29,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}好……你说完了吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Okay... are you finished?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:23.83,0:17:25.17,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-完了。  -好。下一位。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Yeah.   -Right. Next.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:25.34,0:17:28.63,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}在我看来，那小子的说辞根本站不住脚。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}It is obvious, to me anyway, that the boy's entire story was flimsy.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:28.80,0:17:30.88,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他说案发时自己在看电影\N{\rEN\blur0.8}He claimed he was at the movies during the time of the killing
Dialogue: 0,0:17:31.05,0:17:33.84,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}可一小时后，他连看的是什么片子都说不出来\N{\rEN\blur0.8}and yet, one hour later, he couldn't remember the names of the films he saw
Dialogue: 0,0:17:34.01,0:17:35.43,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-也记不清是谁演的。  -对。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-or who played in them.   -That's right.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:35.60,0:17:37.81,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}而且没人看见他进电影院或出来。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}And no one saw him going in or out of the theater.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:37.97,0:17:39.68,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}等等，街对面那个女人呢？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Listen, what about the woman across the street?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:39.85,0:17:41.89,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}要是她的证词都不算数，那就没什么算数了。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}If her testimony don't prove it, nothing does.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:42.06,0:17:44.31,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}没错，她可是亲眼看见凶案的。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}That's right. She was the one who actually saw the killing.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:44.48,0:17:46.82,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}各位，拜托，咱们按顺序来，好吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Now, fellas, please. Let's go in order here, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:46.98,0:17:50.15,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}等一下。这个女人……\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Just a minute. Here's a woman...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:50.32,0:17:52.74,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}这个女人躺在床上，睡不着。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Here's a woman who was lying in bed. She can't sleep.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:52.90,0:17:54.78,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}热得要命，你们懂的。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}She's dying with the heat. You know what I mean?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:54.95,0:17:56.66,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}反正她往窗外一看\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Anyway, she looks out the window
Dialogue: 0,0:17:56.83,0:18:00.37,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}就在街对面，看见那小子把刀捅进了他父亲的身体。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}and right across the street she sees the kid stick the knife into his father.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:00.54,0:18:03.37,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}时间正好是12点10分。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}The time is 12:10 on the nose.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:03.54,0:18:04.96,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}一切都对得上。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Everything fits.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:05.13,0:18:07.13,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}她从小就认识这孩子。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Look, she's known the kid all his life.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:07.30,0:18:09.30,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他的窗户就在她对面，隔着高架铁道\N{\rEN\blur0.8}His window is right opposite hers across the EL tracks
Dialogue: 0,0:18:09.46,0:18:11.21,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}她发誓看见是他干的。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}and she swore she saw him do it.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:11.38,0:18:13.13,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}隔着驶过高架列车的车窗。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Through the windows of a passing EL train.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:13.30,0:18:14.14,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}对。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Right.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:14.30,0:18:17.56,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那趟高架列车没有乘客，只是调车去市中心。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}This EL train had no passengers on it. It was just being moved downtown.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:18.26,0:18:20.93,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}车厢灯是灭的，记得吗？法庭上已经证明\N{\rEN\blur0.8}The lights were out, remember? And they proved in court
Dialogue: 0,0:18:21.10,0:18:22.98,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}夜里你可以透过高架列车的车窗\N{\rEN\blur0.8}that at night you can look through the windows of an EL train
Dialogue: 0,0:18:23.14,0:18:25.60,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}在灯灭的时候看清对面的情况。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}when the lights are out and see what's happening on the other side.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:25.77,0:18:28.27,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-他们证明了。  -我想问你一个问题。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-They proved it.   -I'd like to ask you something.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:29.03,0:18:31.65,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你不信那小子的话，怎么就信那女人的？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You don't believe the boy's story. How come you believe the woman's?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:31.82,0:18:33.86,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}她也是那边的人，不是吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}She's one of them, too, isn't she?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:36.32,0:18:38.16,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你还真挺聪明的，是吧？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You're a pretty smart fella, aren't you?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:38.33,0:18:39.70,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-好了，先生们。  -好了，好了。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Okay, gentlemen.   -Now, now.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:39.87,0:18:42.08,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-先生们。  -行了，坐下，坐下。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Now, gentlemen.   -Come on. Sit down. Sit down.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:42.25,0:18:44.71,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他有什么好神气的？我跟你们说。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Oh, what's he so wise about? I'm telling you.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:44.87,0:18:47.63,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}好了，别吵了，吵架解决不了问题。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Okay, now come on. Now we're not gonna get anywhere fighting.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:48.13,0:18:49.38,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}下一个轮到谁？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Whose turn is it next?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:49.54,0:18:52.13,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}哦……他。五号。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Oh... his. Number five.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:54.51,0:18:57.09,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}好吧，我能不能……我能不能先跳过？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Okay, may I... Can I pass it?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:57.93,0:18:59.97,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}嗯……这是你的权利。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Well... that's your privilege.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:01.14,0:19:02.52,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那下一位先生呢？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}How about the next gentleman?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:03.35,0:19:06.10,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}哦，这个……我不知道。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Oh. Well... I don't know.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:06.27,0:19:10.23,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}其实案子一开始，我就快被说服了。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I started to be convinced, you know, very early in the case.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:11.03,0:19:15.20,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你看，我一直在找动机。这很重要。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You see, I was looking for a motive. That's very important.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:15.36,0:19:18.74,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}因为要是没有动机，你的案子还站得住吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Because if you don't have a motive, where's your case, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:19.58,0:19:22.58,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}总之，那些人提供的证词\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Anyway, that testimony from those people
Dialogue: 0,0:19:22.74,0:19:25.29,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}就住在孩子家对门那户\N{\rEN\blur0.8}in the apartment across the hall from the kid's apartment,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:25.83,0:19:27.46,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}非常有力。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}that was very powerful.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:28.04,0:19:31.13,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他们不是说过，有一场……一场争吵和打斗\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Didn't they say something about a... a fight and an argument
Dialogue: 0,0:19:31.30,0:19:35.47,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}是老头和他儿子之间，大概那晚七点左右？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}between the old man and his son around about... seven o'clock that night?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:35.63,0:19:37.80,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-我也许记错了，可是——-是八点。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-I mean, I could be wrong, but I-- -It was eight o'clock.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:37.97,0:19:40.05,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}是八点，没错。他们听见了争吵。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}It was eight o'clock. That's right. They heard an argument.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:40.22,0:19:41.76,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}但听不清在吵什么。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}They couldn't hear what it was about.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:41.93,0:19:44.02,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}接着听见父亲打了男孩两下。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Then they heard the father hit the boy twice.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:44.18,0:19:45.98,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-最后他们看见那男孩\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Finally they saw the boy
Dialogue: 0,0:19:46.14,0:19:48.48,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}气冲冲地跑出家门。这能证明什么？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}run angrily out of the house. What does that prove?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:48.65,0:19:51.56,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}嗯，这确实证明不了什么。只是……\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Well, it don't exactly prove anything. It's just...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:51.73,0:19:53.82,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-只是事情的一部分。  -可你说过这提供了动机。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-part of the picture.   -Well, you said it provided a motive.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:53.98,0:19:55.44,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}检察官也是这么说的。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}And the prosecuting attorney said the same thing.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:55.61,0:19:57.53,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我觉得那算不上什么有力的动机。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I don't think that was a very strong motive.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:57.70,0:20:01.37,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}这孩子这辈子挨打挨得太多，暴力对他来说几乎……\N{\rEN\blur0.8}This boy's been hit so many times in his life that violence is practically...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:01.53,0:20:03.54,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}对他来说就是家常便饭。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}it's a normal state of affairs with him.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:04.16,0:20:06.46,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我就是……想不通两个耳光\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I just... I can't see two slaps in the face
Dialogue: 0,0:20:06.62,0:20:08.42,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}就能逼他去杀人。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}provoking him into committing murder.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:08.58,0:20:11.63,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}也许那是压垮他的最后两下。每个人都有崩溃的极限。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}It may have been two too many. Everyone has a breaking point.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:14.17,0:20:15.30,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}还有别的吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Anything else?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:16.34,0:20:18.47,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-没有了。  -好。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-No.   -Okay.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:19.09,0:20:20.59,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你呢？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}How about you?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:21.64,0:20:24.43,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我不知道。该说的都说了。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I don't know. It's all been said.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:26.31,0:20:28.56,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}在这儿说上一天，也还是这么回事。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You can talk here forever, it's still the same thing.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:30.10,0:20:31.81,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}这小子五比零，全输。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}This kid is five for 0.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:33.02,0:20:34.32,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}看看他的记录吧。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Well, look at his record.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:35.07,0:20:36.86,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}十岁就上了少年法庭。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}When he was ten, he was in children's court.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:37.40,0:20:38.74,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}朝老师扔石头。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}He threw a rock at a teacher.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:39.28,0:20:41.41,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}十五岁进了感化院。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}When he was 15, he was in reform school.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:41.57,0:20:42.87,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}偷车。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}He stole a car.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:43.58,0:20:45.08,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}因为抢劫被抓过。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}He's been arrested for mugging.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:46.12,0:20:47.91,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}因为持刀斗殴被逮过两次。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}He was picked up twice for knife fighting.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:48.08,0:20:50.29,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}是啊，人家说他玩刀玩得溜。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Oh, yeah, they say he's real handy with a knife.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:50.46,0:20:53.13,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}哟，多好的孩子啊。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Oh, this is a very fine boy.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:53.29,0:20:56.55,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}从五岁起，他父亲就经常揍他。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Ever since he was five years old, his father beat him up regularly.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:56.71,0:20:58.80,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-他动拳头。  -换我我也打。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-He used his fists.   -Well, so would I.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:58.97,0:21:00.26,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}这种孩子？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}A kid like that?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:00.43,0:21:03.26,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}就是这些孩子，现在都这德行。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}It's these kids, the way they are nowadays.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:06.10,0:21:09.06,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我小时候，管我爸叫“您”。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}When I was a kid, I used to call my father "sir."
Dialogue: 0,0:21:10.10,0:21:11.27,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}没错，“您”。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}That's right. "Sir."
Dialogue: 0,0:21:11.44,0:21:13.40,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}现在还有孩子这么叫爹吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Do you ever hear a kid call his father that anymore?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:13.56,0:21:15.61,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}当爹的好像也不觉得这有什么重要了。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Fathers don't seem to think it's important anymore.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:16.69,0:21:18.57,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-你有孩子吗？  -三个。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-You got any kids?   -Three.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:20.11,0:21:21.20,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我有一个。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I got one.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:23.07,0:21:24.58,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}二十二了。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Twenty-two years old.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:30.87,0:21:33.58,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他九岁那年，打架时跑了。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}When he was nine years old, he ran away from a fight.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:35.46,0:21:38.46,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我看见了。丢人得我差点吐出来。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I saw it. I was so embarrassed I almost threw up.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:40.34,0:21:44.89,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我说：“就算把你劈成两半，我也要把你练成个男人。”\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I said, "I'm gonna make a man out of you if I have to break you in two trying."
Dialogue: 0,0:21:47.39,0:21:48.89,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}后来我真把他练成了个男人。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Well, I made a man out of him.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:50.39,0:21:52.19,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他十六岁时，我们打了一架。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}When he was 16, we had a fight.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:54.02,0:21:56.27,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}一拳打在我下巴上。他个子大。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Hit me in the jaw. He was a big kid.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:59.78,0:22:01.86,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}两年没见了。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Haven't seen him for two years.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:03.70,0:22:05.82,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}孩子啊。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Kids.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:07.74,0:22:09.37,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}掏心掏肺地养。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Work your heart out.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:12.25,0:22:13.46,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}好了，咱们继续吧。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Well, let's get going.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:14.17,0:22:15.96,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我觉得我们跑题了。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I think we're missing the point here.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:16.13,0:22:18.30,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}这孩子，就算他是破碎家庭的产物\N{\rEN\blur0.8}This boy, let's say he's the product of a broken home
Dialogue: 0,0:22:18.46,0:22:20.59,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}还有肮脏的贫民区。这我们无能为力。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}and a filthy neighborhood. We can't help that.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:20.76,0:22:23.13,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我们是来判定他有罪还是无罪的\N{\rEN\blur0.8}We're here to decide whether he's innocent or guilty
Dialogue: 0,0:22:23.30,0:22:26.18,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}不是来追究他为什么会那样长大的。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}not to go into the reasons why he grew up the way he did.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:26.34,0:22:29.14,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他生在贫民窟。贫民窟是罪犯的温床。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}He was born in a slum. Slums are breeding grounds for criminals.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:29.31,0:22:30.47,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我知道，你也知道。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I Know it, and so do you.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:30.98,0:22:33.18,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}这不是秘密：贫民窟出身的孩子\N{\rEN\blur0.8}It's no secret children from slum backgrounds
Dialogue: 0,0:22:33.35,0:22:36.31,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}都是社会的潜在威胁。现在我觉得——\N{\rEN\blur0.8}are potential menaces to society. Now I think--
Dialogue: 0,0:22:36.48,0:22:37.94,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}老兄，这话说得太对了。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Brother, you can say that again.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:38.11,0:22:40.69,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}从那种地方爬出来的孩子都是十足的垃圾。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}The kids who crawl out of these places are real trash.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:40.86,0:22:41.65,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我不想跟他们沾一点边。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I don't want any part of them.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:41.82,0:22:42.90,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-我跟你说。  -听着，先生。听着。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-I'm telling you.   -Listen, mister. Listen.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:43.07,0:22:46.07,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我……我一辈子都住在贫民窟。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I... I've lived in a slum all my life.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:46.24,0:22:47.87,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-等一下。  -求你了，我……\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Wait a minute.   -Please, I...
Dialogue: 0,0:22:48.03,0:22:50.16,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我在堆满垃圾的后院里玩过。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I played in backyards that were filled with garbage.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:50.33,0:22:52.58,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我是说，也许你们还能从我身上闻到那股味儿。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I mean, maybe you can still smell it on me.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:52.75,0:22:53.91,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}听我说，小伙子。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Now, listen, sonny.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:54.08,0:22:55.42,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}行了。这不是针对你个人。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Come on now. There's nothing personal about this.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:55.58,0:22:58.25,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-不，就是针对我。  -得了吧，伙计。他不是说你。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-No, there was something personal.   -Come on, fella. He didn't mean you.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:58.42,0:23:02.34,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-别这么敏感。  -这种敏感我能理解。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Let's not be so sensitive.   -This sensitivity I can understand.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:02.51,0:23:04.63,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}好了，听着，我们别吵了。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Okay, look, let's stop the arguing.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:04.80,0:23:06.72,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我们只是在浪费时间，而且……\N{\rEN\blur0.8}We're only wasting time, and...
Dialogue: 0,0:23:08.14,0:23:10.01,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}喂，轮到你了。开始吧。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Look, your turn down there. Let's go.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:11.43,0:23:14.52,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}哦，我没料到会轮到我。我以为你们都要来说服我呢。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Oh, I didn't expect a turn. I thought you were all gonna try to convince me.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:14.68,0:23:16.27,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-不是这么打算的吗？  -没错。就是这么想的。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Wasn't that the idea?   -Check. That was the idea.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:16.44,0:23:18.61,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-哦，我忘了这事。他说得对。  -那有什么区别？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Oh, I forgot about that. He's right.   -What difference does it make?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:18.77,0:23:20.90,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}就是他让我们留在这儿的。听听他有什么话说。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}He's the one who's keeping us in here. Let's hear what he's got to say.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:21.07,0:23:23.78,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}等等。我们说好要按某种方式来办的。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Well, now wait a minute. We decided to do this a certain way.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:23.94,0:23:27.41,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-我觉得我们应该照那样办。  -哦，别像个孩子似的，行吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-I think we ought to stick to that way.   -Oh, stop being a kid, will you?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:27.57,0:23:29.58,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-你说“孩子”是什么意思？  -你觉得我是什么意思？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-What do you mean "a kid"?   -What do you think I mean?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:29.74,0:23:31.33,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}小—孩—子。孩子。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}K-I-D. Kid.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:33.79,0:23:37.42,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}什么？就因为我想把这件事组织好？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}What? Listen, just because I'm trying to keep this thing organized?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:37.58,0:23:39.84,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}给，你来。你来担这个责任。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Here, you take it. You take on the responsibility.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:40.00,0:23:41.80,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那我就……我就闭嘴。就这样。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I'll just... I'll Keep my mouth shut. That's all.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:41.96,0:23:43.88,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你干嘛这么激动？冷静点，行吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}What are you getting so hot about? Calm down, will you?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:44.05,0:23:45.26,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}别叫我冷静。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Don't tell me to calm down.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:45.42,0:23:47.51,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}给。你想坐这个位子，就坐吧。就这样。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Here. You wanna take the chair, just take the chair. That's all.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:47.68,0:23:49.14,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-你们见过这种事吗？  -看看你能不能把会开下去。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Did you ever see such a thing?   -See if you can keep it running.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:49.84,0:23:50.85,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}听着，你觉得这很好笑\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Listen, you think it's funny
Dialogue: 0,0:23:51.01,0:23:52.18,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-还是怎么着？  -嘿，算了，伙计。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-or something?   -Hey, forget it, fella.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:52.35,0:23:53.85,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}整件事都无关紧要。行了。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}The whole thing's unimportant. Come on.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:54.02,0:23:56.98,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-不重要？哦，给，你来试试。  -不，没人想换。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Unimportant? Oh, here, you try it.   -No, nobody wants to change.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:57.14,0:23:58.81,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你干得很漂亮。坐下吧。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You're doing a beautiful job. Sit down.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:58.98,0:24:01.23,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}是啊，你干得真好。好极了，伙计。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Yeah, you're doing great. Just great, fella.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:01.77,0:24:03.52,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你就待在那儿继续干，懂吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You stay in there and pitch, you know?
Dialogue: 0,0:24:04.61,0:24:06.86,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}好了。听听别人怎么说。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}All right. Let's hear from somebody.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:08.32,0:24:10.66,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}如果你们要我说说我的想法，\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Well, if you want me to tell you how I feel about it,
Dialogue: 0,0:24:10.82,0:24:12.12,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那我没问题。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}it's all right with me.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:12.28,0:24:13.91,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}天哪，你们爱怎么做就怎么做，我不管。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Boy, I don't care what you do.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:14.70,0:24:17.16,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}好吧，我没什么高见。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}All right, I don't have anything brilliant.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:17.71,0:24:19.17,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我知道的不比你们多。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I only know as much as you do.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:19.88,0:24:22.88,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}根据证词，这孩子看起来有罪。也许他真有罪。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}According to the testimony, the boy looks guilty. Maybe he is.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:23.71,0:24:27.59,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我在法庭上坐了六天，听着证据一点点堆积起来。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I sat there in court for six days listening while the evidence built up.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:28.47,0:24:30.09,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}每个人听起来都那么肯定，懂吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Everybody sounded so positive, you know?
Dialogue: 0,0:24:30.26,0:24:32.80,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你知道，我……我开始对这场审判有种奇怪的感觉。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You know, I... I began to get a peculiar feeling about this trial.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:32.97,0:24:34.60,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我是说，没什么事能那么肯定。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I mean, nothing is that positive.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:35.52,0:24:37.14,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}有很多问题我本来想问。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}There are a lot of questions I'd have liked to ask.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:37.31,0:24:38.64,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我不知道，也许那些问题没什么意义，\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I don't know, maybe they wouldn't have meant anything,
Dialogue: 0,0:24:38.81,0:24:41.98,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}但是……我开始觉得辩护律师\N{\rEN\blur0.8}but... I began to get the feeling that the defense counsel
Dialogue: 0,0:24:42.15,0:24:44.57,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}没有进行足够彻底的交叉询问。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}wasn't conducting a thorough-enough cross-examination.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:44.73,0:24:47.90,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我是说，他……他放过了太多东西，那些小地方……\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I mean, he... he let too many things go by, little things that...
Dialogue: 0,0:24:48.07,0:24:50.99,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}什么小地方？听着，这些家伙不问问题\N{\rEN\blur0.8}What little things? Listen, when these fellas don't ask questions
Dialogue: 0,0:24:51.16,0:24:53.74,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}是因为他们已经知道答案，而且觉得问了会对自己不利。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}it's because they know the answers already and they figure they'll be hurt.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:53.91,0:24:57.62,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}也许律师也可能就是单纯的蠢，不是吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Maybe it's also possible for a lawyer to be just plain stupid, isn't it?
Dialogue: 0,0:24:57.79,0:24:59.00,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我是说，这有可能。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I mean, it's possible.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:59.16,0:25:00.75,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你听起来像见过我姐夫似的。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You sound like you met my brother-in-law once.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:03.71,0:25:06.46,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我……我一直把自己放在那孩子的处境上想。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I... I kept putting myself in the kid's place.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:08.17,0:25:10.18,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我想我会要求换个律师。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I'd have asked for another lawyer, I think.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:10.34,0:25:12.97,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我是说，如果我受审，命都可能没了\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I mean, if I was on trial for my life
Dialogue: 0,0:25:13.14,0:25:17.68,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我希望我的律师把控方证人驳得体无完肤，至少也得试试。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I'd want my lawyer to tear the prosecution witnesses to shreds or at least try to.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:17.85,0:25:21.56,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}听着，这起凶案只有一个所谓的目击证人。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Look, there was one alleged eyewitness to this killing.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:22.40,0:25:25.77,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}另一个人声称他听到了凶案发生，还看见那孩子之后跑出去。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Someone else claims he heard the killing, saw the boy run out afterwards.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:25.94,0:25:27.98,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}还有很多间接证据。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}And there was a lot of circumstantial evidence.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:28.15,0:25:31.61,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}但实际上，控方的整个案子就靠这两个证人。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}But actually, those two witnesses were the entire case for the prosecution.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:31.78,0:25:33.45,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}假设他们错了呢。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Supposing they're wrong.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:33.62,0:25:35.37,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你说的“假设他们错了”是什么意思？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}What do you mean supposing they're wrong?
Dialogue: 0,0:25:35.53,0:25:37.24,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那还要证人干什么？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}What's the point of having witnesses at all?
Dialogue: 0,0:25:37.41,0:25:38.45,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他们有可能错吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Could they be wrong?
Dialogue: 0,0:25:39.33,0:25:41.58,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你想说什么？那些人可是宣誓后坐上证人席的。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}What are you trying to say? Those people sat on the stand under oath.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:41.75,0:25:44.79,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他们也只是人。人都会犯错。他们有可能错吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}They're only people. People make mistakes. Could they be wrong?
Dialogue: 0,0:25:45.92,0:25:48.21,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-不，我觉得不会。  -你能确定吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Well, no, I don't think so.   -Do you know so?
Dialogue: 0,0:25:48.84,0:25:50.84,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}哦，得了吧。这种事没人能确定。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Oh, come on. Nobody can know a thing like that.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:51.01,0:25:53.68,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-这不是精确科学。  -没错。不是。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-This isn't an exact science.   -That's right. It isn't.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:59.10,0:26:01.64,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}好了，让……我们说正题吧。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Okay, let... let's get to the point.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:01.81,0:26:04.60,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他们从老人胸口找到的那把弹簧刀怎么说？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}What about the switch knife they found in the old man's chest?
Dialogue: 0,0:26:04.77,0:26:07.02,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}等等……等一下。还有人没发言呢。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Wait... wait a minute. There's some people who haven't talked yet.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:07.19,0:26:09.15,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-我们不该按顺序来吗？  -他们会有机会说的。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Shouldn't we go in order?   -They'll get a chance to talk.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:09.32,0:26:10.90,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}安静一下，行吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Be quiet a second, will you?
Dialogue: 0,0:26:11.49,0:26:14.74,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那把刀呢，这个……这个正派的好孩子\N{\rEN\blur0.8}What about it, this... the knife this fine upright boy
Dialogue: 0,0:26:14.91,0:26:17.78,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}承认在凶案当晚买的刀？我们来说说它。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}admitted buying the night of the killing? Let's talk about it.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:17.95,0:26:20.24,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}好，那就说说。把它拿进来看看。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}All right, let's talk about it. Let's get it in here and look at it.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:20.41,0:26:22.16,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我想再看一次。主席先生？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I'd like to see it again. Mr. Foreman?
Dialogue: 0,0:26:22.33,0:26:25.25,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我们都见过它长什么样。为什么还要再看？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}We all saw what it looks like. Why do we have to see it again?
Dialogue: 0,0:26:25.42,0:26:27.29,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}这位先生有权查看物证。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}The gentleman has a right to see exhibits in evidence.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:29.67,0:26:30.92,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}喂，能把刀拿给我们吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Say, could you bring us the knife?
Dialogue: 0,0:26:31.09,0:26:32.67,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-刀？  -对。谢谢。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Knife?   -Yeah. Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:34.51,0:26:35.84,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那把刀，以及买刀的经过\N{\rEN\blur0.8}The knife and the way it was bought
Dialogue: 0,0:26:36.01,0:26:37.76,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}是相当有力的证据，你们不觉得吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}is pretty strong evidence, don't you think?
Dialogue: 0,0:26:37.93,0:26:39.35,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-我觉得是。  -好。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-I do.   -Good.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:39.52,0:26:41.98,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}现在，我们不妨把这些事实一条一条来看。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Now, suppose we take these facts one at a time.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:42.14,0:26:44.02,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}第一，那男孩承认他出了家门\N{\rEN\blur0.8}One. The boy admitted going out of the house
Dialogue: 0,0:26:44.19,0:26:45.27,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}在凶案当晚八点\N{\rEN\blur0.8}at eight o'clock on the night of the murder
Dialogue: 0,0:26:45.44,0:26:47.44,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}在被父亲扇了几个耳光之后。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}after being slapped several times by his father.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:47.61,0:26:50.23,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}不，不。他没说“扇耳光”，他说的是“拳打”。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}No, no. No, he didn't say "slapped." He said "punched."
Dialogue: 0,0:26:50.40,0:26:52.57,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}扇耳光和拳打可不一样。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}There's a difference between a slap and a punch.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:52.74,0:26:55.24,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}在被父亲打了几下之后。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}After being hit several times by his father.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:55.40,0:26:57.91,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}第二。他直接去了附近一家旧货店\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Two. He went directly to a neighborhood junk shop
Dialogue: 0,0:26:58.08,0:26:59.87,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-在那儿买了一把那种……  -弹簧刀。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-where he bought one of those...   -Switch knives.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:00.04,0:27:01.87,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}……弹簧刀。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}... switchblade knives.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:02.04,0:27:03.87,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}这可不是一把普通的刀。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}This wasn't what you'd call an ordinary knife.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:04.04,0:27:06.62,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}它的刀柄和刀刃上都有很特别的雕花。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}It had a very unusual carved handle and blade.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:06.79,0:27:08.00,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}卖给他刀的那个店主\N{\rEN\blur0.8}The storekeeper who sold it to him
Dialogue: 0,0:27:08.17,0:27:10.84,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}说那是他店里进过的唯一一把这种刀。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}said it was the only one of its kind he had ever had in stock.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:11.42,0:27:15.22,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}第三。大约8点45分，他在一家酒馆门前见了几个朋友。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Three. He met some friends of his in front of a tavern about 8:45.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:15.38,0:27:16.68,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}到目前为止我说得对吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Am I right so far?
Dialogue: 0,0:27:16.84,0:27:18.85,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-对。  -当然对。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Yes, you are.   -You bet he is.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:19.01,0:27:22.14,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他和朋友们聊了大约一个小时，9点45分离开。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}He talked with his friends for about an hour, leaving them at 9:45.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:22.31,0:27:24.64,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}这期间，他们看到了那把弹簧刀。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}During this time, they saw the switch knife.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:25.35,0:27:26.31,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}第四。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Four.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:27.19,0:27:29.61,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他们在法庭上指认了凶器\N{\rEN\blur0.8}They identified the death weapon in court
Dialogue: 0,0:27:29.77,0:27:31.48,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}就是那把刀。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}as that very same knife.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:32.36,0:27:34.99,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}第五。他大约十点到家。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Five. He arrived home at about ten o'clock.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:35.15,0:27:37.57,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}现在，控方和这男孩的说法\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Now this is where the stories offered by the State and the boy
Dialogue: 0,0:27:37.74,0:27:39.07,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}开始出现一点分歧。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}begin to diverge slightly.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:39.62,0:27:42.12,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他声称自己大约11点半去看了电影\N{\rEN\blur0.8}He claims that he went to a movie at about 11:30
Dialogue: 0,0:27:42.29,0:27:46.29,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}3点10分回家，发现父亲死了，自己也被逮捕了。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}returning home at 3:10 to find his father dead and himself arrested.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:46.46,0:27:48.58,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他还声称，逮捕他的两名警探\N{\rEN\blur0.8}He also claims that the two detectives who arrested him
Dialogue: 0,0:27:48.75,0:27:50.59,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}把他从半层楼梯上推了下去。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}threw him down a half a flight of stairs.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:50.75,0:27:52.25,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那么，那把弹簧刀呢？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Now, what happened to the switch knife?
Dialogue: 0,0:27:52.80,0:27:55.55,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他声称在去看电影的路上，刀从他口袋的破洞掉了出去\N{\rEN\blur0.8}He claims that it fell through a hole in his pocket on the way to the movies
Dialogue: 0,0:27:55.72,0:27:59.89,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}时间大约在11点半到3点10分之间，之后他就再没见过。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}sometime between 11:30 and 3:10 and that he never saw it again.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:00.51,0:28:01.85,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}各位，这可真是个故事啊。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Now there's a tale, gentlemen.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:02.39,0:28:05.77,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我认为很明显，那男孩当晚根本没去看电影。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I think it's quite clear that the boy never went to the movies that night.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:05.93,0:28:07.90,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}家里没人看见他11点半出门。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}No one in the house saw him go out at 11:30.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:08.06,0:28:09.35,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}影院里也没人能认出他。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}No one at the theater identified him.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:09.52,0:28:11.69,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他连自己看了什么电影都记不住。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}He couldn't even remember the names of the pictures he saw.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:14.44,0:28:16.20,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-实际情况是这样的。  -谢谢。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-What actually happened is this.   -Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:16.36,0:28:19.49,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那男孩待在家里，又和父亲打了一架，\N{\rEN\blur0.8}The boy stayed home, had another fight with his father,
Dialogue: 0,0:28:19.66,0:28:20.95,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}把他刺死了\N{\rEN\blur0.8}stabbed him to death
Dialogue: 0,0:28:21.12,0:28:23.28,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}然后在12点10分离开了家。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}and left the house at ten minutes after 12:00.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:23.45,0:28:26.12,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他甚至还记得把刀上的指纹擦干净。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}He even remembered to wipe the knife clean of fingerprints.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:26.29,0:28:28.79,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你现在是想告诉我，这把刀\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Now are you trying to tell me that this knife
Dialogue: 0,0:28:28.96,0:28:31.08,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}真的从男孩口袋的破洞掉了出去\N{\rEN\blur0.8}really fell through a hole in the boy's pocket
Dialogue: 0,0:28:31.25,0:28:33.42,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}有人从街上捡到它，跑到男孩家\N{\rEN\blur0.8}someone picked it up off the street, went to the boy's house
Dialogue: 0,0:28:33.59,0:28:36.22,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}用它刺死他父亲，就为了试试刀快不快？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}and stabbed his father with it just to test its sharpness?
Dialogue: 0,0:28:36.38,0:28:38.47,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}不，我只是说，那男孩有可能弄丢了刀\N{\rEN\blur0.8}No, I'm just saying it's possible the boy lost his knife
Dialogue: 0,0:28:38.63,0:28:40.72,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}而别人用一把相似的刀刺死了他父亲。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}and that somebody else stabbed his father with a similar knife.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:40.89,0:28:43.10,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-只是有可能。  -看看这把刀。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-It's just possible.   -Take a look at this knife.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:45.56,0:28:47.68,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}这刀很不寻常。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}It's a very unusual knife.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:47.85,0:28:49.31,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我从没见过这样的刀。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I've never seen one like it.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:49.48,0:28:51.77,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}卖刀给男孩的店主也没见过。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Neither had the storekeeper who sold it to the boy.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:52.36,0:28:55.44,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你这不是要我们相信一个相当离谱的巧合吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Aren't you asking us to accept a pretty incredible coincidence?
Dialogue: 0,0:28:55.61,0:28:57.69,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我只是说，巧合是有可能的。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I'm just saying a coincidence is possible.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:57.86,0:28:59.57,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我说这不可能。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}And I say it's not possible.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:05.99,0:29:07.41,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-那把刀哪来的？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Where did that come from?
Dialogue: 0,0:29:07.58,0:29:08.83,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-你从哪儿弄来的？  -是同一把刀。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Where'd you get that?   -It's the same knife.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:09.00,0:29:11.83,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-你觉得自己在干什么？  -你从哪儿弄来的？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-What do you think you're doing?   -Where did you get it?
Dialogue: 0,0:29:12.46,0:29:14.63,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}昨晚我出去走了几个小时。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I went out walking for a couple of hours last night.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:14.80,0:29:16.34,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我走过那男孩家附近。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I walked through the boy's neighborhood.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:16.92,0:29:20.05,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我是在离男孩家两个街区的一家小当铺买的。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I bought that at a little pawnshop just two blocks from the boy's house.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:20.22,0:29:21.64,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}花了六美元。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}It cost six dollars.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:22.26,0:29:24.93,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}买卖弹簧刀是违法的。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}It's against the law to buy or sell switchblade knives.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:25.10,0:29:26.60,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}没错。我犯了法。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}That's right. I broke the law.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:26.76,0:29:30.56,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}听着，你这招可真高明。那你告诉我，这能证明什么。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Listen, you pulled a real bright trick. Now, supposing you tell me what it proves.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:31.10,0:29:33.23,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}也许那种刀有十把。那又怎样？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Maybe there are ten knives like that. So what?
Dialogue: 0,0:29:33.40,0:29:35.48,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-也许真有。  -那这说明了什么？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Maybe there are.   -Well, what does it mean?
Dialogue: 0,0:29:36.07,0:29:37.48,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你找到了另一把一样的刀。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You found another knife like it.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:37.65,0:29:39.53,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}这算什么，世纪大发现吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}What's that, the discovery of the age or something?
Dialogue: 0,0:29:39.70,0:29:41.90,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你是说，你要我们相信是别人刺死了他\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You mean you're asking us to believe that somebody else did the stabbing
Dialogue: 0,0:29:42.07,0:29:45.16,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-而且用的是一模一样的刀？  -可能性只有百万分之一。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-with exactly the same kind of knife?   -The odds are a million-to-one.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:45.32,0:29:48.04,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-有可能。  -但可能性不大。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-It's possible.   -But not very probable.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:49.00,0:29:50.83,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}好了，各位，都坐下吧。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Okay, fellas, let's take our seats.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:51.00,0:29:52.79,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}没必要到处站着。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}There's no point standing around all over the place.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:54.79,0:29:56.63,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你们知道，有意思的是，他居然能找到一把刀\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You know, it's interesting that he'd find a knife
Dialogue: 0,0:29:56.80,0:29:58.30,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}和那男孩买的刀一模一样。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}exactly like the one the boy bought.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:58.46,0:30:00.80,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}这有什么意思？“有意思”。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}What's interesting about it? "Interesting."
Dialogue: 0,0:30:01.38,0:30:02.93,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}呃，我不知道。我只是觉得挺有意思。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Well, I don't know. I just thought it was interesting.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:03.09,0:30:05.34,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我们这儿还有11个人认为他有罪。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}There are still 11 of us here who think he's guilty.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:05.51,0:30:07.35,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}对。你觉得你能达到什么目的？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Right. What do you think you're gonna accomplish?
Dialogue: 0,0:30:07.51,0:30:09.14,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你改变不了任何人的想法。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You're not gonna change anybody's mind.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:09.31,0:30:11.64,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}所以你要是想固执己见，让陪审团僵持不下，那就随你。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}So if you wanna be stubborn and hang this jury, go ahead.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:11.81,0:30:14.69,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那孩子会被再审一次，而且肯定会被判有罪，那是肯定的。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}The kid will be tried again and found guilty, sure as he's born.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:16.40,0:30:17.57,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}大概是这样。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}That's probably right.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:18.40,0:30:21.44,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那你打算怎么办？你知道，我们可能得在这儿待一整夜。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}So what are you gonna do? You know, we could be here all night.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:21.61,0:30:24.28,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}只是一夜而已。可一个男孩可能会死。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}It's only one night. A boy may die.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:24.99,0:30:27.41,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那咱们干脆在这儿安家算了，行吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Well, why don't we just set up house here, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:30:27.58,0:30:30.08,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}谁去把警察波齐叫来，再拿一副皮纳克尔牌来，\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Someone send for Potsy the policeman and get a pinochle deck,
Dialogue: 0,0:30:30.24,0:30:32.41,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}咱们就在这儿把这事儿熬到底。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}and we'll just sweat the whole thing out right here.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:34.12,0:30:37.08,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-我觉得他不该拿这事儿开玩笑。  -那你想让我怎么办？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-I don't think he ought to joke about it.   -What do you want me to do about it?
Dialogue: 0,0:30:37.25,0:30:39.00,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}哦，听着！我不明白这些\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Oh, listen! I don't see what all this stuff
Dialogue: 0,0:30:39.17,0:30:40.96,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}关于刀的这些东西跟这案子有什么关系。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}about the knife's got to do with anything.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:41.13,0:30:43.59,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}有人看见那孩子刺死了他父亲。我们还需要什么？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Somebody saw the kid stab his father. What more do we need?
Dialogue: 0,0:30:44.18,0:30:46.80,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你们能说得我耳朵起茧。懂我意思吧？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You guys can talk the ears right off my head. You know what I mean?
Dialogue: 0,0:30:46.97,0:30:49.64,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你们在这儿说话的时候，我三家修车厂都快垮了。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I got three garages of mine goin' to pot while you're talking.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:49.81,0:30:51.31,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}所以咱们赶紧结束，离开这儿。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}So let's get done and get outta here.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:51.48,0:30:53.89,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那把刀对地方检察官来说非常重要。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}The knife was very important to the district attorney.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:54.06,0:30:56.60,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-他花了一整天—— -他不过是个第十五助理检察官之类的。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-He spent a whole day-- -He's a 15th assistant or something.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:56.77,0:30:59.02,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-他懂什么？  -嘿，小声点。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-What does he know about it?   -Hey, let's hold it down.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:59.19,0:31:01.19,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}这些旁枝末节的争论只会拖慢我们。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}These side arguments are only slowing us up.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:04.24,0:31:06.86,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-那又怎么样？  -只有你一个人这么想。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Well, what about it?   -You're the only one.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:09.49,0:31:11.70,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I
Dialogue: 0,0:31:15.04,0:31:16.88,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我想向各位提个建议。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I have a proposition to make to all of you.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:18.25,0:31:19.71,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我要再发起一次投票。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I'm gonna call for another vote.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:21.34,0:31:26.47,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我希望你们11个人……用秘密书面投票。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I want you 11 men to... vote by secret written ballot.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:27.01,0:31:28.26,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我弃权。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I'll abstain.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:28.89,0:31:31.72,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}如果有11票赞成有罪，我就不再独自坚持。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}If there are 11 votes for guilty, I won't stand alone.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:31.89,0:31:35.06,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我们马上就把有罪裁决交给法官。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}We'll take in a guilty verdict to the judge right now.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:36.94,0:31:40.65,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}但只要有人投无罪，我们就留在这里谈清楚。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}But if anyone votes not guilty, we stay here and talk it out.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:44.28,0:31:46.82,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}好，就这么办。你们想试，我奉陪。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Well, that's it. If you want to try it, I'm ready.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:46.99,0:31:49.62,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-好吧，那就按麻烦的办法来。  -行，听起来公平。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-All right, let's do it the hard way.   -Okay, that sounds fair.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:49.78,0:31:51.41,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}大家都同意吗？有人不同意吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Everyone agreed? Anyone doesn't agree?
Dialogue: 0,0:31:51.58,0:31:53.66,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-好，好。开始吧。  -来，把这些传下去。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Fine, fine. Let's go.   -Here, pass these along.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:53.83,0:31:55.25,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}现在时间对吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Is that the right time?
Dialogue: 0,0:31:55.41,0:31:57.46,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}～J\N{\rEN\blur0.8}~J
Dialogue: 0,0:32:01.25,0:32:03.26,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}tJ\N{\rEN\blur0.8}tJ
Dialogue: 0,0:32:27.70,0:32:28.66,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}“有罪。”\N{\rEN\blur0.8}"Guilty."
Dialogue: 0,0:32:31.62,0:32:32.45,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}“有罪。”\N{\rEN\blur0.8}"Guilty."
Dialogue: 0,0:32:35.00,0:32:35.87,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}“有罪。”\N{\rEN\blur0.8}"Guilty."
Dialogue: 0,0:32:38.54,0:32:39.42,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}“有罪。”\N{\rEN\blur0.8}"Guilty."
Dialogue: 0,0:32:41.29,0:32:42.17,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}“有罪。”\N{\rEN\blur0.8}"Guilty."
Dialogue: 0,0:32:44.30,0:32:45.21,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}“有罪。”\N{\rEN\blur0.8}"Guilty."
Dialogue: 0,0:32:47.55,0:32:48.42,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}“有罪。”\N{\rEN\blur0.8}"Guilty."
Dialogue: 0,0:32:49.84,0:32:50.76,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}“有罪。”\N{\rEN\blur0.8}"Guilty."
Dialogue: 0,0:32:52.43,0:32:53.26,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}“有罪。”\N{\rEN\blur0.8}"Guilty."
Dialogue: 0,0:32:58.02,0:32:59.27,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}“无罪。”\N{\rEN\blur0.8}"Not guilty."
Dialogue: 0,0:33:00.19,0:33:01.69,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-“有罪。”\N{\rEN\blur0.8}- "Guilty."
Dialogue: 0,0:33:01.86,0:33:05.90,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-好家伙，这你怎么说？  -哦，又有一位老兄扑腾起翅膀了。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Boy, how do you like that?   -Oh, and another chap flaps his wings.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:06.07,0:33:08.65,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}好了，是谁投的？说吧，我想知道。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}All right, who was it? Come on, I wanna know.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:08.82,0:33:11.07,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}对不起，这是秘密投票。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Excuse me. This was a secret ballot.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:11.24,0:33:12.87,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我们都同意的，对吧？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}We all agreed on that, no?
Dialogue: 0,0:33:13.03,0:33:15.16,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}如果这位先生想保持匿名——\N{\rEN\blur0.8}If the gentleman wanted to remain secret--
Dialogue: 0,0:33:15.33,0:33:17.08,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}秘密？你什么意思，秘密？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Secret? What do you mean secret?
Dialogue: 0,0:33:17.24,0:33:20.16,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}陪审室里没有秘密。我知道是谁。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}There are no secrets in a jury room. I Know who it was.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:21.08,0:33:22.96,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}老兄，你可真有一套。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Brother, you really are something.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:23.13,0:33:25.17,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你坐在这儿，像我们其他人一样投有罪\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You sit here, vote guilty like the rest of us
Dialogue: 0,0:33:25.34,0:33:28.67,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}然后某个金嗓子的传教士开始把你的心撕碎\N{\rEN\blur0.8}and then some golden-voiced preacher starts tearin' your poor heart out
Dialogue: 0,0:33:28.84,0:33:31.93,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}说什么某个穷苦孩子就是没法不变成杀人犯\N{\rEN\blur0.8}about some underprivileged kid just couldn't help becomin' a murderer
Dialogue: 0,0:33:32.09,0:33:33.39,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你就改票了。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}and you change your vote.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:33.55,0:33:35.72,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}这要不是最恶心的……\N{\rEN\blur0.8}If that isn't the most sick...
Dialogue: 0,0:33:35.89,0:33:38.60,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你怎么不往他的募捐箱里投个二十五美分？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Why don't you drop a quarter in his collection box?
Dialogue: 0,0:33:39.39,0:33:41.39,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}哦，等等，等一下。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Oh, now just wait a minute.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:41.56,0:33:43.10,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-听着，你不能这样跟我说话。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Listen, you can't talk to me like that.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:43.27,0:33:45.19,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-不行。你以为你是谁？  -冷静点。冷静点。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-No. Who do you think you are?   -Calm down. Calm down.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:45.36,0:33:46.19,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}不行。他以为他是谁？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}No. Who does he think he is?
Dialogue: 0,0:33:46.36,0:33:48.28,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-你听见他说的了吗？  -没关系。他很容易激动。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Did you hear him?   -It doesn't matter. He's very excitable.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:48.44,0:33:50.65,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-坐下。  -容易激动？我当然容易激动！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Sit down.   -Excitable? You bet I'm excitable!
Dialogue: 0,0:33:50.82,0:33:53.78,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我们是要把一个有罪的人送上他该坐的电椅！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}We're trying to put a guilty man in the chair where he belongs!
Dialogue: 0,0:33:53.95,0:33:56.66,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}有人开始给我们讲童话，我们居然还听着！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Someone starts telling us fairy tales, and we're listenin'!
Dialogue: 0,0:33:56.83,0:33:58.37,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}嘿，行了，好不好？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Hey, come on, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:33:58.54,0:34:00.41,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你为什么改票？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}What made you change your vote?
Dialogue: 0,0:34:00.58,0:34:03.17,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他没改票。是我改的。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}He didn't change his vote. I did.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:03.33,0:34:05.13,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-哦，好啊。  -我就知道。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Oh, fine.   -I knew it.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:05.75,0:34:07.38,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你想让我告诉你为什么吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Would you like me to tell you why?
Dialogue: 0,0:34:07.55,0:34:09.59,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}不，我不想听你解释为什么。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}No, I wouldn't like you to tell me why.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:09.76,0:34:12.22,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}不过，如果你不介意，我还是想说清楚。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Well, I'd like to make it clear anyway, if you don't mind.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:12.38,0:34:15.51,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-我们非得听这些吗？  -这位先生想说。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Do we have to listen to this?   -The man wants to talk.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:15.68,0:34:16.68,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}谢谢。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:17.26,0:34:20.52,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}这位先生一直独自一人反对我们。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}This gentleman has been standing alone against us.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:20.68,0:34:23.02,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他并没有说这孩子无罪。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Now, he doesn't say the boy is not guilty.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:23.19,0:34:24.48,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他只是不确定。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}He just isn't sure.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:25.19,0:34:27.94,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}独自面对别人的嘲笑可不容易。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Well, it's not easy to stand alone against the ridicule of others.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:28.11,0:34:31.07,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}所以他赌一把寻求支持，我给了他支持。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}So he gambled for support, and I gave it to him.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:31.24,0:34:32.49,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我尊重他的动机。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I respect his motives.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:33.11,0:34:37.53,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}受审的男孩也许有罪，但是……我想再听听。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}The boy on trial is probably guilty, but... I want to hear more.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:37.70,0:34:39.45,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}现在是10票对2票。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Right now, the vote is 10 to two.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:39.62,0:34:41.75,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我在这儿说话呢！你没权离开这个房间！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I'm talking here! You have no right to leave this room!
Dialogue: 0,0:34:41.91,0:34:44.62,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他听不见你。他永远也听不见。坐下吧。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}He can't hear you. He never will. Let's sit down.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:50.09,0:34:51.21,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我们继续吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Shall we continue?
Dialogue: 0,0:34:51.88,0:34:54.22,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}呃，我……我觉得我们该休息一下。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Well, I... I think we ought to take a break.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:54.38,0:34:57.55,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你知道，有个人在里面，我觉得我们该等等他。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You know, one man's inside, and I think we ought to wait for him.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:58.39,0:34:59.93,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-好吧。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Okay.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:01.52,0:35:03.10,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}看来我们真卡住了，是吧？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Looks like we're really hung up here, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:35:04.44,0:35:06.81,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}还有那老头的事，真够出人意料的。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}And that thing with the old man, that was pretty unexpected.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:08.94,0:35:11.40,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}真希望我能想出个办法打破僵局。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I wish I could figure out some way we could break it up.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:13.24,0:35:18.20,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你知道，在广告业，我跟你说过我在一家广告公司工作。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You know, in advertising, I told you I worked in an agency.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:18.37,0:35:19.12,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}嗯哼。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Mm-hm.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:19.28,0:35:21.20,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那儿有些挺古怪的人。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Well, there's some pretty strange people working there.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:21.37,0:35:23.33,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}其实也不算古怪，我想。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Well, they're not strange really, I guess.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:23.50,0:35:26.25,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}只是他们表达自己的方式很特别。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}It's just that they have peculiar ways of expressing themselves.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:26.42,0:35:27.25,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你懂我意思吧。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You know what I mean.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:27.42,0:35:29.71,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}当然，我想你那行也一样吧？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Well, of course, I suppose it's the same in your business too, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:35:30.46,0:35:31.34,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你是做什么的？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}What do you do?
Dialogue: 0,0:35:32.09,0:35:34.13,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-我是钟表匠。  -哦，真的吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-I'm a watchmaker.   -Oh, really?
Dialogue: 0,0:35:34.30,0:35:36.89,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我想世界上最好的钟表匠都来自欧洲吧？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Well, I imagine the finest watchmakers in the world come from Europe, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:35:37.51,0:35:39.26,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}总之，就像我刚跟你说的，在广告公司里，\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Well anyway, as I was telling you, in an agency,
Dialogue: 0,0:35:39.43,0:35:40.64,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}当我们遇到这种僵局时……\N{\rEN\blur0.8}when we reach a point like this...
Dialogue: 0,0:35:40.80,0:35:42.35,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我跟他说，在广告公司里，\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I'm telling him about, in an ad agency,
Dialogue: 0,0:35:42.52,0:35:44.35,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}开会时遇到这种局面\N{\rEN\blur0.8}when a point like this is reached in a meeting
Dialogue: 0,0:35:44.52,0:35:46.69,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}总有个家伙随时准备好一个点子，明白吧。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}there's always some character ready with an idea, see.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:47.19,0:35:48.90,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}这真是要命。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}And it kills me.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:49.06,0:35:50.86,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他们那种方式真是世界上最奇怪的\N{\rEN\blur0.8}It's the weirdest thing in the world the way they
Dialogue: 0,0:35:51.02,0:35:53.57,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}有时会先在点子前加一句话，明白吧，比如……\N{\rEN\blur0.8}sometimes precede their idea with a little phrase, see, like...
Dialogue: 0,0:35:54.11,0:35:56.24,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}某个客户主管会站起来说……\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Some account exec will get up, and he'll say...
Dialogue: 0,0:35:57.11,0:35:59.03,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}“好，我有个点子。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}"Okay, here's an idea.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:59.20,0:36:02.28,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}咱们把它升到旗杆上，看看有没有人敬礼。”\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Let's, run it up the flagpole and see if anyone salutes it."
Dialogue: 0,0:36:02.45,0:36:05.29,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我是说，这很白痴，但挺好笑，是吧？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I mean, it's idiotic, but it's funny, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:36:06.04,0:36:09.63,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我……我刚才有点激动。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I... I got a little excited back there.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:09.79,0:36:12.96,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我……不是故意要那么凶。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I... didn't mean to get nasty.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:14.17,0:36:15.13,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我很高兴你不是那种\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I'm glad you're not one of those
Dialogue: 0,0:36:15.30,0:36:17.72,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}会被这种感情牌影响的人。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}lets these emotional appeals influence him.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:34.48,0:36:35.69,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我不知道那风扇怎么回事。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I don't know what's the matter with that fan.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:35.86,0:36:37.20,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}好像启动不了。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Can't seem to get it started.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:46.83,0:36:48.25,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}嘿，你是推销员吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Hey, you a salesman?
Dialogue: 0,0:36:48.92,0:36:50.21,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我是建筑师。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I'm an architect.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:51.46,0:36:52.29,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}嗯。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Hmm.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:53.00,0:36:54.84,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你知道什么叫‘软推销’吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You know what the soft sell is?
Dialogue: 0,0:36:58.13,0:36:59.93,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}好家伙，你说对了。相信我。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Boy, you got it. Believe me.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:01.55,0:37:02.93,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我有另一套手法。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I got a different technique.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:04.22,0:37:08.14,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}笑声、喝酒、笑话、花招，懂吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Laughs, drinks, jokes, tricks, you know?
Dialogue: 0,0:37:09.02,0:37:10.02,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}是啊。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:12.02,0:37:13.98,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}“直击要害。”这是我的座右铭。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}"Hit 'em where they live." That's my motto.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:15.44,0:37:17.90,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我去年卖橘子酱赚了两万七千块。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I made 27 grand last year sellin' marmalade.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:19.07,0:37:21.57,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}不错了。我是说，考虑到是卖橘子酱的。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}That's not bad. I mean, you know, considering marmalade.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:24.78,0:37:26.54,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}嘿，你图什么？图个刺激？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Hey, what are you gettin' outta this? Kicks?
Dialogue: 0,0:37:28.62,0:37:31.21,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}还是有人敲过你脑袋，你一直没缓过来？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Or did somebody bump you on the head one time and you haven't gotten over it?
Dialogue: 0,0:37:31.37,0:37:32.75,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}也许吧。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Maybe.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:33.33,0:37:36.17,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你知道，你们这些爱做好事的人都一个样。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-You know, you do-gooders are all alike.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:36.76,0:37:39.38,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你们总是为某个搞砸了的家伙大动肝火。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You're always blowing your stacks over some guy that fanned.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:42.47,0:37:44.22,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}可你干吗浪费我们的时间？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}But what are you wasting our time for?
Dialogue: 0,0:37:45.18,0:37:47.43,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你不如给这项事业捐五块钱，\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Why don't you donate five dollars to the cause,
Dialogue: 0,0:37:47.60,0:37:49.10,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}也许你会好受点。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}and maybe it'll make you feel better.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:52.56,0:37:53.94,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}这小子有罪，老兄。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}This kid is guilty, pal.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:54.98,0:37:56.78,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}这再明显不过了。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}It's as plain as the nose on your face.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:57.40,0:37:59.53,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那咱们干吗还在这儿浪费时间？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}So why don't we stop wasting our time here?
Dialogue: 0,0:37:59.69,0:38:01.95,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}再这么下去大家嗓子都要疼了，知道吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}We're gonna all get sore throats if we keep it up, you know?
Dialogue: 0,0:38:02.66,0:38:04.74,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你是在这儿喊哑嗓子，还是在球赛上喊哑嗓子，有什么区别？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}What difference does it make if you get it here or at the ball game?
Dialogue: 0,0:38:05.78,0:38:08.12,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}哦，没区别，老兄。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Oh, no difference, pal.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:09.12,0:38:10.29,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}一点区别都没有。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}No difference at all.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:22.80,0:38:24.47,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}这帮人真不错，是吧？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Nice bunch of guys, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:38:24.64,0:38:26.43,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}哦，他们跟别人差不多。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Oh, they're about the same as anyone else.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:26.93,0:38:29.89,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}天哪，这鬼天气真要命。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Boy, what a murderous day.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:30.93,0:38:33.77,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-你觉得我们还要待很久吗？  -我不知道。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-You think we'll be much longer?   -I don't know.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:34.60,0:38:38.19,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}哦，他绝对有罪，毫无疑问。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Oh, he's guilty for sure. Not a doubt in the whole world.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:38.36,0:38:41.03,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我们早该……早该结束了。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}We should... should've been done already.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:41.19,0:38:44.20,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}哦，我倒不介意，你知道。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Oh, I don't mind, you know.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:44.36,0:38:46.45,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}总比干活强。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Beats workin'.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:53.92,0:38:55.62,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你觉得他无罪，是吧？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You think he's not guilty, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:38:56.25,0:38:58.00,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我不知道。有可能。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I don't know. It's possible.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:58.80,0:39:02.46,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我跟你素不相识，但我敢打赌你这辈子没犯过比这更大的错。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Well, I don't know you, but I'm bettin' you never been wronger in your life.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:02.63,0:39:04.80,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你在浪费时间。你该收场了。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You're wasting your time. You ought to wrap it up.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:05.30,0:39:07.26,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}假设受审的人是你呢。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Supposing you were the one who was on trial.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:08.18,0:39:11.52,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我不习惯假设。我就是个干活的。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Well, I'm not used to supposing. I'm just a working man.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:11.68,0:39:15.77,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}假设的事归我老板管，不过……好吧，我试一个。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}My boss does the supposing, but... well, I'll try one.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:17.48,0:39:18.94,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}假设你说服我们所有人放弃了，\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Supposing you talk us all out of this,
Dialogue: 0,0:39:19.11,0:39:22.78,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}可那小子真拿刀捅了他父亲，嗯？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}and the kid really did knife his father, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:39:25.57,0:39:28.07,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}是\N{\rEN\blur0.8}IS
Dialogue: 0,0:39:31.95,0:39:33.75,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你准备好了吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Are you ready?
Dialogue: 0,0:39:34.41,0:39:36.79,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-那个。  -抱歉，蓝眼睛。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-That one.   -Sorry, blue eyes.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:38.25,0:39:39.50,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-嗯，还能在哪儿……  -好了，伙计们，\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Well, where else...   -Okay, fellas,
Dialogue: 0,0:39:39.67,0:39:40.84,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}大家就座吧。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}let's take our seats.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:41.63,0:39:43.30,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}看来我们要在这儿吃晚饭了，是吧？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Looks like we'll be here for dinner, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:39:43.46,0:39:45.97,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}好了，现在咱们……咱们谈正事吧。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Okay, now let's... let's get down to business.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:46.13,0:39:47.26,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那么，谁想先开始？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Now, who wants to start it off?
Dialogue: 0,0:39:47.43,0:39:48.84,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-我来。  -好，说吧。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-I would.   -Okay, go.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:49.01,0:39:50.43,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你，坐在那头那位。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You, down there.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:51.26,0:39:52.72,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}住在楼下的那个老人\N{\rEN\blur0.8}The old man who lived downstairs
Dialogue: 0,0:39:52.89,0:39:55.02,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}说他听见那孩子大喊：‘我要杀了你。’\N{\rEN\blur0.8}says he heard the kid yell out, "I'm gonna kill ya."
Dialogue: 0,0:39:55.18,0:39:57.60,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}一秒钟后，他听见身体倒地的声音。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}A second later, he heard the body hit the floor.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:57.77,0:39:58.98,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}然后他跑到门口，\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Now, he ran to the door,
Dialogue: 0,0:39:59.15,0:40:01.94,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}看见那孩子跑下楼梯，冲出房子。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}and he saw the kid running down the stairs and out of the house.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:02.11,0:40:03.11,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}这说明了什么？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}What does that mean to you?
Dialogue: 0,0:40:03.28,0:40:06.11,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我在想，那老人能多清楚地听见那孩子的声音\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Well, I was wondering how clearly the old man could have heard the boy's voice
Dialogue: 0,0:40:06.28,0:40:07.82,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-隔着天花板。  -他不是隔着天花板听见的。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-through the ceiling.   -He didn't hear it through the ceiling.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:07.99,0:40:09.74,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}窗户开着，楼上的窗户也开着。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}The window was open. So was the one upstairs.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:09.91,0:40:11.78,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-那晚很热，记得吗？  -可那是在另一间公寓。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-It was a hot night, remember?   -Well, it was another apartment.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:11.95,0:40:13.79,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}辨认声音没那么容易，\N{\rEN\blur0.8}It's not that easy to identify a voice,
Dialogue: 0,0:40:13.95,0:40:16.12,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-尤其是喊叫声。  -他在法庭上辨认出来了。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-particularly a shouting voice.   -He identified it in court.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:16.29,0:40:18.21,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}没错。别忘了街对面的那位女士。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}That's right. And don't forget the lady across the street.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:18.37,0:40:21.13,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}她正好往开着的窗户里看，看见那男孩捅了他父亲。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}She looked right in the open window and saw the boy stab his father.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:21.29,0:40:23.59,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-我是说，这对你来说还不够吗？  -不，不够。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Now, I mean, isn't that enough for you?   -No, it isn't.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:23.76,0:40:25.55,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}天哪，你们受得了这家伙吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Boy, how do you like this guy, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:40:25.72,0:40:27.43,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}简直像对着断线的电话说话。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}It's like talking into a dead phone.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:27.59,0:40:29.34,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}她说她透过车窗看见了凶杀\N{\rEN\blur0.8}She said she saw the killing through the windows
Dialogue: 0,0:40:29.51,0:40:30.72,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那是一列正在行驶的高架列车。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}of a moving elevated train.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:30.89,0:40:32.10,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那列车有六节车厢。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}There were six cars on the train.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:32.26,0:40:34.31,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}她是从最后两节车厢的窗户看见凶杀的。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}She saw the killing through the last two cars.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:34.47,0:40:36.22,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}她连最不起眼的细节都记得。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}She remembered the most insignificant details.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:36.39,0:40:37.77,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我看不出这有什么可争辩的。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I don't see how you can argue with that.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:38.56,0:40:42.94,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}这里有人知道一列高架列车……\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Has anybody here, any idea how long it would take an el...
Dialogue: 0,0:40:51.82,0:40:52.99,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}嘿！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Hey!
Dialogue: 0,0:40:53.16,0:40:54.66,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}这不是游戏。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}This isn't a game.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:58.87,0:41:00.38,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-你看见他了吗？  -嘿。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Did you see him?   -Hey.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:01.25,0:41:03.13,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-真不要脸。  -好了，听着——\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-The nerve.   -All right, listen--
Dialogue: 0,0:41:03.29,0:41:06.51,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-简直无耻。  -好了，算了。这不重要。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-The absolute nerve.   -All right, forget it. It's not important.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:06.67,0:41:08.59,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-“这不是游戏？” -不，不，冷静点。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-"This isn't a game?"   -No, no, calm down.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:08.76,0:41:11.97,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-他以为自己是谁？  -我跟你说，算了。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Who does he think he is?   -I'm telling you, forget it now.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:12.14,0:41:15.52,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}有谁知道一列高架列车\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Has anybody any idea how long it takes an elevated train
Dialogue: 0,0:41:15.68,0:41:17.64,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}以中速驶过某一地点需要多久？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}going at medium speed to pass a given point?
Dialogue: 0,0:41:17.81,0:41:19.35,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-这跟案子有什么关系？  -多久？猜猜看。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-What has that to do with anything?   -How long? Take a guess.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:19.52,0:41:21.40,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-我一点头绪都没有。  -你觉得呢？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-I wouldn't have the slightest idea.   -What do you think?
Dialogue: 0,0:41:22.10,0:41:24.02,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我不知道，也许十秒、十二秒？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I don't know, maybe ten, 12 seconds?
Dialogue: 0,0:41:25.11,0:41:26.65,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我觉得这猜得挺靠谱。还有谁？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I think that's a pretty good guess. Anyone else?
Dialogue: 0,0:41:26.82,0:41:28.15,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-我觉得差不多。  -得了吧。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-That sounds right to me.   -Come on.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:28.32,0:41:30.20,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-猜这个干吗？  -你说呢？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-What's the guessing game for?   -What do you say?
Dialogue: 0,0:41:30.36,0:41:32.78,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-十秒差不多。  -好。就算十秒。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Ten seconds is about right.   -All right. Say ten seconds.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:32.95,0:41:34.07,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-你想说什么？  -这个。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-What are you getting at?   -This.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:34.78,0:41:38.54,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}一列六节车厢的高架列车驶过某一地点需要十秒。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}It takes a six-car EL train ten seconds to pass a given point.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:38.70,0:41:41.46,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}现在假设这个地点就是那个房间开着的窗户\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Now let's say the given point is the open window of the room
Dialogue: 0,0:41:41.62,0:41:42.92,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}凶杀就发生在那房间里。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}where the killing took place.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:43.08,0:41:46.34,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}从那个窗户伸手出去，几乎能碰到高架轨道，对吧？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You can reach out of that window and almost touch the EL tracks, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:41:46.50,0:41:47.80,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}现在我问你们这个。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Now let me ask you this.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:47.96,0:41:50.13,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}这儿有人住过高架铁路附近吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Has anyone here ever lived near the EL tracks?
Dialogue: 0,0:41:50.30,0:41:52.89,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我刚刷完一套公寓的墙\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Well, I just finished painting an apartment
Dialogue: 0,0:41:53.05,0:41:54.26,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那套公寓正对着高架铁路。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}that overlooked an EL line.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:54.43,0:41:55.80,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-我在那儿待了三天。  -感觉怎么样？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-I was there for three days.   -What was it like?
Dialogue: 0,0:41:55.97,0:41:56.81,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-你指什么？  -很吵吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-What do you mean?   -Noisy?
Dialogue: 0,0:41:56.97,0:41:59.60,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}哦，天哪。不过倒无所谓，我们都快被吵晕了。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Oh, brother. Don't matter though. We were all punchy.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:59.77,0:42:02.27,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我住过一次高架铁路附近的二楼公寓。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I lived in a second-floor apartment near the EL line once.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:02.44,0:42:05.61,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}窗户一开，列车经过时，噪音几乎让人受不了。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}When the window was open and the train goes by, the noise is almost unbearable.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:05.77,0:42:06.90,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}吵得人根本没法思考。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You can hardly hear yourself think.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:07.07,0:42:08.40,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}好，吵得人没法思考。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}All right, you can't hear yourself think.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:08.57,0:42:10.65,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-你能说重点吗？  -我会的。再等一下。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Will you get to the point?   -I will. Now just a minute.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:10.82,0:42:13.99,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我们把两份证词放在一起看看。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Let's take two pieces of testimony and try to put them together.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:14.70,0:42:18.24,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}第一，楼下公寓里的老人。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}First. The old man in the apartment downstairs.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:19.00,0:42:21.37,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他说他听见那男孩说“我要杀了你”……\N{\rEN\blur0.8}He says he heard the boy say "I'm gonna kill you"...
Dialogue: 0,0:42:21.54,0:42:24.17,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}紧接着一秒钟后就听见有身体倒在地上。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}and a split second later heard a body hit the floor.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:24.33,0:42:25.96,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-一秒之后，对吧？  -对。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-One second later, right?   -That's right.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:26.13,0:42:31.84,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}第二，街对面的女人一口咬定她从窗户望出去\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Second. The woman across the street swore positively she looked out of the window
Dialogue: 0,0:42:32.01,0:42:34.14,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}透过最后两节车厢看见了凶案\N{\rEN\blur0.8}and saw the killing through the last two cars
Dialogue: 0,0:42:34.30,0:42:36.51,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那是一列驶过的高架列车，对吧？最后两节车厢。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}of a passing elevated train, right? The last two cars.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:36.68,0:42:39.18,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-你到底想说明什么？  -只是……等等，等一下。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-What are you giving us here?   -Just... now, just a minute.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:39.35,0:42:43.64,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我们都同意，列车经过某一点需要十秒钟。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}We've agreed that it takes ten seconds for a train to pass a given point.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:44.56,0:42:47.86,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}既然那女人是透过最后两节车厢看到凶案\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Since the woman saw the killing through the last two cars
Dialogue: 0,0:42:48.02,0:42:52.57,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我们可以推断，尸体倒地时列车正好经过。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}we can assume that the body hit the floor just as the train went by.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:53.32,0:42:57.49,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}因此，列车轰隆隆地经过老人窗前\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Therefore, the train had been roaring by the old man's window
Dialogue: 0,0:42:57.66,0:43:01.00,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}是在尸体倒地整整十秒之前。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}a full ten seconds before the body hit the floor.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:01.16,0:43:03.37,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}根据老人自己的证词，\N{\rEN\blur0.8}The old man, according to his own testimony,
Dialogue: 0,0:43:03.54,0:43:06.38,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}“我要杀了你”之后紧接着尸体就倒地，\N{\rEN\blur0.8}"I'm gonna kill you," body hitting the floor a split second later,
Dialogue: 0,0:43:06.54,0:43:08.96,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他必须听见男孩说这句话\N{\rEN\blur0.8}would have had to hear the boy make this statement
Dialogue: 0,0:43:09.13,0:43:12.51,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}而当时高架列车就在他窗前轰鸣。他不可能听得见。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}with the EL roaring past his nose. It's not possible he could've heard it.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:12.67,0:43:14.80,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-这太荒唐了。他当然听见了。  -你觉得他可能听见吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-That's idiotic. Of course he heard it.   -Do you think he could've heard it?
Dialogue: 0,0:43:14.97,0:43:17.14,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他说他是扯着嗓子喊的。我觉得这就够了。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}He said he yelled at the top of his voice. That's good enough for me.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:17.30,0:43:19.55,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}就算他听见了什么，也没法辨认出是谁的声音\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Even if he heard something, he still couldn't have identified the voice
Dialogue: 0,0:43:19.72,0:43:22.31,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-在高架列车轰鸣而过的时候。  -你说的是几秒钟的事！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-with the EL roaring by.   -You're talking about a matter of seconds!
Dialogue: 0,0:43:22.48,0:43:23.68,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}没人能那么精确。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Nobody can be that accurate.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:23.85,0:43:26.40,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我认为，能把一个男孩送上电椅的证词\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Well, I think testimony that could put a boy into the electric chair
Dialogue: 0,0:43:26.56,0:43:27.94,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}就应该那么精确。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}should be that accurate.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:30.07,0:43:31.65,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}知道吗？我觉得他不可能听见。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You know something? I don't think he could've heard it.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:32.24,0:43:34.49,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}也许他没听见。我是说，高架列车那么吵。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Maybe he didn't hear it. I mean, with all that EL noise.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:34.65,0:43:36.41,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}哦，你们到底在说什么？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Oh, what are you people talking about?
Dialogue: 0,0:43:36.57,0:43:38.49,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}按道理，他不可能听见。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Well, it stands to reason he couldn't have heard it.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:38.66,0:43:40.95,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他为什么要撒谎？他能得到什么好处？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Why should he lie? What's he got to gain?
Dialogue: 0,0:43:41.12,0:43:42.83,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}也许是想引人注意。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Attention, maybe.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:43.00,0:43:45.00,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你老爱说这些自作聪明的话！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You keep coming in with these bright sayings!
Dialogue: 0,0:43:45.16,0:43:47.79,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你怎么不寄给报社？他们一条给三块钱。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Why don't you send 'em in to a paper? They pay three dollars apiece.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:48.33,0:43:50.25,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你干吗那样跟他说话？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}What are you talking to him like that for?
Dialogue: 0,0:43:51.21,0:43:54.51,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}这样跟老人说话的人，真该被教训一顿，懂吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Guy talks like that to an old man really ought to get stepped on, you know?
Dialogue: 0,0:43:54.67,0:43:56.47,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你该放尊重些，先生。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You ought to have more respect, mister.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:57.76,0:44:02.10,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你再跟他说那种话，我就把你打趴下。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}If you say stuff like that to him again, I'm gonna lay you out.
Dialogue: 0,0:44:12.36,0:44:15.03,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你接着说。你……你想说什么都行。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Now you go ahead. You... you say anything you like.
Dialogue: 0,0:44:16.15,0:44:18.61,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你为什么觉得那老人可能撒谎？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Why do you think the old man might lie?
Dialogue: 0,0:44:19.32,0:44:22.66,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}只是我观察了他很久。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}It was just that I looked at him for a very long time.
Dialogue: 0,0:44:23.37,0:44:26.20,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他外套肩下的缝线裂开了。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}The seam of his jacket was split, under the shoulder.
Dialogue: 0,0:44:26.71,0:44:28.04,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你注意到了吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Or did you notice that?
Dialogue: 0,0:44:28.21,0:44:30.33,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我是说，他竟然那样就来出庭。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I mean, to come to court like that.
Dialogue: 0,0:44:31.00,0:44:32.21,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-为什么——\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Why--
Dialogue: 0,0:44:33.84,0:44:37.09,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他是个穿着破外套的非常年迈的老人。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}He was a very old man in a torn jacket.
Dialogue: 0,0:44:37.84,0:44:40.51,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他慢慢走向证人席。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}And he walked very slowly to the stand.
Dialogue: 0,0:44:41.26,0:44:44.93,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他拖着左腿，还想掩饰\N{\rEN\blur0.8}He was dragging his left leg and trying to hide it
Dialogue: 0,0:44:45.52,0:44:47.06,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}因为他觉得难为情。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}because he was ashamed.
Dialogue: 0,0:44:48.31,0:44:51.56,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我想我比在座任何人都了解这个人。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I think I Know this man better than anyone here.
Dialogue: 0,0:44:52.65,0:44:57.07,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他是个安静、胆怯、无足轻重的老人\N{\rEN\blur0.8}This is a quiet, frightened, insignificant old man
Dialogue: 0,0:44:57.24,0:44:59.82,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他……他这一辈子都什么也不是，\N{\rEN\blur0.8}who... who has been nothing all his life,
Dialogue: 0,0:45:00.78,0:45:02.49,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}从来没被人认可过\N{\rEN\blur0.8}who has never had recognition
Dialogue: 0,0:45:03.03,0:45:04.99,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}名字也从没上过报纸。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}or his name in the newspapers.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:05.91,0:45:07.50,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}没人认识他。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Nobody knows him.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:08.21,0:45:09.58,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}没人引用他的话。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Nobody quotes him.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:10.25,0:45:14.04,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}活了七十五岁，没人来向他请教。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Nobody seeks his advice after 75 years.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:14.88,0:45:18.76,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}先生们，一事无成是很可悲的。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Gentlemen, that's a very sad thing, to be nothing.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:19.68,0:45:23.76,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}这样的人需要别人引用他的话，需要有人听他说话。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}A man like this needs to be quoted, to be listened to.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:24.43,0:45:26.35,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}哪怕只被引用一次。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}To be quoted just once.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:26.52,0:45:28.18,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}这对他非常重要。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Very important to him.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:28.85,0:45:31.65,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}要他重新退回到无人注意的角落，太难了——\N{\rEN\blur0.8}It would be so hard for him to recede into the background--
Dialogue: 0,0:45:31.81,0:45:32.98,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-等等。  -当他有机会——\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Wait a minute.   -When there was a chance--
Dialogue: 0,0:45:33.15,0:45:35.90,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你想干什么，告诉我们他为了重要一次就会撒谎？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}What are you trying to do, tell us he'd lie just so he could be important once?
Dialogue: 0,0:45:36.07,0:45:38.94,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}不。他不会真的撒谎。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}No. He wouldn't really lie.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:39.11,0:45:42.41,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}但也许他让自己相信他听见了那些话\N{\rEN\blur0.8}But perhaps he made himself believe he heard those words
Dialogue: 0,0:45:42.57,0:45:44.58,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}也认出了那男孩的脸。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}and recognized the boy's face.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:44.74,0:45:47.20,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}这是我听过最离谱的说法。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}That's the most fantastic story I've ever heard.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:47.37,0:45:50.04,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你怎么能编出这种话？你凭什么这么说？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}How can you make up a thing like that? What do you know about it?
Dialogue: 0,0:45:59.09,0:46:01.34,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}哦，有人要止咳糖吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Oh, does anybody want a cough drop?
Dialogue: 0,0:46:01.51,0:46:03.55,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-不用，谢谢。  -我要一颗。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-No, thanks.   -I'll take one.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:03.72,0:46:04.64,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}随你怎么说。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You can say what you like.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:04.80,0:46:06.93,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我还是不明白怎么会有人觉得他无罪。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I still don't see how anybody can think he's not guilty.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:07.43,0:46:09.64,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我还想再谈另一件事。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}There's something else I'd like to talk about for a minute.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:09.81,0:46:10.81,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}谢谢。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Thanks.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:11.60,0:46:12.73,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我想我们已经证明，那个老人\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I think we've proved that the old man
Dialogue: 0,0:46:12.90,0:46:14.73,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}不可能听见男孩说“我要杀了你”。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}couldn't have heard the boy say "I'm gonna kill you."
Dialogue: 0,0:46:14.90,0:46:16.48,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-可要是—— -你们根本没证明。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-But supposing-- -You didn't prove it at all.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:16.65,0:46:18.94,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-你在说什么？  -要是他真的听见了呢。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-What are you talking about?   -Supposing he really did hear it.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:19.53,0:46:21.95,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}这句话，我们大家说过多少次？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}This phrase, how many times have all of us used it?
Dialogue: 0,0:46:22.11,0:46:23.49,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}大概几千次了。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Probably thousands.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:23.66,0:46:25.45,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}“亲爱的，为这事我都能杀了你。”\N{\rEN\blur0.8}"I could kill you for that, darling."
Dialogue: 0,0:46:25.62,0:46:27.58,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}“小子，你再敢那样，我就杀了你。”\N{\rEN\blur0.8}"Junior, you do that once more, and I'm gonna kill you."
Dialogue: 0,0:46:27.74,0:46:29.37,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}“上啊，洛奇，杀了他。”我们天天这么说。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}"Get in there, Rocky, and kill him." We say it every day.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:29.54,0:46:30.58,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}这不代表我们真会杀谁。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}That doesn't mean we're really gonna kill anybody.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:30.75,0:46:32.50,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}等等。你到底想跟我们说什么？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Wait a minute. What are you trying to give us here?
Dialogue: 0,0:46:32.66,0:46:36.42,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那句话是“我要杀了你”。那孩子是扯着嗓子喊的。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}The phrase was "I'm gonna kill you." The kid yelled it at the top of his lungs.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:36.58,0:46:37.63,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}别告诉我他不是那个意思。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Don't tell me he didn't mean it.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:37.80,0:46:40.13,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}任何人像他那样说这种话，就是当真的。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Anybody says a thing like that the way he said it, they mean it.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:40.30,0:46:41.88,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}唉，天哪，现在我也不知道了。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Well, gee, now I don't know.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:42.05,0:46:43.84,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我记得我跟一个人吵过架\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I remember I was arguing with a guy
Dialogue: 0,0:46:44.01,0:46:46.18,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}几周前在银行，他就在我旁边工作。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I work next to at the bank a couple weeks ago.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:46.34,0:46:48.31,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他骂我白痴，我就冲他吼了。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}He called me an idiot, so I yelled at him.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:48.47,0:46:51.31,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}听着，这家伙想让你相信一些根本不成立的事。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Now listen, this guy's trying to make you believe things that aren't so.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:51.48,0:46:53.64,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那孩子说过要杀他，而且他真杀了他。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}The kid said he was gonna kill him, and he did kill him.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:53.81,0:46:54.60,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我问你，\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Let me ask you this.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:54.77,0:46:56.60,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你真觉得那孩子会大声喊出那种话\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Do you really think the boy would shout out a thing like that
Dialogue: 0,0:46:56.77,0:46:58.27,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}让整条街都听见吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}so the whole neighborhood could hear him?
Dialogue: 0,0:46:58.44,0:47:00.48,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我不这么想。他聪明得很，不会那么做。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I don't think so. He's much too bright for that.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:00.65,0:47:04.90,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}聪明？他就是个无知的粗人。连英语都说不好。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Bright? He's a common ignorant slob. He don't even speak good English.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:05.57,0:47:07.82,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}“他连英语都说不好。”\N{\rEN\blur0.8}"He doesn't even speak good English."
Dialogue: 0,0:47:10.62,0:47:14.04,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}主席先生，我想改投无罪。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Mr. Foreman, I'd like to change my vote to not guilty.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:14.96,0:47:17.00,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-你说什么？  -你听见了。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-You what?   -You heard me.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:17.17,0:47:18.25,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你确定？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Are you sure?
Dialogue: 0,0:47:19.34,0:47:20.38,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}是的，我确定。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Yeah, I'm sure.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:20.96,0:47:23.13,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}投票结果是九比三，赞成有罪。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}The vote is nine to three, favor of guilty.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:23.30,0:47:26.14,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}哎，这可真是绝了，是吧？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Well, if this isn't the living end, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:47:30.10,0:47:32.56,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你凭什么？凭这家伙编的故事？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}What are you basing it on? The stories this guy made up?
Dialogue: 0,0:47:33.60,0:47:35.85,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你该去给那些怪里怪气的侦探杂志写稿。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You ought to write for one of those kooky detective magazines.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:36.02,0:47:37.19,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你能发大财。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You'd make a fortune.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:37.94,0:47:41.07,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}老天爷，那孩子自己的律师都知道他没戏。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}For crying out loud, the kid's own lawyer knew he didn't stand a chance.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:41.69,0:47:44.36,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}从一开始，他自己的律师就知道。你看得出来。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Right from the beginning, his own lawyer knew it. You could see it.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:45.28,0:47:48.91,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}好家伙，我跟你说，这家伙可真有两下子。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Boy, oh, boy. I'm tellin' you, this guy here is really something.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:49.66,0:47:51.45,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}听着，那孩子有律师，不是吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Look, the kid had a lawyer, didn't he?
Dialogue: 0,0:47:51.62,0:47:54.41,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}是律师替他辩护，不是你。你怎么这么多话？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}He presented his case, not you. How come you got so much to say?
Dialogue: 0,0:47:54.58,0:47:56.12,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}听着，律师也不是不会犯错。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Look, lawyers aren't infallible, you know.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:56.29,0:47:58.92,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-少来这套，拜托。嗯？嗯？  -他是法院指派的。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Baltimore, please. Huh? Huh?   -He was court-appointed.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:59.08,0:48:01.38,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-那是什么意思？  -嗯，可能有很多意思。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Now, what's that supposed to mean?   -Well, it could mean a lot of things.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:01.54,0:48:04.72,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}可能说明他不想接这个案子，或者不满被指派。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}It could mean he didn't want the case, or he resented being appointed.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:04.88,0:48:06.05,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}这种案子什么都给他带不来，\N{\rEN\blur0.8}It's the kind of case that brings him nothing
Dialogue: 0,0:48:06.22,0:48:09.05,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}没钱，没名声，连胜诉的机会都不大。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}no money, no glory, not even much chance of winning.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:09.55,0:48:12.52,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}对一个年轻律师来说，这可不是什么有前途的差事。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}That's not a very promising situation for a young lawyer.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:12.68,0:48:15.52,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他得真心相信自己的当事人，才能好好辩护，\N{\rEN\blur0.8}He'd really have to believe in his client to put up any kind of a good case
Dialogue: 0,0:48:15.68,0:48:17.56,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}而且，就像你刚才指出的，显然他并不相信。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}and, as you pointed out a minute ago, obviously he didn't.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:17.73,0:48:19.77,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他当然不信。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Of course he didn't.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:20.52,0:48:21.98,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}谁他妈的会信？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Who the heck could?
Dialogue: 0,0:48:22.90,0:48:25.24,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}也许只有他妈妈或者什么人会信。我……\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Except maybe some guy's mother or somebody. I...
Dialogue: 0,0:48:25.82,0:48:28.20,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}哎，看看，看看几点了，行吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Ah, look. Will you look at the time, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:48:28.36,0:48:30.12,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-行了。天哪……  -抱歉。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Come on. For crying out...   -Pardon me.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:30.78,0:48:33.20,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-我在这里做了些笔记……  -笔记。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-I have made some notes here...   -Notes.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:33.37,0:48:35.50,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}……我想，麻烦让我说几句。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}...I would like to please, to say something.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:35.66,0:48:38.29,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-好。  -我一直在认真听。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Yeah.   -I have been listening very carefully.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:38.46,0:48:42.75,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我觉得这个人提出了一些很好的观点。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}And it seems to me that this man has some very good points to make.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:42.92,0:48:47.59,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}从庭审呈现的情况看，表面上这孩子像是有罪。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}From what was presented at the trial, the boy looks guilty on the surface.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:47.76,0:48:51.10,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-但也许再深入想想呢？  -哦，拜托，行不行？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-But maybe if we go deeper?   -Oh, come on, will you?
Dialogue: 0,0:48:51.64,0:48:53.60,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我有个问题想问。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}There is a question I would like to ask.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:54.14,0:48:57.39,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我们假设这孩子真的杀了人。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Let us assume that the boy really did commit the murder.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:57.56,0:49:00.77,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}事情发生在12点过10分。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Now, this happened at ten minutes after 12:00.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:00.94,0:49:03.36,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那他是怎么被警察抓住的？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Now, how was he caught by the police?
Dialogue: 0,0:49:03.52,0:49:08.03,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他回到家……大概三点钟，\N{\rEN\blur0.8}He came back home... at three o'clock or so
Dialogue: 0,0:49:08.20,0:49:11.70,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}在自家走廊里被两个警探抓了。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}and he was captured by two detectives in the hallway of his house.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:11.87,0:49:16.54,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我的问题是，如果他真杀了父亲，\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Now, my question is, if he really had killed his father
Dialogue: 0,0:49:16.70,0:49:19.62,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}为什么三小时后还要回家？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}why would he come back home three hours later?
Dialogue: 0,0:49:19.79,0:49:21.96,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他不怕被抓吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Wouldn't he be afraid of being caught?
Dialogue: 0,0:49:22.88,0:49:24.42,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他回家拿刀。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}He came home to get his knife.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:24.59,0:49:27.13,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}把刀插在人胸口上不管，可不太好。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}It's not nice to go around leaving knives sticking in people's chests.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:27.30,0:49:29.97,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-是啊，尤其是亲戚。  -是啊。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Yeah, especially relatives.   -Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:30.13,0:49:31.89,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我看不出这有什么好笑的。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I don't see anything funny about it.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:32.80,0:49:35.97,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那孩子知道那把刀能被认出来是他刚买的。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}The boy knew the knife could be identified as the one he had just bought.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:36.14,0:49:37.81,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他得赶在警察之前拿到它。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}He had to get it before the police did.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:38.31,0:49:40.52,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}可如果他知道刀能被认出来，\N{\rEN\blur0.8}But if he knew the knife could be identified,
Dialogue: 0,0:49:40.69,0:49:42.52,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那当初为什么把刀留在那儿？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}why did he leave it there in the first place?
Dialogue: 0,0:49:43.27,0:49:46.19,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}嗯，我们可以假设那孩子是在惊慌中跑出去的，\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Well, I think we can assume the boy ran out in a state of panic
Dialogue: 0,0:49:46.36,0:49:48.19,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}刚杀完他父亲之后。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}after having just killed his father.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:48.94,0:49:51.57,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}等他终于冷静下来，才意识到把刀落在那里了。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}When he finally calmed down, he realized he had left his knife there.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:51.74,0:49:54.58,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}啊，那这就要看你怎么定义“惊慌”了。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Ah, this then depends on your definition of panic.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:55.08,0:49:56.99,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他得足够冷静，才能确保\N{\rEN\blur0.8}He would have had to be calm enough to see to it
Dialogue: 0,0:49:57.16,0:49:59.33,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}刀上没留下指纹。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}that there were no fingerprints left on the knife.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:59.96,0:50:03.46,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那么，这阵惊慌从哪里开始，又到哪里结束？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Now, where did this panic start and where did it end?
Dialogue: 0,0:50:04.17,0:50:06.71,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}听着，你投了有罪。你到底站哪边？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Look, you voted guilty. What side are you on?
Dialogue: 0,0:50:06.88,0:50:09.96,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我不认为自己必须忠于哪一方。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I don't believe I have to be loyal to one side or the other.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:10.13,0:50:11.42,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我只是在问问题。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I'm simply asking questions.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:12.09,0:50:14.51,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}嗯，这只是我随口一说，不过……\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Well, this is just off the top of my head, but...
Dialogue: 0,0:50:15.55,0:50:17.52,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}如果我是那孩子，人是我捅的，事是我干的，\N{\rEN\blur0.8}well, if I were the boy and I'd done the stabbing and everything
Dialogue: 0,0:50:17.68,0:50:19.31,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我会冒险回去拿刀。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I'd take a chance and go back for the knife.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:19.93,0:50:22.02,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我敢打赌他觉得没人看见他跑出去，\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I'll bet he figured that nobody had seen him running out
Dialogue: 0,0:50:22.52,0:50:24.48,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}而且尸体要到第二天才会被发现。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}and that the body wouldn't be discovered till the next day.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:25.23,0:50:26.90,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}毕竟那是半夜。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Well, after all, it was the middle of the night.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:27.07,0:50:29.48,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我敢打赌他觉得没人会到第二天才发现尸体。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I'll bet he'd figured nobody would find the body till the next day.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:29.65,0:50:31.65,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}抱歉，这正是我的重点。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Pardon. This is my whole point.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:31.82,0:50:35.53,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}街对面的女人作证说，她看见凶杀发生后的那一刻，\N{\rEN\blur0.8}The woman across the street testified that the moment after she saw the killing
Dialogue: 0,0:50:35.70,0:50:38.08,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}也就是火车开过之后的一刻，\N{\rEN\blur0.8}that is, a moment after the train went by,
Dialogue: 0,0:50:38.24,0:50:41.33,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}她尖叫起来，然后去打电话报警。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}she screamed and then went to telephone the police.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:41.50,0:50:44.75,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那么，那孩子肯定听到了尖叫声，\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Now, the boy certainly must have heard the scream
Dialogue: 0,0:50:44.92,0:50:47.29,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}所以他知道有人看见了什么。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}so he knew that somebody saw something.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:48.46,0:50:51.01,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我就是觉得他不会回去。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I just don't think that he would have gone back.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:51.17,0:50:54.22,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}两点。第一，在他惊慌的状态下，可能根本没听见尖叫。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Two things. One, in his state of panic, he may not have heard the scream.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:54.38,0:50:55.43,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}也许声音并不大。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Perhaps it wasn't very loud.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:55.93,0:50:59.35,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}第二，就算他听见了，也可能没把它和自己的行为联系起来。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Two, if he did hear it, he may not have connected it with his own act.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:59.52,0:51:02.48,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}别忘了，他住的街区，尖叫声相当常见。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Remember, he lived in a neighborhood where screams were fairly commonplace.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:02.64,0:51:04.44,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-这就是答案。  -也许吧。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-There's your answer.   -Maybe.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:05.10,0:51:08.19,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}也许那孩子确实杀了父亲，没听见尖叫，\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Maybe the boy did kill his father, didn't hear the scream
Dialogue: 0,0:51:08.36,0:51:12.19,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}确实惊慌地跑出去，三小时后确实冷静下来，\N{\rEN\blur0.8}did run out in a panic, did calm down three hours later
Dialogue: 0,0:51:12.36,0:51:14.49,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}冒险回来拿刀，冒着被警察抓住的风险。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}and come back to get the knife, risking being caught by the police.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:14.66,0:51:17.07,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}也许这些都发生了，但也许没有。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Maybe all of those things happened, but maybe they didn't.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:17.74,0:51:20.37,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我觉得疑点够多，足以让我们怀疑他到底在不在那里，\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I think there's enough doubt that we can wonder whether he was there at all
Dialogue: 0,0:51:20.54,0:51:21.83,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}在凶杀发生的时候。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}during the time the killing took place.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:22.00,0:51:23.54,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}什么叫疑点？你在说什么？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}What do you mean doubt? What are you talking about?
Dialogue: 0,0:51:23.71,0:51:25.33,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那老人不是看见他跑出房子了吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Didn't the old man see him running out of the house?
Dialogue: 0,0:51:25.50,0:51:27.54,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他在歪曲事实，我跟你说。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}He's twisting the facts, I'm telling you.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:27.71,0:51:30.88,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那老人到底看没看见那孩子12点10分跑出房子？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Did or didn't the old man see the kid running out of the house at 12:10?
Dialogue: 0,0:51:31.05,0:51:32.42,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那到底看见没有？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Well, did or didn't he?
Dialogue: 0,0:51:33.13,0:51:36.34,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-他说他看见了。  -他说他看见了？好家伙！你听听。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-He says he did.   -"Says he did?" Boy! How do you like that?
Dialogue: 0,0:51:36.51,0:51:39.56,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-听着，证人也会犯错。  -当然，你想让他们犯错时，他们就会。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Now, look, witnesses can make mistakes.   -Sure, when you want them to, they do.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:39.72,0:51:41.18,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}或者他希望他们犯错时，他们就会。你懂我意思吧？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Or when he wants them to, they do. You know what I mean?
Dialogue: 0,0:51:41.35,0:51:43.43,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-别嚷嚷了！  -哦，你就一直这么说。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Keep the yelling down!   -Oh, you keep saying that.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:43.60,0:51:45.18,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}也许这里就需要嚷嚷几句。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Maybe what we need is a little yelling in here.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:45.35,0:51:47.15,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}这些人老是东拉西扯。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}These guys keep going off every which way.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:47.31,0:51:49.11,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}听见尖叫了。没听见尖叫。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Did hear the scream. Didn't hear the scream.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:49.27,0:51:50.65,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那有什么区别？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}What difference does it make?
Dialogue: 0,0:51:50.82,0:51:52.74,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你们这些人只谈些细枝末节。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You people are talking only about the little details.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:52.90,0:51:55.03,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你们忘了重要的东西。我是说，突然之间，这里所有人——\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You're forgetting the important stuff. I mean, all of a sudden, everybody here--
Dialogue: 0,0:51:55.20,0:51:57.28,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-我要提议再投一次票。  -我这儿正说着呢！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-I wanna call for another vote.   -I'm talking here!
Dialogue: 0,0:51:57.45,0:52:00.95,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}有人提议再投一次票。现在都坐下吧。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}There's another vote called for. Now let's take our seats.
Dialogue: 0,0:52:05.04,0:52:07.71,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我从没见过为这么点事浪费这么多时间。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I never saw so much time spent on nothing.
Dialogue: 0,0:52:07.88,0:52:09.25,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}就一秒钟的事。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}It only takes a second.
Dialogue: 0,0:52:10.71,0:52:13.92,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}好吧，我看最快的办法就是搞清楚谁投无罪。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Okay, I guess the fastest way is to find out who's voting not guilty.
Dialogue: 0,0:52:14.09,0:52:16.26,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}现在，所有投无罪的，请举手。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Now, all those voting not guilty, please raise your hands.
Dialogue: 0,0:52:18.09,0:52:21.51,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}还是老样子。一、二、三票无罪。九票有罪。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Still the same. One, two, three not guilty. Nine guilty.
Dialogue: 0,0:52:21.68,0:52:23.02,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那现在是什么情况？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}So now where are we?
Dialogue: 0,0:52:23.18,0:52:25.06,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我跟你们说，我们可以一直扯到下周二。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I'm telling you, we can yackety-yack until next Tuesday.
Dialogue: 0,0:52:25.22,0:52:29.73,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-这有什么用？  -抱歉。我投无罪。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Where's it all getting us?   -Pardon. I vote not guilty.
Dialogue: 0,0:52:29.90,0:52:32.15,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-哦！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Oh!
Dialogue: 0,0:52:32.32,0:52:33.48,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你在说什么？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}What are you talking about?
Dialogue: 0,0:52:33.65,0:52:36.15,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我是说，我们这儿都疯了还是怎么的。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I mean, we're all going crazy in here or something.
Dialogue: 0,0:52:36.32,0:52:39.66,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那孩子有罪。你们为什么不听事实？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}The kid is guilty. Why don't you listen to the facts?
Dialogue: 0,0:52:40.16,0:52:42.37,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你跟他说说，行吗？这都快成笑话了。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Tell him, will you? Now this is getting to be a joke.
Dialogue: 0,0:52:42.53,0:52:45.00,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}投票结果是八比四，赞成有罪。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}The vote is eight to four, favor of guilty.
Dialogue: 0,0:52:45.79,0:52:49.04,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}这算什么，关爱贫困兄弟周还是什么？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}What is this, love your underprivileged brother week or something?
Dialogue: 0,0:52:49.83,0:52:52.09,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我要你站起来告诉我你为什么改投。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I want you to get up and tell me why you changed your vote.
Dialogue: 0,0:52:52.25,0:52:53.38,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}来吧。说说你的理由。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Come on, now. Give me your reasons.
Dialogue: 0,0:52:53.54,0:52:56.42,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我没必要向你解释我的决定。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I don't have to defend my decision to you.
Dialogue: 0,0:52:56.59,0:52:58.22,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我心里有合理怀疑。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}There is a reasonable doubt in my mind.
Dialogue: 0,0:52:58.38,0:53:01.26,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}什么合理怀疑？那不过是空话。来，看看这个。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}What reasonable doubt? That's nothing but words. Here, look at this.
Dialogue: 0,0:53:01.43,0:53:06.22,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你刚认定无罪的那个孩子，被人看见把这把刀捅进他父亲身体里。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}The kid you just decided isn't guilty was seen ramming this into his father.
Dialogue: 0,0:53:06.39,0:53:08.44,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}现在这个你怎么说，合理怀疑先生？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Now, what about this, Mr. Reasonable Doubt?
Dialogue: 0,0:53:08.60,0:53:10.60,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那不是那把刀。你不记得了吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}That's not the knife. Don't you remember?
Dialogue: 0,0:53:11.27,0:53:12.73,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}哦，真高明。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Oh, brilliant.
Dialogue: 0,0:53:13.23,0:53:15.23,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-我跟你说，这真是最疯的。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-I'm telling ya, this is the craziest.
Dialogue: 0,0:53:15.94,0:53:17.44,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我是说，我们到底该相信什么？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I mean, what are we supposed to believe?
Dialogue: 0,0:53:18.07,0:53:19.03,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我是说，你坐在这儿，\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I mean, you're sittin' here,
Dialogue: 0,0:53:19.20,0:53:20.91,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}凭空编故事，你知道吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}you're pulling stories out of thin air, you know?
Dialogue: 0,0:53:21.07,0:53:24.95,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}像这样的人，要是……坐在登普西对菲尔波拳赛的场边\N{\rEN\blur0.8}A guy like this, if he's... sitting ringside at the Dempsey-Firpo fight
Dialogue: 0,0:53:25.12,0:53:26.54,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他会想告诉你……\N{\rEN\blur0.8}he'd be trying to tell you that...
Dialogue: 0,0:53:27.41,0:53:29.71,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}看。那老人呢？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Look. Now, what about the old man?
Dialogue: 0,0:53:29.87,0:53:31.38,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我们该相信他没有起身\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Are we supposed to believe that he didn't get up
Dialogue: 0,0:53:31.54,0:53:33.50,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}跑到门口，看见那孩子冲下楼梯\N{\rEN\blur0.8}and run to his door and see the kid tearing down the steps
Dialogue: 0,0:53:33.67,0:53:35.34,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}在凶案发生后15秒？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}15 seconds after the killing?
Dialogue: 0,0:53:35.50,0:53:37.76,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他这么说只是为了显得重要，对吧？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}He's just saying so to be important, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:53:38.38,0:53:39.51,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我是说，这整件事有什么意义？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I mean, what's the point of the whole thing?
Dialogue: 0,0:53:39.68,0:53:40.51,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}等等。稍等一下，行吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Wait. Hold on a second, will you?
Dialogue: 0,0:53:40.68,0:53:42.84,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}哦，巴尔的摩的啦啦队长又开腔了\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Oh, and the Baltimore rooter is heard from again now
Dialogue: 0,0:53:43.01,0:53:44.56,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}高飞球都变成安打了\N{\rEN\blur0.8}and pop-ups are fallin' for base hits
Dialogue: 0,0:53:44.72,0:53:46.06,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-到处都是。  -等一下。看。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-wherever we look.   -Hold on a second. Now, look.
Dialogue: 0,0:53:46.72,0:53:48.52,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}老人是说他跑到门口吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Did the old man say he ran to the door?
Dialogue: 0,0:53:48.68,0:53:50.73,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}跑也好，走也好。有什么区别？他到了，不是吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Ran, walked. What's the difference? He got on, didn't he?
Dialogue: 0,0:53:50.89,0:53:52.35,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-我是说，他到那儿了，不是吗？  -不，等等——\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-I mean, he got there, didn't he?   -No, well, wait a second--
Dialogue: 0,0:53:52.52,0:53:54.40,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他说他是跑的。至少我觉得他是这么说的。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}He said he ran. At least I think he did.
Dialogue: 0,0:53:54.56,0:53:55.94,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}听着，我不记得他怎么说的了，\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Look, I don't remember what he said,
Dialogue: 0,0:53:56.11,0:53:57.53,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}可我不明白他怎么可能跑到门口。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}but I don't see how he could have run to the door.
Dialogue: 0,0:53:57.69,0:54:00.36,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他说他从卧室走到前门。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}He said he went from his bedroom to the front door.
Dialogue: 0,0:54:00.53,0:54:02.11,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-这还不够吗？  -卧室在哪儿？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Now, isn't that enough?   -Where was the bedroom?
Dialogue: 0,0:54:02.28,0:54:04.16,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-在走廊那头什么地方。  -我以为你什么都记得。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-It was down the hall somewhere.   -I thought you remembered everything.
Dialogue: 0,0:54:04.32,0:54:06.12,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-你不记得吗？  -不记得。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Don't you remember that?   -No.
Dialogue: 0,0:54:06.83,0:54:09.12,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}主席先生，我想看看公寓的平面图。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Mr. Foreman, I'd like to see a diagram of the apartment.
Dialogue: 0,0:54:09.29,0:54:11.46,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我说，干脆让他们把审判重新来一遍\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Look, why don't we just have 'em run the trial all over again
Dialogue: 0,0:54:11.62,0:54:13.17,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-好让你把一切弄清楚？  -为什么这屋里就你一个人\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-so you can get everything straight?   -How come you're the only one in this room
Dialogue: 0,0:54:13.33,0:54:14.75,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}老想看证物？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}wants to see exhibits all the time?
Dialogue: 0,0:54:14.92,0:54:17.63,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-我也想看看这个。  -我也想别再浪费时间了。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-I want to see this one too.   -And I'd like to stop wasting time.
Dialogue: 0,0:54:17.80,0:54:19.59,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}要是我们开始纠缠那些废话\N{\rEN\blur0.8}If we're gonna start wading through all that nonsense
Dialogue: 0,0:54:19.76,0:54:21.18,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-关于尸体在哪儿被发现。  -我们不会，\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-about where the body was found.   -We're not,
Dialogue: 0,0:54:21.34,0:54:24.26,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}除非还有人想。但我想弄清楚，一个老人\N{\rEN\blur0.8}not unless somebody else wants to. But I'd like to find out if an old man
Dialogue: 0,0:54:24.43,0:54:27.01,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}走路拖着一只脚，因为他去年中风\N{\rEN\blur0.8}who drags one foot when he walks 'cause he had a stroke last year
Dialogue: 0,0:54:27.18,0:54:29.43,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}能不能在15秒内从卧室到前门。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}can get from his bedroom to his front door in 15 seconds.
Dialogue: 0,0:54:29.60,0:54:31.14,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-他说20秒。  -他说15秒。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-He said 20 seconds.   -He said 15.
Dialogue: 0,0:54:31.31,0:54:33.35,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他说20秒。你想歪曲什么？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}He said 20 seconds. What are you trying to distort?
Dialogue: 0,0:54:33.52,0:54:37.06,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-他说15秒。  -他怎么知道15秒有多长？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-He said 15.   -How does he know how long 15 seconds is?
Dialogue: 0,0:54:37.23,0:54:39.57,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-这种事没法判断。  -他说15秒。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-You can't judge a thing like that.   -He said 15 seconds.
Dialogue: 0,0:54:39.74,0:54:41.94,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-他对此非常肯定。  -他是个老人。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-He was very positive about it.   -He was an old man.
Dialogue: 0,0:54:42.11,0:54:45.36,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他多半时候都糊里糊涂的。他怎么可能对什么那么肯定？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Half the time he was confused. How could he be positive about anything?
Dialogue: 0,0:54:53.29,0:54:55.00,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我看不出你想证明什么。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I don't see what you're going to prove here.
Dialogue: 0,0:54:55.17,0:54:57.50,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那人说他看见男孩跑出去。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}The man said he saw the boy running out.
Dialogue: 0,0:54:57.67,0:54:59.63,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那我们就看看细节是否支持他的说法。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Well, let's see if the details bear him out.
Dialogue: 0,0:54:59.80,0:55:02.92,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他说尸体一倒地，他就听到楼上脚步声\N{\rEN\blur0.8}As soon as the body hit the floor, he said he heard footsteps upstairs
Dialogue: 0,0:55:03.09,0:55:04.34,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}朝前门跑去，\N{\rEN\blur0.8}running toward the front door,
Dialogue: 0,0:55:04.51,0:55:07.51,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}听到楼上房门打开，脚步声开始下楼。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}heard the upstairs door open, the footsteps start down the stairs.
Dialogue: 0,0:55:07.68,0:55:09.68,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他说他以最快速度赶到自己前门\N{\rEN\blur0.8}He said he got to his own front door as fast as he could
Dialogue: 0,0:55:09.85,0:55:12.02,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他发誓那不可能超过15秒。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}and he swore it couldn't have been more than 15 seconds.
Dialogue: 0,0:55:12.18,0:55:13.85,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那么，如果凶手立刻开始跑——\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Now, if the killer began running immediately--
Dialogue: 0,0:55:14.02,0:55:16.02,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-也许他没有。  -老人说他跑了。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Maybe he didn't.   -The old man said he did.
Dialogue: 0,0:55:16.19,0:55:18.77,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你真该去大西洋城参加那个钻牛角尖大会。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You ought to be at Atlantic City at that hairsplitters convention.
Dialogue: 0,0:55:18.94,0:55:20.98,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-嘿，你能不能别老\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Hey, why don't you stop makin'
Dialogue: 0,0:55:21.15,0:55:23.11,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-说这些俏皮话，嗯？  -哦，朋友，\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-smart remarks all the time, huh?   -Oh, my friend,
Dialogue: 0,0:55:23.28,0:55:25.40,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你一天拿三块钱，就得什么都听，知道吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}for your three dollars a day, you have to listen to everything, you know?
Dialogue: 0,0:55:25.57,0:55:27.07,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-你把这东西带来了，那又怎样？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-You got it in here, what about it?
Dialogue: 0,0:55:27.24,0:55:28.99,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}好，这是凶案发生的公寓。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}All right, here's the apartment where the killing took place.
Dialogue: 0,0:55:29.16,0:55:31.91,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}老人的公寓就在正下方，布局完全一样。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}The old man's apartment was directly beneath and exactly the same.
Dialogue: 0,0:55:32.79,0:55:36.12,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}这里是高架铁路，卧室、客厅、厨房、浴室。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Here are the EL tracks, the bedroom, living room, kitchen, bathroom.
Dialogue: 0,0:55:36.29,0:55:38.04,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}这是走廊。这是楼梯。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Here's the hall. Here are the stairs.
Dialogue: 0,0:55:38.21,0:55:39.96,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}现在，老人就在这间卧室里。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Now, the old man was in this bedroom right here.
Dialogue: 0,0:55:40.50,0:55:43.05,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他说他走到门口，穿过走廊，\N{\rEN\blur0.8}He says he crossed to the door and walked down the hall,
Dialogue: 0,0:55:43.22,0:55:46.22,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}打开大门，正好看见那孩子跑下楼梯。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}opened the front door just in time to see the boy running down the stairs.
Dialogue: 0,0:55:46.38,0:55:48.39,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-到这儿我没错吧？  -他就是这样说的，\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Am I right so far?   -That's the story,
Dialogue: 0,0:55:48.55,0:55:50.81,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-说了十九遍了。  -十五秒\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-for the 19th time.   -Fifteen seconds
Dialogue: 0,0:55:50.97,0:55:53.10,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-尸体落地之后。  -没错。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-after the body hit the floor.   -Correct.
Dialogue: 0,0:55:53.27,0:55:54.73,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我们来算算。那是……\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Now, let's see. It was...
Dialogue: 0,0:55:55.52,0:55:58.98,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}从床到门是12英尺。走廊是43英尺。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}It's 12 feet from the bed to the door. The hall is 43 feet.
Dialogue: 0,0:55:59.56,0:56:02.73,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他得走12英尺，打开卧室门，\N{\rEN\blur0.8}He would have had to walk 12 feet, open the bedroom door,
Dialogue: 0,0:56:02.90,0:56:06.49,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}再走43英尺，打开大门，全在15秒内完成。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}walk 43 feet down and open the front door all in 15 seconds.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:06.66,0:56:08.82,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-你觉得他能做到吗？  -他当然能做到。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Do you think he could have done it?   -Sure he could have done it.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:08.99,0:56:10.28,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}可他只能走得很慢。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}He can walk only very slowly.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:10.45,0:56:11.95,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}还得有人扶他上证人席。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}They had to help him into the witness chair.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:12.12,0:56:13.70,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你说得好像路很长似的。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You make it sound like a long walk.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:13.87,0:56:16.00,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}对一个中风过的老人来说，那路是够长的。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}For an old man who had a stroke, it is a long walk.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:16.16,0:56:17.25,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}哦！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Oh!
Dialogue: 0,0:56:17.42,0:56:18.92,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-你干什么？  -我来试试，\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-What are you doing?   -I'm gonna try it,
Dialogue: 0,0:56:19.08,0:56:21.09,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-看看他花了多久。  -什么叫你要试试？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-see how long it took him.   -What do you mean, you wanna try it?
Dialogue: 0,0:56:21.25,0:56:23.13,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}这么重要，他的律师怎么没提？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Why didn't his lawyer bring it up if it's so important?
Dialogue: 0,0:56:23.30,0:56:24.42,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}也许他根本没想到，啊？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Maybe he just didn't think about it, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:56:24.59,0:56:26.38,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}什么叫没想到？你以为那人是白痴吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}What do you mean, didn't think of it? You think the man's an idiot or something?
Dialogue: 0,0:56:26.55,0:56:28.09,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-这么明显的事。  -你想到了吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-It's an obvious thing.   -Did you think of it?
Dialogue: 0,0:56:28.26,0:56:29.93,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}听着，聪明人。我有没有想到不重要。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Listen, smart guy. Don't matter whether I thought of it.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:30.10,0:56:31.43,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他没提，是因为他知道那会对自己不利。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}He didn't bring it up because he knew it would hurt his case.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:31.60,0:56:33.43,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-你怎么看？  -也许他没提\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-What do you think of that?   -Maybe he didn't bring it up
Dialogue: 0,0:56:33.60,0:56:36.44,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}是因为那等于欺负、刁难一个无助的老人。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}because it would have meant bullying and badgering a helpless old man.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:36.60,0:56:38.19,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你知道陪审团可不吃这一套。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You know that doesn't sit very well with a jury.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:38.35,0:56:40.02,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}大多数律师能避就避。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Most lawyers avoid it if they can.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:40.19,0:56:42.65,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-那他算什么混蛋？  -老兄，我一直在问的就是这个。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-So, what kind of a bum is he then?   -That's what I've been asking, buddy.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:42.82,0:56:45.78,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}把那把椅子递给我好吗？这两把椅子就是老人的床。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Pass me that chair, will you? Those two chairs are the old man's bed.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:45.94,0:56:48.70,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我刚在这屋里量了12英尺。这儿就是卧室门。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I just paced off 12 feet across the room. This will be the bedroom door.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:48.86,0:56:51.45,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}哦，太荒唐了，这种事没法重演。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Oh, that's crazy. You can't recreate a thing like that.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:51.62,0:56:53.37,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-我倒想看看。  -走廊是43英尺。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-I'd like to see it.   -The hall was 43 feet.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:53.54,0:56:55.12,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我从那堵墙走到头再走回来。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I'll pace from that wall and back again.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:57.08,0:56:58.71,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}瞧，这简直是疯了。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Look, this is absolutely insane.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:58.87,0:57:00.79,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你在这儿浪费大家时间干什么？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}What are you wasting everybody's time in here for?
Dialogue: 0,0:57:00.96,0:57:04.00,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}照你说，只要15秒。这点时间我们浪费得起，明白吗。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}According to you, it'll only take 15 seconds. Now, we can spare that, see.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:07.34,0:57:09.01,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}行了，别闹了。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Come on, knock it off.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:09.72,0:57:12.76,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}好，好好，杀手。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Okay. Okay, okay, killer.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:13.43,0:57:14.51,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}对。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:17.22,0:57:19.10,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你站那儿，标出大门的位置好吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Will you stand right there and mark the front door?
Dialogue: 0,0:57:19.64,0:57:21.86,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}证词说门上了链锁，记得吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}It was chain-locked according to the testimony, remember?
Dialogue: 0,0:57:22.02,0:57:23.36,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}谁有带秒针的表？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Has anybody got a watch with a second hand?
Dialogue: 0,0:57:23.52,0:57:24.82,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-我有。  -你想让我开始时，\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-I have.   -When you want me to start,
Dialogue: 0,0:57:24.98,0:57:26.53,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}就跺一下脚。那表示尸体落地。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}stamp your foot. That'll be the body falling.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:26.69,0:57:27.86,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你从那儿开始给我计时。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You can time me from there.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:28.70,0:57:30.70,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我们这是要干什么，玩猜谜游戏吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}What are we gonna do, play charades now?
Dialogue: 0,0:57:30.86,0:57:32.78,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-快点！还等什么？  -好，我准备好了。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Come on! What are we waiting for?   -Okay, I'm ready.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:32.95,0:57:34.66,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我想等秒针走到60。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Well, I want to wait till the second hand reaches 60.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:34.83,0:57:36.62,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}哦，得了吧。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Oh, come on.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:43.58,0:57:46.59,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}快点，走快些。他能比这快一倍。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Come on. Speed it up. He could walk twice as fast as that.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:48.05,0:57:50.30,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你要我走快些，我就走快些。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}If you want me to walk faster than that, I will.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:07.40,0:58:09.99,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}锁门。开门。停。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Lock. Door. Stop.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:10.15,0:58:11.78,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-对。  -多少时间？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Right.   -What's the time?
Dialogue: 0,0:58:12.91,0:58:15.53,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}整整41秒。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Exactly 41 seconds.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:15.70,0:58:17.58,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-我认为事情是这样的。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-This is what I think happened.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:17.74,0:58:19.41,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}老人听见那孩子和他父亲的争吵，\N{\rEN\blur0.8}The old man heard the fight between the boy and his father
Dialogue: 0,0:58:19.58,0:58:20.54,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那是几小时前。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}a few hours earlier.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:20.71,0:58:22.50,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}然后他躺在床上，听见有人倒地的声音\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Then when he's lying in bed, he heard the body hit the floor
Dialogue: 0,0:58:22.67,0:58:25.34,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}从男孩家传来，听见街对面女人的尖叫，\N{\rEN\blur0.8}in the boy's apartment, heard the woman scream from across the street,
Dialogue: 0,0:58:25.50,0:58:27.04,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他尽快赶到自家大门，\N{\rEN\blur0.8}got to his front door as fast as he could,
Dialogue: 0,0:58:27.21,0:58:29.67,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}听见有人冲下楼梯，就以为那是男孩。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}heard somebody racing down the stairs and assumed it was the boy.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:29.84,0:58:31.63,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-我觉得有可能。  -以为？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-I think that's possible.   -Assumed?
Dialogue: 0,0:58:34.26,0:58:37.26,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}老兄，我这辈子见过各种不老实的事，\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Brother, I've seen all kinds of dishonesty in my day,
Dialogue: 0,0:58:37.43,0:58:39.64,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}但这一出真是登峰造极。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}but this little display takes the cake.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:40.39,0:58:43.14,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你们一个个进来，心肝都哭出来了，\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You all come in here with your hearts bleeding all over the floor
Dialogue: 0,0:58:43.31,0:58:45.23,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}为贫民窟的孩子、为不公不义。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}about slum kids and injustice.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:45.40,0:58:47.40,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}听了几句童话，\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You listen to some fairy tales.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:47.57,0:58:49.69,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}突然就打动了几位老太太。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Suddenly you start getting through to some of these old ladies.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:49.86,0:58:51.86,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}可惜打动不了我。我受够了。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Well, you're not getting through to me. I've had enough.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:52.65,0:58:54.66,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你们这些人怎么了？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}What's the matter with you guys?
Dialogue: 0,0:58:54.82,0:58:57.20,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你们都知道他有罪！他得烧死！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You all know he's guilty! He's got to burn!
Dialogue: 0,0:58:57.37,0:58:59.16,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你们要让他从我们手里溜走。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You're letting him slip through our fingers.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:59.33,0:59:01.91,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}“从我们手里溜走？”你是他的刽子手吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}"Slip through our fingers?" Are you his executioner?
Dialogue: 0,0:59:02.08,0:59:03.37,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我是其中之一！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I'm one of 'em!
Dialogue: 0,0:59:04.71,0:59:06.46,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}也许你想亲手拉电闸。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Perhaps you'd like to pull the switch.
Dialogue: 0,0:59:06.63,0:59:09.63,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-为了这小子，我当然想。  -我为你感到难过。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-For this kid, you bet I would.   -I feel sorry for you.
Dialogue: 0,0:59:09.80,0:59:12.47,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}想拉电闸的人，那是什么滋味。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}What it must feel like to want to pull the switch.
Dialogue: 0,0:59:12.63,0:59:13.97,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}自从你走进这个房间，\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Ever since you walked into this room,
Dialogue: 0,0:59:14.13,0:59:16.55,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你就表现得像个自封的公义复仇者。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}you've been acting like a self-appointed public avenger.
Dialogue: 0,0:59:16.72,0:59:18.85,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你想看这孩子死，是因为你个人想这样，\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You want to see this boy die because you personally want it,
Dialogue: 0,0:59:19.01,0:59:20.22,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}而不是因为事实。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}not because of the facts.
Dialogue: 0,0:59:20.85,0:59:23.06,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-你是个虐待狂。  -你……\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-You're a sadist.   -YOU...
Dialogue: 0,0:59:23.94,0:59:26.98,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}放开我！我要杀了他！我要杀了他！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Let me go! I'll kill him. I'll kill him!
Dialogue: 0,0:59:27.31,0:59:29.57,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你不是真的想杀我吧？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You don't really mean you'll kill me, do you?
Dialogue: 0,0:59:36.91,0:59:39.33,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}先生们，出什么事了吗？我听见有响声。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Is there anything wrong, gentlemen? I heard some noise.
Dialogue: 0,0:59:39.49,0:59:41.37,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}哦，没事，一切都好。我们只是……\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Oh, no, everything's all right. We're just...
Dialogue: 0,0:59:41.54,0:59:43.08,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你知道，友好的小争论。这……\N{\rEN\blur0.8}you know, friendly little argument. It's...
Dialogue: 0,0:59:43.87,0:59:46.67,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}听着，那张图我们用完了。你要就拿走。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Listen, we're through with that diagram. You can take it if you want.
Dialogue: 0,0:59:48.04,0:59:49.71,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}给你。谢谢。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Here you are. Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,0:59:55.42,0:59:56.80,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你看什么看？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}What are you lookin' at?
Dialogue: 0,1:00:18.20,1:00:19.99,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}总得有人重新开始吧。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I suppose somebody has to start it off again.
Dialogue: 0,1:00:20.16,1:00:22.20,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-抱歉，您说什么？  -“抱歉，您说什么？”\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-I beg pardon.   -"I beg pardon."
Dialogue: 0,1:00:22.37,1:00:25.75,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-你干吗这么客气？  -就跟你干吗这么不客气的理由一样。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-What are you so polite about?   -For the same reason you're not.
Dialogue: 0,1:00:26.46,1:00:28.17,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我从小受的就是这种教育。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}It's the way I was brought up.
Dialogue: 0,1:00:30.25,1:00:31.46,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}这样争吵……\N{\rEN\blur0.8}This fighting...
Dialogue: 0,1:00:32.30,1:00:34.26,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我们到这里来，不是为了吵架。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}that's not why we are here, to fight.
Dialogue: 0,1:00:34.42,1:00:36.72,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我们有一份……责任。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}We have a... responsibility.
Dialogue: 0,1:00:37.97,1:00:42.60,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我一直认为，民主的可贵之处就在这里，\N{\rEN\blur0.8}This, I have always thought, is a remarkable thing about democracy
Dialogue: 0,1:00:42.76,1:00:44.43,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那就是我们……\N{\rEN\blur0.8}that we are...
Dialogue: 0,1:00:46.27,1:00:47.39,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那个词怎么说？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}What is the word?
Dialogue: 0,1:00:48.27,1:00:51.44,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}通知。就是我们收到邮件通知\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Notified. That we are notified by mail
Dialogue: 0,1:00:51.61,1:00:55.99,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}来这个地方裁定一个人有罪还是无罪\N{\rEN\blur0.8}to come down to this place to decide on the guilt or innocence
Dialogue: 0,1:00:56.15,1:00:59.49,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}而这个人我们……从没听说过。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}of a man we... have never heard of before.
Dialogue: 0,1:01:00.16,1:01:04.58,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}无论怎么裁决，我们都无所得也无所失。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}We have nothing to gain or lose by... by our verdict.
Dialogue: 0,1:01:05.58,1:01:08.62,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}这正是我们强大的原因之一。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}This is one of the reasons why we are strong.
Dialogue: 0,1:01:10.04,1:01:12.59,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我们不该把它变成个人恩怨。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}We should not make it a personal thing.
Dialogue: 0,1:01:14.13,1:01:15.13,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}谢谢。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,1:01:17.30,1:01:19.38,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}如果别人没主意，我这儿倒有个好点子。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}If nobody else has an idea, I might have a cutie here.
Dialogue: 0,1:01:19.55,1:01:22.22,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我是说，我没怎么细想，但咱们不妨把它扔到门廊上\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I mean, I haven't given it much thought, but let's throw it out on the stoop
Dialogue: 0,1:01:22.39,1:01:23.56,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}看看猫会不会舔掉。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}and see if the cat licks it up.
Dialogue: 0,1:01:23.72,1:01:26.10,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-猫会舔掉？  -对。如果那孩子……\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-The cat licks it up?   -Yeah. If the boy...
Dialogue: 0,1:01:30.77,1:01:32.69,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}看外面天多黑了。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Look how dark it's getting out there.
Dialogue: 0,1:01:33.40,1:01:35.23,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我敢打赌要下暴雨了。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I'll bet we're gonna have a storm now.
Dialogue: 0,1:01:36.98,1:01:39.45,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}天哪，真够热的，是吧？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Boy, oh, boy. It's really hot, huh?
Dialogue: 0,1:01:41.20,1:01:43.87,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}恕我冒昧，你从来不出汗吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Pardon me, but don't you ever sweat?
Dialogue: 0,1:01:45.37,1:01:46.54,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}不出。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}No, I don't.
Dialogue: 0,1:01:47.54,1:01:48.87,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}呃，听我说，我……\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Well, listen, I...
Dialogue: 0,1:01:49.62,1:01:51.17,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我在想是不是……\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I was wondering if...
Dialogue: 0,1:01:52.42,1:01:55.17,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}也许……也许我们该再投一次票。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}maybe... maybe we should take another vote.
Dialogue: 0,1:01:55.34,1:01:56.59,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}哦，好极了。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Oh, great.
Dialogue: 0,1:01:56.76,1:01:59.72,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}也许投完票还能跳个舞、吃点茶点，是吧？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Maybe we can follow this one up with a little dancing and refreshments, huh?
Dialogue: 0,1:01:59.88,1:02:02.01,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-嗯。  -主席先生？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Hmm.   -Mr. Foreman?
Dialogue: 0,1:02:02.18,1:02:05.22,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我没意见。有人不想投票吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Well, that's okay with me. Anyone doesn't want to vote?
Dialogue: 0,1:02:05.97,1:02:09.31,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-嘿，别这样。别这样。  -抱歉。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Hey, come on. Come on.   -I'm sorry.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:09.48,1:02:12.94,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我觉得应该公开投票，把票喊出来，懂吧。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I think we ought to have an open ballot, call out our votes, you know.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:13.10,1:02:14.98,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}看看谁站哪边。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Let's see who stands where.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:15.15,1:02:17.40,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}这听起来挺公平。有人反对吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Well, that sounds fair to me. Anyone object?
Dialogue: 0,1:02:20.44,1:02:22.36,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}好，我按陪审员编号点名。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Okay. I'll call off your jury numbers.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:22.53,1:02:26.95,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}一号。哦，是我。我投有罪。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}One. Oh, that's me. I vote guilty.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:27.12,1:02:28.12,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}二号？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Two?
Dialogue: 0,1:02:29.16,1:02:30.16,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}无罪。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Not guilty.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:30.91,1:02:33.54,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-三号？  -有罪。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Number three?   -Guilty.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:34.63,1:02:35.84,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}四号？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Number four?
Dialogue: 0,1:02:38.13,1:02:39.17,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}有罪。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Guilty.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:39.84,1:02:42.26,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-五号？  -无罪。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Number five?   -Not guilty.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:43.64,1:02:46.51,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-六号？  -无罪。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Number six?   -Not guilty.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:47.72,1:02:48.93,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}七号？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Number seven?
Dialogue: 0,1:02:49.85,1:02:50.98,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}有罪。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Guilty.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:51.48,1:02:52.60,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}八号？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Number eight?
Dialogue: 0,1:02:53.56,1:02:54.81,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}无罪。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Not guilty.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:56.65,1:02:58.73,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-九号？  -无罪。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Number nine?   -Not guilty.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:59.61,1:03:01.49,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-十号？  -有罪。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Number 10?   -Guilty.
Dialogue: 0,1:03:03.49,1:03:04.57,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}十一号？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Number 117?
Dialogue: 0,1:03:05.62,1:03:06.78,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}无罪。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Not guilty.
Dialogue: 0,1:03:07.58,1:03:08.66,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}十二号？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Number 12?
Dialogue: 0,1:03:10.00,1:03:11.33,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}十二号。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Number 12.
Dialogue: 0,1:03:12.46,1:03:13.50,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}有罪。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Guilty.
Dialogue: 0,1:03:20.05,1:03:21.55,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}现在票数是六比六。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}The vote is now six to Six.
Dialogue: 0,1:03:22.05,1:03:25.38,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}是啊，没错。咱们还得打加时赛，是吧？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Yeah, right. And we go into extra innings here, huh?
Dialogue: 0,1:03:27.47,1:03:29.64,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}六比六。我跟你们说，\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Six to six. I'm telling you,
Dialogue: 0,1:03:29.81,1:03:32.18,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你们这里有些人肯定是疯了。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}some of you people in here must be out of your minds.
Dialogue: 0,1:03:32.35,1:03:33.98,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}就那样的孩子。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}A kid like that.
Dialogue: 0,1:03:34.14,1:03:37.02,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我觉得他是什么样的人跟这案子没关系。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I don't think the kind of boy he is has anything to do with it.
Dialogue: 0,1:03:37.56,1:03:39.52,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}案子应该由事实来决定。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}The facts are supposed to determine the case.
Dialogue: 0,1:03:39.69,1:03:41.82,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}少来这套！我受够事实了！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Don't give me that! I'm sick and tired of facts!
Dialogue: 0,1:03:41.98,1:03:43.65,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}事实随便你怎么歪曲。你懂我意思吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You can twist them any way you like. You know what I mean?
Dialogue: 0,1:03:43.82,1:03:46.53,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}这位先生说的正是这个意思。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}That's exactly the point this gentleman has been making.
Dialogue: 0,1:03:46.70,1:03:48.16,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-哦！  -我是说，你一直在大喊\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Oh!   -I mean, you keep shouting
Dialogue: 0,1:03:48.32,1:03:50.37,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-扯着嗓子喊。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-at the top of your lungs.
Dialogue: 0,1:03:51.12,1:03:52.75,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我倒希望自己年轻几岁。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I'd like to be a few years younger.
Dialogue: 0,1:03:52.91,1:03:54.91,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那人真让我……\N{\rEN\blur0.8}That man gets on my...
Dialogue: 0,1:03:58.63,1:04:01.13,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-天哪，这里真热，是吧？  -你要喝点水吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-My, it's hot in here, isn't it?   -Do you want a drink of water?
Dialogue: 0,1:04:01.30,1:04:03.92,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}不用。不用，谢谢。谢谢。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}No. No, thanks. Thanks.
Dialogue: 0,1:04:11.68,1:04:14.06,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}要下雨了。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}It's gonna rain.
Dialogue: 0,1:04:14.89,1:04:16.69,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}哟，你是怎么琢磨出来的，高手？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Well, how'd you figure that out, killer?
Dialogue: 0,1:04:18.31,1:04:19.77,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你怎么改票了？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}How come you changed your vote?
Dialogue: 0,1:04:20.36,1:04:22.90,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}呃，我只是觉得还有怀疑的余地。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Well, it just seemed to me there was room for doubt.
Dialogue: 0,1:04:23.07,1:04:24.99,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你根本站不住脚。希望你自己明白。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You haven't got a leg to stand on. You know that, I hope.
Dialogue: 0,1:04:25.15,1:04:26.24,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}哦，我可不这么觉得。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Oh, I don't feel that way.
Dialogue: 0,1:04:26.40,1:04:28.16,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}有很多细节根本没摆出来。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}There were a lot of details that never came out.
Dialogue: 0,1:04:28.32,1:04:31.83,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-是啊。那祝你好运。  -哦，得了吧。你跟别人一样。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Yeah. Well, good luck.   -Oh, come on. You're like everybody else.
Dialogue: 0,1:04:31.99,1:04:33.95,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你想太多，把自己搞糊涂了。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You think too much. You get mixed up.
Dialogue: 0,1:04:35.37,1:04:37.04,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-你懂我意思吧？  -听着。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-You know what I mean?   -Now, listen.
Dialogue: 0,1:04:37.21,1:04:40.54,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我觉得你没资格……你这个大嘴巴。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I don't think you have any right... loudmouth.
Dialogue: 0,1:05:34.68,1:05:37.06,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你看那雨下的！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Look at that come down, will you?
Dialogue: 0,1:05:38.31,1:05:39.39,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你知道吗……\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You know...
Dialogue: 0,1:05:40.27,1:05:42.23,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}这让我想起去年……\N{\rEN\blur0.8}this reminds me of a storm we had last...
Dialogue: 0,1:05:42.90,1:05:45.78,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}哦，那是什么时候？十一月……\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Oh, when was that? November...
Dialogue: 0,1:05:46.57,1:05:49.65,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我不知道，大概吧。那场暴风雨可真不小。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I don't know, something. It was quite a storm we had there.
Dialogue: 0,1:05:49.82,1:05:51.16,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}正好赶上一场比赛。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}It was right in the middle of a game.
Dialogue: 0,1:05:52.41,1:05:54.62,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我们当时七比六落后，\N{\rEN\blur0.8}We were behind 7-6,
Dialogue: 0,1:05:54.78,1:05:57.20,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}但我们刚开始推进球，就在截锋那个位置。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}but we just started to move the ball, right off the tackle.
Dialogue: 0,1:05:57.37,1:06:00.25,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}开始左冲右突，\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Started cutting right slash here and slash right in,
Dialogue: 0,1:06:00.42,1:06:01.50,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}直接冲了过去。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}cut right through.
Dialogue: 0,1:06:02.04,1:06:03.13,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}然后……\N{\rEN\blur0.8}And...
Dialogue: 0,1:06:04.00,1:06:06.67,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我们有个小子，叫斯拉特里，知道吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}We had this kid, Slattery, you know?
Dialogue: 0,1:06:08.17,1:06:10.68,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}真是个……他壮得像头牛。知道吧，真像头牛。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}A real... He was an ox. You know, a real ox.
Dialogue: 0,1:06:11.59,1:06:13.34,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}真希望我再有一个像他这样的。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I wish I had another one just like him.
Dialogue: 0,1:06:14.14,1:06:15.30,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我忘了告诉你。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I forgot to tell you.
Dialogue: 0,1:06:15.47,1:06:18.72,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我是安德鲁·J·麦考克尔高中的助理主教练。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I'm the assistant head coach at the Andrew J. McCorkle High School.
Dialogue: 0,1:06:18.89,1:06:20.27,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-哦，是吗？  -那学校在皇后区。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Oh, yeah?   -That's out in Queens.
Dialogue: 0,1:06:20.98,1:06:22.48,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}总之……\N{\rEN\blur0.8}And anyway...
Dialogue: 0,1:06:23.86,1:06:25.65,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我们开始推进得很顺。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}we're starting to move along real nice.
Dialogue: 0,1:06:25.82,1:06:29.03,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他们整条防线就……开始崩溃了。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Their whole line is just... they're just coming apart.
Dialogue: 0,1:06:30.49,1:06:34.12,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}然后就开始下起倾盆大雨，就跟现在一样。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}And it starts to come down cats and dogs, just like this.
Dialogue: 0,1:06:34.28,1:06:36.74,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}哗的一下，你知道吧，就这么浇下来。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Just whoosh, you know, right down.
Dialogue: 0,1:06:38.16,1:06:40.91,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}唉，那真是要命，你知道吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Well, that was murder, you know?
Dialogue: 0,1:06:41.62,1:06:44.08,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我发誓，我……我差点哭出来。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I swear, I... I nearly bawled.
Dialogue: 0,1:06:44.25,1:06:46.00,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你根本……哪儿也去不了。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You just... You couldn't go nowhere.
Dialogue: 0,1:06:47.42,1:06:48.59,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}唉。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Well.
Dialogue: 0,1:07:04.85,1:07:07.02,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}嘿，这风扇怎么回事？怎么……\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Hey, what is it with this fan here? How come...
Dialogue: 0,1:07:14.99,1:07:16.87,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}嘿！嗯？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Hey! Huh?
Dialogue: 0,1:07:17.03,1:07:20.33,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}肯定是跟灯用同一个开关。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Must have been on the same switch with the lights.
Dialogue: 0,1:07:21.33,1:07:23.75,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}嗯，这儿情况好转了，是吧？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Well, things are looking up here, huh?
Dialogue: 0,1:07:25.08,1:07:26.25,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}是啊，对吧？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Yeah, huh?
Dialogue: 0,1:07:31.26,1:07:33.05,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}天哪，好多了。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Boy. Better.
Dialogue: 0,1:07:40.14,1:07:42.64,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}嘿！两分。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Hey! Two points.
Dialogue: 0,1:07:47.40,1:07:49.27,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你们有谁去过花园球馆？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Any of you guys ever go to the Garden?
Dialogue: 0,1:07:51.57,1:07:53.49,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那真是蠢透了。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}That's a damn stupid thing to do.
Dialogue: 0,1:07:54.86,1:07:56.86,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}哦，抱歉。我……\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Oh, I'm sorry. I...
Dialogue: 0,1:07:57.95,1:07:59.45,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你知道吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You know?
Dialogue: 0,1:08:00.87,1:08:01.87,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}对不起。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Pardon me.
Dialogue: 0,1:08:03.50,1:08:04.75,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}怎么样，你喜欢吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Well, how do you like it?
Dialogue: 0,1:08:04.91,1:08:07.46,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}打平了。挺让人吃惊的，是吧？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Even Steven. Pretty surprising, isn't it?
Dialogue: 0,1:08:08.50,1:08:09.42,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}是的。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Yes.
Dialogue: 0,1:08:11.67,1:08:15.30,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}对了，刚才那事，那个高个子叫什么来着\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Say, that business before, when that tall guy what's-his-name
Dialogue: 0,1:08:15.47,1:08:18.05,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}想激我，那什么都证明不了。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}was trying to bait me, that doesn't prove anything.
Dialogue: 0,1:08:18.22,1:08:20.72,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我是个……挺容易激动的人。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I'm a... pretty excitable person.
Dialogue: 0,1:08:20.89,1:08:24.73,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我是说，他凭什么说我什么公众复仇者、虐待狂之类的？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I mean, where does he come off calling me a public avenger, sadist, and everything?
Dialogue: 0,1:08:24.89,1:08:27.27,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}任何正常人都会发火的，对吧？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Anyone in his right mind would blow his stack, huh?
Dialogue: 0,1:08:28.27,1:08:29.86,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他就是在激我。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}He was just trying to bait me.
Dialogue: 0,1:08:30.69,1:08:32.23,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他干得很成功。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}He did an excellent job.
Dialogue: 0,1:08:35.28,1:08:37.70,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我说说我的看法。我们这么耗下去没意义。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I'll tell you what I think. We're going nowhere here.
Dialogue: 0,1:08:37.86,1:08:40.24,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我现在就准备进法庭宣布陪审团无法达成一致。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I'm ready to walk into court right now and declare a hung jury.
Dialogue: 0,1:08:40.41,1:08:42.12,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}这事再继续下去也没意义了。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}There's no point in this thing going on anymore.
Dialogue: 0,1:08:42.28,1:08:43.49,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}是啊，我也赞成。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Yeah, I go for that too.
Dialogue: 0,1:08:43.66,1:08:44.66,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}听着，我们交给法官吧\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Listen, let's take it in to the judge
Dialogue: 0,1:08:44.83,1:08:46.54,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}让这孩子去碰碰运气，换另外12个人来审。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}and let the kid take his chances with 12 other guys.
Dialogue: 0,1:08:46.71,1:08:48.33,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我觉得法官不会接受陪审团无法达成一致。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I don't think the judge will accept a hung jury.
Dialogue: 0,1:08:48.50,1:08:51.13,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-我们才进来没多久。  -那就试试看。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-We haven't been in here very long.   -Well, let's find out.
Dialogue: 0,1:08:51.29,1:08:52.84,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我不赞成这样。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I'm not in favor of that.
Dialogue: 0,1:08:53.00,1:08:56.38,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}听着。换一个陪审团，这孩子根本没机会，你心里清楚。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Listen. This kid wouldn't stand a chance with another jury, and you know it.
Dialogue: 0,1:08:56.55,1:08:59.38,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}行了！我们僵住了。没人会改主意。交上去吧。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Come on! We're hung. Nobody's gonna change his vote. Let's take it inside.
Dialogue: 0,1:08:59.55,1:09:01.51,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你还是觉得没有合理怀疑的余地？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You still don't think there's room for reasonable doubt?
Dialogue: 0,1:09:01.68,1:09:03.72,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-对，我不觉得。  -对不起。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-No, I don't.   -Pardon.
Dialogue: 0,1:09:04.35,1:09:08.06,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}也许你没完全理解“合理怀疑”这个词的意思。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Maybe you don't fully understand the term "reasonable doubt."
Dialogue: 0,1:09:08.23,1:09:10.23,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你说我不理解是什么意思？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}What do you mean I don't understand?
Dialogue: 0,1:09:11.27,1:09:12.86,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}天哪，你看看这家伙。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Boy, how do you like this guy?
Dialogue: 0,1:09:13.57,1:09:14.94,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我跟你说，他们都一个样。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I'm tellin' ya, they're all alike.
Dialogue: 0,1:09:15.11,1:09:16.57,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他们跑到这儿来，逃命来的，\N{\rEN\blur0.8}They come over here, running for their life,
Dialogue: 0,1:09:16.74,1:09:17.94,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}还没等喘口气\N{\rEN\blur0.8}and before they can take a deep breath
Dialogue: 0,1:09:18.11,1:09:19.70,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}就开始对我们指手画脚了，是吧？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}they're telling us how to run the show, huh?
Dialogue: 0,1:09:20.45,1:09:22.28,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}天哪，这家伙真傲慢。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Boy, the arrogance of this guy.
Dialogue: 0,1:09:22.45,1:09:23.74,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}嘿，好了。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Hey, all right.
Dialogue: 0,1:09:23.91,1:09:26.50,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我们在这儿先停两分钟别吵了。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Let's stop the arguing for about two minutes in here.
Dialogue: 0,1:09:27.04,1:09:29.37,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}好了，谁有建设性的意见？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Now, who's got something constructive to say?
Dialogue: 0,1:09:29.54,1:09:32.00,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}如果各位不介意，我想再过一遍某件事。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I'd like to go over something, if you gentlemen don't mind.
Dialogue: 0,1:09:33.25,1:09:36.26,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}控方的一个重要论点是……\N{\rEN\blur0.8}An important point for the prosecution was the fact that...
Dialogue: 0,1:09:37.13,1:09:38.92,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}孩子声称他在看电影\N{\rEN\blur0.8}after the boy claimed he'd been at the movies
Dialogue: 0,1:09:39.09,1:09:40.68,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}在凶案发生的那几个小时里\N{\rEN\blur0.8}during the hours that the killing took place
Dialogue: 0,1:09:40.84,1:09:44.35,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}却记不住电影的名字，也记不住出演的明星。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}couldn't remember the names of the movies or the stars who appeared in them.
Dialogue: 0,1:09:44.89,1:09:47.35,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}这位先生已经好几次提到这点了。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}This gentleman here has brought that point in here several times.
Dialogue: 0,1:09:47.52,1:09:48.77,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}没错。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}That's correct.
Dialogue: 0,1:09:48.94,1:09:50.65,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那是孩子唯一提供的不在场证明\N{\rEN\blur0.8}It was the only alibi the boy offered
Dialogue: 0,1:09:50.81,1:09:53.19,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}而他自己根本拿不出任何细节来支持。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}and he himself couldn't back it up with any details at all.
Dialogue: 0,1:09:53.36,1:09:56.78,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你设身处地想想，换作是你，你觉得你能记住细节吗\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Putting yourself in the boy's place, do you think you could remember details
Dialogue: 0,1:09:56.94,1:09:58.99,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}在经历那种让人心烦意乱的事，比如被你父亲\N{\rEN\blur0.8}after an upsetting experience such as being slapped
Dialogue: 0,1:09:59.15,1:10:00.28,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}扇了一巴掌之后？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}in the face by your father?
Dialogue: 0,1:10:00.45,1:10:03.20,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我觉得能，如果有值得记住的特殊细节。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I think so, if there were any special details to remember.
Dialogue: 0,1:10:03.74,1:10:05.45,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那孩子记不住他看的电影名字\N{\rEN\blur0.8}The boy couldn't remember the names of the movies he saw
Dialogue: 0,1:10:05.62,1:10:06.99,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}是因为他那晚根本不在那儿。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}because he wasn't there that night.
Dialogue: 0,1:10:07.16,1:10:08.83,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}根据法庭上警方的证词\N{\rEN\blur0.8}According to the police testimony in court
Dialogue: 0,1:10:09.00,1:10:12.04,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}孩子是在他公寓的厨房里接受侦探问话的，\N{\rEN\blur0.8}the boy was questioned by the detectives in the kitchen of his apartment,
Dialogue: 0,1:10:12.21,1:10:14.75,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}而他父亲的尸体就躺在卧室的地板上。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}while the body of his father was lying on the floor in the bedroom.
Dialogue: 0,1:10:15.34,1:10:17.71,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你觉得在那种情况下你能记住细节吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Do you think you could remember details under those circumstances?
Dialogue: 0,1:10:17.88,1:10:19.80,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-我能。  -在极大的情绪压力下？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-I do.   -Under great emotional stress?
Dialogue: 0,1:10:19.97,1:10:22.47,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-在极大的情绪压力下。  -他在法庭上记得一清二楚。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Under great emotional stress.   -He remembered them correctly in court.
Dialogue: 0,1:10:22.64,1:10:24.43,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他说出了片名和出演的明星。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}He named the pictures and the stars who played in them.
Dialogue: 0,1:10:24.60,1:10:27.68,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}是的。他的律师费了好大劲才把这点引出来。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Yes. His lawyer took great pains to bring that out.
Dialogue: 0,1:10:27.85,1:10:30.31,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}从凶案那晚到开庭那天，他有三个月时间\N{\rEN\blur0.8}He had three months from the night of the murder to the day of the trial
Dialogue: 0,1:10:30.48,1:10:31.85,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}来记住这些。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}in which to memorize them.
Dialogue: 0,1:10:32.02,1:10:33.73,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}律师不难查出来\N{\rEN\blur0.8}It's not difficult for a lawyer to find out
Dialogue: 0,1:10:33.90,1:10:36.40,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}某个晚上某个影院放了什么。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}what played at a particular theater on a particular night.
Dialogue: 0,1:10:36.57,1:10:38.23,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我更相信警察的证词\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I'll take the testimony of the policemen
Dialogue: 0,1:10:38.40,1:10:40.40,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他们在凶案后马上审问了孩子，\N{\rEN\blur0.8}who interrogated the boy right after the murder,
Dialogue: 0,1:10:40.57,1:10:42.70,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}当时他对电影的事一点都记不起来。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}when he couldn't remember a thing about the movies.
Dialogue: 0,1:10:42.86,1:10:44.66,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}不管有没有极大的情绪压力。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Great emotional stress or not.
Dialogue: 0,1:10:45.16,1:10:48.33,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-我想问你个私人问题。  -问吧。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-I'd like to ask you a personal question.   -Go ahead.
Dialogue: 0,1:10:48.49,1:10:51.41,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-你昨晚在哪？  -我在家。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Where were you last night?   -I was home.
Dialogue: 0,1:10:51.58,1:10:54.21,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-那前一晚呢？  -拜托！这是干什么？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-How about the night before that?   -Come on! What is this?
Dialogue: 0,1:10:54.38,1:10:55.46,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}不，没关系。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}No, that's all right.
Dialogue: 0,1:10:55.63,1:10:58.17,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我8点半离开办公室，直接回家睡觉了。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I left the office at 8:30 and went straight home and to bed.
Dialogue: 0,1:10:58.34,1:10:59.84,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那再前一晚呢？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}And the night before that?
Dialogue: 0,1:11:00.01,1:11:02.34,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那是……周二晚上？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}That was... Tuesday night?
Dialogue: 0,1:11:02.51,1:11:04.80,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}桥牌锦标赛那晚。我打桥牌了。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}The night of the bridge tournament. I played bridge.
Dialogue: 0,1:11:04.97,1:11:05.84,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}周一晚上？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Monday night?
Dialogue: 0,1:11:06.01,1:11:08.51,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}等你问到1954年除夕夜的时候，告诉我一声，行吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}When you get down to New Year's Eve, 1954, let me know, huh?
Dialogue: 0,1:11:11.14,1:11:12.60,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}周一晚上？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Monday night?
Dialogue: 0,1:11:14.35,1:11:17.56,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}周一晚上……我和我妻子去看电影了。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Monday night... my wife and I went to the movies.
Dialogue: 0,1:11:17.73,1:11:19.15,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-看了什么？  -《猩红圈》。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-What did you see?   -The Scarlet Circle.
Dialogue: 0,1:11:19.32,1:11:22.36,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-一部很巧妙的侦探片。  -第二部是什么？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-It was a clever whodunit.   -What was the second feature?
Dialogue: 0,1:11:22.53,1:11:23.70,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那个……\N{\rEN\blur0.8}The...
Dialogue: 0,1:11:25.20,1:11:26.91,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}马上告诉你。那个……\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I'll tell you in a minute. The...
Dialogue: 0,1:11:27.91,1:11:32.79,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}非凡的……太太，什么的……那个……\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Remarkable Mrs., something... the...
Dialogue: 0,1:11:34.92,1:11:37.63,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}班布里奇太太。《非凡的班布里奇太太》。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Mrs. Bainbridge. The Remarkable Mrs. Bainbridge.
Dialogue: 0,1:11:37.79,1:11:40.50,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我看过。是叫《了不起的班布里奇太太》。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I saw that. It's called The Amazing Mrs. Bainbridge.
Dialogue: 0,1:11:41.80,1:11:43.92,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}对，《了不起的班布里奇太太》。我想是这样。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Yes, The Amazing Mrs. Bainbridge. I think that's right.
Dialogue: 0,1:11:44.09,1:11:45.84,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}《了不起的班布里奇太太》是谁演的？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Who was in The Amazing Mrs. Bainbridge?
Dialogue: 0,1:11:46.64,1:11:50.31,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}芭芭拉……朗，我想是的。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Barbara... Long, I think it was.
Dialogue: 0,1:11:50.47,1:11:52.10,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}一个黑发、很漂亮的姑娘。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}A dark, very pretty girl.
Dialogue: 0,1:11:53.94,1:11:56.27,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}大概叫“林”还是“朗”之类的。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Ling or Long something like that.
Dialogue: 0,1:11:56.44,1:11:59.27,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-还有谁？  -我以前都没听过他们。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Who else?   -I'd never heard of them before.
Dialogue: 0,1:11:59.90,1:12:03.49,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那是一部很廉价的副片，演员都是些无名……\N{\rEN\blur0.8}It was a very inexpensive second feature with, unknown...
Dialogue: 0,1:12:04.24,1:12:06.82,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}而且你当时也没有情绪压力，对吧？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}And you weren't under an emotional stress, were you?
Dialogue: 0,1:12:10.03,1:12:11.16,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}没有。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}No.
Dialogue: 0,1:12:12.37,1:12:13.58,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我没有。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I wasn't.
Dialogue: 0,1:12:16.08,1:12:17.54,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我觉得这一点已经说清楚了。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I think the point is made.
Dialogue: 0,1:12:17.71,1:12:20.46,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}了不起的一点！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Big point!
Dialogue: 0,1:12:20.63,1:12:22.67,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你就是说到舌头拖到地上也没用。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You can talk till your tongue is draggin' on the floor.
Dialogue: 0,1:12:22.84,1:12:26.05,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那孩子有罪，就这样。你懂我意思吧，朋友？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}The boy is guilty, period. You know what I mean, my friend?
Dialogue: 0,1:12:27.01,1:12:30.30,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-谁还有那止咳糖？  -都吃完了，朋友。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Who's got those cough drops?   -They're all gone, my friend.
Dialogue: 0,1:12:32.27,1:12:34.02,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}哎哟，看这雨。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Oh, boy. Look at that rain.
Dialogue: 0,1:12:34.52,1:12:35.85,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你的球赛泡汤了。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}There goes your ball game.
Dialogue: 0,1:12:37.10,1:12:38.48,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}只是阵雨。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}It's only a shower.
Dialogue: 0,1:12:39.52,1:12:41.61,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}再说，内场有盖布。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Besides, they got the infield covered.
Dialogue: 0,1:12:41.77,1:12:44.86,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}对。喂，能把那把刀给我看一下吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Right. Say, could I see that knife a second, please?
Dialogue: 0,1:12:47.66,1:12:49.99,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我们还是六比六平。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Well, we're still tied up six to six.
Dialogue: 0,1:12:50.16,1:12:51.41,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}谁有什么建议？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Who's got a suggestion?
Dialogue: 0,1:12:52.24,1:12:54.12,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}六点过五分了。我们去吃点晚饭吧。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}It's five after 6:00. Let's get some dinner.
Dialogue: 0,1:12:54.29,1:12:56.66,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我们不如等到七点，再给它一个小时，怎么样？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Why don't we wait till seven o'clock, give it another hour, huh?
Dialogue: 0,1:12:56.83,1:12:57.79,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我没意见。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Okay with me.
Dialogue: 0,1:12:58.92,1:13:01.13,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我有点话想说。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}There's something I'd like to say.
Dialogue: 0,1:13:01.29,1:13:04.17,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我是说，这事一直让我有点不安，既然我们卡在这儿了。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I mean, it's been bothering me a little, and as long as we're stuck.
Dialogue: 0,1:13:05.05,1:13:08.93,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}就是关于那个刺伤，还有它是怎么造成的，\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Well, there was this whole business about the stab wound and how it was made,
Dialogue: 0,1:13:09.09,1:13:10.43,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那个向下的角度，你们知道吧？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}the downward angle of it, you know?
Dialogue: 0,1:13:10.60,1:13:12.60,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}别告诉我我们又要从头来一遍。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Don't tell me we're gonna start with that again.
Dialogue: 0,1:13:12.76,1:13:14.22,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}这已经翻来覆去说过多少遍了。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}They've been over it and over it.
Dialogue: 0,1:13:14.39,1:13:16.60,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我知道说过很多遍，但我不认同。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Well, I know they did, but I don't go along with it.
Dialogue: 0,1:13:16.77,1:13:20.85,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那男孩身高五英尺七英寸。他父亲是六英尺二英寸。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Now, the boy was 5 feet 7 inches tall. His father was 6'2".
Dialogue: 0,1:13:21.02,1:13:22.73,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}差七英寸。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}That's a difference of seven inches.
Dialogue: 0,1:13:23.48,1:13:25.69,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}要向下刺进一个比你高半英尺多的人的胸膛，\N{\rEN\blur0.8}It's a very awkward thing to stab down into the chest
Dialogue: 0,1:13:25.86,1:13:27.78,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那是很别扭的。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}of someone who's more than half a foot taller than you are.
Dialogue: 0,1:13:27.94,1:13:28.95,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}把那个给我。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Give me that.
Dialogue: 0,1:13:30.20,1:13:32.82,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我给你们演示一下。谁站起来。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I'll give you a demonstration. Somebody get up.
Dialogue: 0,1:13:34.20,1:13:35.37,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You.
Dialogue: 0,1:13:40.62,1:13:43.34,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你们仔细看着，因为我不想再来一遍。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I want you to watch this 'cause I don't want to have to do it again.
Dialogue: 0,1:13:43.50,1:13:46.38,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我把自己的身高降低六到七英寸，行吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I'll make myself about six or seven inches shorter, okay?
Dialogue: 0,1:13:46.55,1:13:49.38,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-差不多。也许再多一点。  -好，再多一点。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-It's about right. Maybe a little more.   -Okay. A little more.
Dialogue: 0,1:13:57.43,1:13:59.56,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-这不好笑。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}- That's not funny.
Dialogue: 0,1:14:01.69,1:14:05.77,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}好了，没人受伤吧？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Now, nobody's hurt. Right?
Dialogue: 0,1:14:06.27,1:14:07.61,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}对，没人受伤。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Right. Nobody hurt.
Dialogue: 0,1:14:11.61,1:14:16.37,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}这就是我刺杀一个比我高的人的方式。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Now, this is the way I'd stab a man who was taller than I was.
Dialogue: 0,1:14:16.54,1:14:18.58,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}看这个角度。向下，向内。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Look at the angle. Down and in.
Dialogue: 0,1:14:19.20,1:14:20.62,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}而当时的伤口就是这么造成的。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}And this is the way it was done.
Dialogue: 0,1:14:21.21,1:14:22.62,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}现在告诉我我错了。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Now tell me I'm wrong.
Dialogue: 0,1:14:25.63,1:14:28.46,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-向下向内。我看没什么好争的了。  -等一下，好吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Down and in. I guess there's no argument.   -Hold it a minute, will you?
Dialogue: 0,1:14:29.09,1:14:30.17,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}能把那个给我吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Can you give me that?
Dialogue: 0,1:14:31.93,1:14:33.18,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}天哪，我讨厌这玩意儿。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Boy, I hate these things.
Dialogue: 0,1:14:33.89,1:14:35.55,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-你见过持刀打斗吗？  -没有。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Did you ever see a knife fight?   -No.
Dialogue: 0,1:14:35.72,1:14:37.14,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-你呢？  -没有。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-You?   -No.
Dialogue: 0,1:14:37.31,1:14:40.14,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-这儿有谁见过持刀打斗吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Anybody here ever see a knife fight?
Dialogue: 0,1:14:40.31,1:14:42.98,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我见过。就在我家后门台阶上，\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Well, I have. You know, on my back stoop,
Dialogue: 0,1:14:43.15,1:14:45.23,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}街对面的空地、后院。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}the lot across the street, backyard.
Dialogue: 0,1:14:45.40,1:14:47.69,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我住的那一带，弹簧刀是家常便饭。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Switchblades came with the neighborhood where I lived.
Dialogue: 0,1:14:48.27,1:14:51.11,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}奇怪，我以前从没想过这个。大概人总想忘掉那些事吧。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}It's funny I never thought of it before. I guess you try to forget those things.
Dialogue: 0,1:14:51.28,1:14:54.78,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-弹簧刀怎么用？  -你绝不会这样用。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-How do you use a switchblade?   -Well, you'd never use it like this.
Dialogue: 0,1:14:56.45,1:14:58.54,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你看，换手太耽误时间。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}See, you lose too much time switching hands.
Dialogue: 0,1:15:00.62,1:15:02.96,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}是这样。从下往上。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Here's how. Underhanded.
Dialogue: 0,1:15:05.84,1:15:09.00,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}用过弹簧刀的人，绝不会用别的方式。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Anyone who's ever used a switch knife wouldn't handle it any other way.
Dialogue: 0,1:15:09.17,1:15:11.05,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-你确定？  -我确定。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Are you sure?   -I'm sure.
Dialogue: 0,1:15:11.63,1:15:13.34,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}所以它才设计成那样弹开。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}That's why they're made to open like that.
Dialogue: 0,1:15:13.51,1:15:15.26,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你是说那男孩用刀很熟练？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You'd say the boy was pretty handy with a knife?
Dialogue: 0,1:15:15.43,1:15:16.18,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}嗯。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Mm-hm.
Dialogue: 0,1:15:16.34,1:15:19.31,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你觉得他能造成杀死他父亲的那种伤口吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You think he could have made the kind of wound that killed his father?
Dialogue: 0,1:15:19.47,1:15:22.94,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}不能。以他一辈子摆弄这玩意儿的身手，不会那样。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}No. Not with the experience he'd had all his life handling these things.
Dialogue: 0,1:15:23.60,1:15:25.35,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我觉得他会从下往上刺。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I feel he'd have gone for him underhanded.
Dialogue: 0,1:15:25.52,1:15:28.69,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你怎么知道？他父亲被杀时你在房间里吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}How do you know? Were you in the room when the father was killed?
Dialogue: 0,1:15:28.86,1:15:30.73,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}没有。别人也没有。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}No. Neither was anybody else.
Dialogue: 0,1:15:30.90,1:15:34.11,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那你跟我们扯这些废话干什么？我不信。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}So what are you giving us all this mumbo jumbo for? I don't believe it.
Dialogue: 0,1:15:34.28,1:15:36.16,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我认为你没法断定什么样的伤口\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I don't think you can determine what type of wound
Dialogue: 0,1:15:36.32,1:15:37.58,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}是那男孩可能或不可能造成的\N{\rEN\blur0.8}the boy might or might not have made
Dialogue: 0,1:15:37.74,1:15:39.58,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}就因为他会用刀。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}simply because he knew how to handle a knife.
Dialogue: 0,1:15:40.24,1:15:41.37,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你怎么想？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}What do you think?
Dialogue: 0,1:15:42.66,1:15:44.71,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-我不知道。  -你说不知道是什么意思？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-I don't know.   -What do you mean you don't know?
Dialogue: 0,1:15:44.87,1:15:46.08,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我不知道。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I don't know.
Dialogue: 0,1:15:50.84,1:15:52.05,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你呢？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}How about you?
Dialogue: 0,1:15:52.92,1:15:54.01,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我不知道其他人怎么想，\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I don't know about the rest of them,
Dialogue: 0,1:15:54.18,1:15:56.59,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}但我有点受够这样来回扯皮了。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}but I'm getting a little tired of this yackety-yackin' back and forth.
Dialogue: 0,1:15:56.76,1:15:59.56,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}一点用都没有。所以我只好打破僵局了。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}It's gettin' us nowhere. So I guess I'll have to break it up.
Dialogue: 0,1:16:00.31,1:16:02.10,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我改投无罪。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I change my vote to not guilty.
Dialogue: 0,1:16:02.93,1:16:06.10,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-你什么？  -你听见了。我受够了。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-You what?   -You heard me. I've had enough.
Dialogue: 0,1:16:06.27,1:16:08.52,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你受够了是什么意思？这算什么回答！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}What do you mean you've had enough? That's no answer!
Dialogue: 0,1:16:08.69,1:16:12.53,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}喂，听着。你还是管好你自己吧，懂吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Hey, listen. You just take care of yourself, huh? You know?
Dialogue: 0,1:16:12.69,1:16:15.95,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他说得对。这不算回答。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}He's right. That's not an answer.
Dialogue: 0,1:16:17.32,1:16:19.41,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你算什么男人？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}What kind of a man are you?
Dialogue: 0,1:16:19.99,1:16:23.24,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你坐在这儿跟大家一样投有罪，\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You have sat here and voted guilty with everyone else
Dialogue: 0,1:16:23.41,1:16:27.00,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}就因为你口袋里那几张棒球票烧得你坐不住。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}because there are some baseball tickets burning a hole in your pocket.
Dialogue: 0,1:16:27.62,1:16:28.92,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}现在你又改了票\N{\rEN\blur0.8}And now you've changed your vote
Dialogue: 0,1:16:29.08,1:16:31.84,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}就因为你说你听腻了这些讨论？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}because you say you're sick of all the talking here?
Dialogue: 0,1:16:32.59,1:16:34.26,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}喂，听着，伙计！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Now listen, buddy!
Dialogue: 0,1:16:34.42,1:16:38.97,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}谁给了你这样拿别人的命当儿戏的权利？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Who tells you that you have the right to play like this with a man's life?
Dialogue: 0,1:16:39.14,1:16:41.06,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-你就不在乎——-等等！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Don't you care-- -Now wait a minute!
Dialogue: 0,1:16:41.72,1:16:45.52,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-你不能这样跟我说话！  -我就能这样跟你说话。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-You can't talk like that to me!   -I can talk like that to you.
Dialogue: 0,1:16:45.68,1:16:47.60,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你要是想投无罪\N{\rEN\blur0.8}If you want to vote not guilty
Dialogue: 0,1:16:47.77,1:16:49.98,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那就因为确信他无罪而投\N{\rEN\blur0.8}then do it because you are convinced the man is not guilty
Dialogue: 0,1:16:50.15,1:16:51.48,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}而不是因为你受够了。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}not because you've had enough.
Dialogue: 0,1:16:52.11,1:16:54.57,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你要是觉得他有罪，那就那样投。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}And if you think he is guilty, then vote that way.
Dialogue: 0,1:16:55.07,1:16:57.86,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}还是你没胆子做你认为对的事？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Or don't you have the guts to do what you think is right?
Dialogue: 0,1:16:58.03,1:17:00.32,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-听着。  -有罪还是无罪？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Now listen.   -Guilty or not guilty?
Dialogue: 0,1:17:01.12,1:17:04.24,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-我说了，无罪。  -为什么？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-I told you, not guilty.   -Why?
Dialogue: 0,1:17:06.54,1:17:08.00,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}瞧，我不必……\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Look, I don't have to...
Dialogue: 0,1:17:08.16,1:17:10.54,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你必须说！为什么？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You do have to! Say it! Why?
Dialogue: 0,1:17:11.34,1:17:14.05,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}好吧。我……不认为他有罪。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}All right. I don't... think he's guilty.
Dialogue: 0,1:17:23.30,1:17:24.43,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我要再投一次票。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}! want another vote.
Dialogue: 0,1:17:25.02,1:17:27.48,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}好。有人要求再投一次票。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Okay. There's another vote called for.
Dialogue: 0,1:17:27.64,1:17:29.98,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我想最快的方法就是举手表决。有人反对吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I guess the quickest way is a show of hands. Anyone object?
Dialogue: 0,1:17:30.73,1:17:33.15,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}好。赞成无罪的人，举手。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Okay. All those voting not guilty, raise your hands.
Dialogue: 0,1:17:34.11,1:17:39.90,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}一、二、三、四、五、六、七……\N{\rEN\blur0.8}One, two, three, four, five, six, seven...
Dialogue: 0,1:17:42.32,1:17:43.53,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}八。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}eight.
Dialogue: 0,1:17:48.75,1:17:49.92,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}九。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Nine.
Dialogue: 0,1:17:53.00,1:17:55.25,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}赞成有罪的人，举手。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}All those voting guilty, raise your hands.
Dialogue: 0,1:17:56.13,1:17:57.59,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}一、二、三。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}One, two, three.
Dialogue: 0,1:17:58.76,1:18:00.84,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}表决结果是九比三，赞成无罪。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Well, the vote's nine to three in favor of acquittal.
Dialogue: 0,1:18:02.18,1:18:04.22,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我真搞不懂你们这些人！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I don't understand you people!
Dialogue: 0,1:18:04.39,1:18:06.68,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我是说，你们老抓着这些鸡毛蒜皮的小问题。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I mean, all these picky little points you keep bringing up.
Dialogue: 0,1:18:06.85,1:18:09.94,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}这些根本无关紧要！你们跟我一样都见过这孩子。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}They don't mean nothing! You saw this kid just like I did.
Dialogue: 0,1:18:10.10,1:18:13.69,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你们不会要告诉我，你们相信他编的那套丢刀子的鬼话吧\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You're not gonna tell me you believe that phony story about losing the knife
Dialogue: 0,1:18:13.86,1:18:15.69,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}还有在电影院那套说辞。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}and that business about being at the movies.
Dialogue: 0,1:18:15.86,1:18:18.74,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}听着，你知道这些人怎么撒谎。他们天生就爱撒谎。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Look, you know how these people lie. It's born in them.
Dialogue: 0,1:18:18.90,1:18:20.86,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我是说，搞什么。这还用我说吗。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I mean, what the heck. I don't have to tell you.
Dialogue: 0,1:18:21.03,1:18:22.86,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他们根本不知道什么叫真话。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}They don't know what the truth is.
Dialogue: 0,1:18:23.03,1:18:23.91,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}让我告诉你们，\N{\rEN\blur0.8}And let me tell you,
Dialogue: 0,1:18:24.07,1:18:26.66,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他们杀人也不需要什么真正的大理由。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}they don't need any real big reason to kill someone either.
Dialogue: 0,1:18:26.83,1:18:28.00,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}绝对不需要。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}No, sir.
Dialogue: 0,1:18:28.62,1:18:31.83,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他们喝醉酒！哦，他们个个都是大酒鬼。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}They get drunk! Oh, they're real big drinkers, all of 'em.
Dialogue: 0,1:18:32.00,1:18:34.96,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你知道的。砰，就有人躺在阴沟里。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You know that. And bang, someone's lying in the gutter.
Dialogue: 0,1:18:35.13,1:18:38.05,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}没人怪他们。他们天生就是这样。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Well, nobody's blaming them for it. That's the way they are, by nature.
Dialogue: 0,1:18:38.21,1:18:41.34,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}懂我意思吗？暴力成性！你去哪儿？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You know what I mean? Violent! Where are you going?
Dialogue: 0,1:18:41.84,1:18:44.47,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}人命在他们眼里不如在我们眼里重要。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Human life don't mean as much to them as it does to us.
Dialogue: 0,1:18:45.93,1:18:48.81,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}瞧！他们总是喝得烂醉，整天打架，\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Look! They're lushing it up and fighting all the time,
Dialogue: 0,1:18:48.97,1:18:50.89,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}要是有人被杀，那就被杀呗！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}and if somebody gets killed, so somebody gets killed!
Dialogue: 0,1:18:51.06,1:18:52.23,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他们根本不在乎！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}They don't care!
Dialogue: 0,1:18:52.39,1:18:54.65,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}哦，当然，他们也有好的地方。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Oh, sure, there's some good things about 'em too.
Dialogue: 0,1:18:54.81,1:18:56.48,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}瞧，我第一个承认这一点。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Look, I'm the first one to say that.
Dialogue: 0,1:18:56.65,1:18:58.23,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我认识几个还算不错的人，\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I've Known a couple who were okay,
Dialogue: 0,1:18:58.40,1:19:00.11,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}但那是例外，懂我意思吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}but that's the exception, you know what I mean?
Dialogue: 0,1:19:00.28,1:19:03.11,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他们大多数人就像没感情一样。什么都干得出来。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Most of 'em, it's like they have no feelings. They can do anything.
Dialogue: 0,1:19:04.07,1:19:05.57,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}这里怎么回事？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}What's going on here?
Dialogue: 0,1:19:06.66,1:19:08.28,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我……我是想告诉你们……\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I'm... I'm trying to tell you...
Dialogue: 0,1:19:08.83,1:19:10.45,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你们这些人犯了大错。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}you're making a big mistake, you people.
Dialogue: 0,1:19:10.96,1:19:13.50,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}这孩子是个骗子！我知道。他们那套我全清楚。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}This kid is a liar! I Know it. I know all about them.
Dialogue: 0,1:19:15.67,1:19:17.84,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}听我说。他们都不是好东西。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Listen to me. They're no good.
Dialogue: 0,1:19:18.00,1:19:19.63,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他们没一个是好的。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}There's not a one of 'em who's any good.
Dialogue: 0,1:19:21.67,1:19:24.26,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我是说，这……这里到底怎么了？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I mean, what... what's happening in here?
Dialogue: 0,1:19:24.84,1:19:26.80,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我在说我的看法，而你们……\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I'm speaking my piece, and you...
Dialogue: 0,1:19:28.35,1:19:29.35,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}听我说。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Listen to me.
Dialogue: 0,1:19:32.52,1:19:35.10,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我们……我们……受审这孩子，他那种人……\N{\rEN\blur0.8}We're... we're... This kid on trial here, his type...
Dialogue: 0,1:19:35.27,1:19:36.98,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}嗯……嗯，你们还不了解他们吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Well... well, don't you know about them?
Dialogue: 0,1:19:39.07,1:19:41.61,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}这……这里……这里有危险。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Th... there's... there's a danger here.
Dialogue: 0,1:19:42.57,1:19:44.11,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}这些人是危险分子。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}These people are dangerous.
Dialogue: 0,1:19:44.78,1:19:46.82,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}他们……很野蛮。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}They're... wild.
Dialogue: 0,1:19:47.95,1:19:48.95,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}听我说。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Listen to me.
Dialogue: 0,1:19:49.91,1:19:51.87,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-听着。  -我一直在听。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Listen.   -I have.
Dialogue: 0,1:19:52.45,1:19:55.21,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}现在坐下，别再开口了。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Now sit down and don't open your mouth again.
Dialogue: 0,1:19:58.63,1:20:01.96,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我只是想……告诉你们。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I was only trying to... tell you.
Dialogue: 0,1:20:38.58,1:20:41.50,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}要在这类事情里排除个人偏见\N{\rEN\blur0.8}It's always difficult to keep personal prejudice
Dialogue: 0,1:20:41.67,1:20:42.92,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}总是很难。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}out of a thing like this.
Dialogue: 0,1:20:43.96,1:20:47.51,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}不管在哪儿遇到，偏见总会遮蔽真相。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Wherever you run into it, prejudice always obscures the truth.
Dialogue: 0,1:20:49.55,1:20:51.56,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我并不真的知道真相是什么。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I don't really know what the truth is.
Dialogue: 0,1:20:51.72,1:20:54.85,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我想没人会真正知道。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I don't suppose anybody will ever really know.
Dialogue: 0,1:20:56.31,1:20:59.48,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我们现在似乎有九个人认为被告无罪。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Nine of us now seem to feel that the defendant is innocent.
Dialogue: 0,1:21:00.27,1:21:04.44,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}但我们只是在赌可能性。我们可能错了。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}But we're just gambling on probabilities. We may be wrong.
Dialogue: 0,1:21:05.32,1:21:08.61,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我们可能是在放一个罪人逍遥法外。我不知道。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}We may be trying to let a guilty man go free. I don't know.
Dialogue: 0,1:21:09.20,1:21:10.66,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}没人真能知道。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Nobody really can.
Dialogue: 0,1:21:11.49,1:21:13.16,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}但我们有合理怀疑\N{\rEN\blur0.8}But we have a reasonable doubt
Dialogue: 0,1:21:13.91,1:21:17.54,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}这在我们制度里非常宝贵。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}and that's something that's very valuable in our system.
Dialogue: 0,1:21:17.71,1:21:21.79,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}陪审团除非确信，否则不能宣布一个人有罪。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}No jury can declare a man guilty unless it's sure.
Dialogue: 0,1:21:23.63,1:21:28.38,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我们九个人不明白你们三个为什么还这么肯定。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}We nine can't understand how you three are still so sure.
Dialogue: 0,1:21:29.55,1:21:31.68,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-也许你可以告诉我们。  -我试试。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Maybe you can tell us.   -I'll try.
Dialogue: 0,1:21:33.01,1:21:34.60,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你们提出了一些很好的观点，\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You've made some excellent points,
Dialogue: 0,1:21:34.77,1:21:36.60,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}但我仍然相信这男孩犯有谋杀罪\N{\rEN\blur0.8}but I still believe the boy is guilty of murder
Dialogue: 0,1:21:36.77,1:21:38.19,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我有两个理由。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}and I have two reasons.
Dialogue: 0,1:21:38.35,1:21:41.48,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}第一，街对面那个女人提供的证词\N{\rEN\blur0.8}One, the evidence given by the woman across the street
Dialogue: 0,1:21:41.65,1:21:43.77,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}她亲眼看见了谋杀发生。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}who actually saw the murder committed.
Dialogue: 0,1:21:44.32,1:21:46.86,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}在我看来，那是最重要的证词。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}As far as I'm concerned, that's the most important testimony.
Dialogue: 0,1:21:47.03,1:21:50.16,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}第二，她描述刺杀过程时说\N{\rEN\blur0.8}And two, the fact that she described the stabbing by saying
Dialogue: 0,1:21:50.32,1:21:52.82,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}她看见男孩把手举过头顶\N{\rEN\blur0.8}she saw the boy raise his arm over his head
Dialogue: 0,1:21:52.99,1:21:55.66,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}然后向下刺进父亲的胸口。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}and stab down into the father's chest.
Dialogue: 0,1:21:55.83,1:21:58.00,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}她看见他刺杀的方式不对。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}She saw him do it the wrong way.
Dialogue: 0,1:21:58.16,1:21:59.66,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}完全正确。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}That's absolutely right.
Dialogue: 0,1:22:00.46,1:22:02.25,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我们来谈谈这个女人。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Let's talk about this woman for a moment.
Dialogue: 0,1:22:02.75,1:22:05.88,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}她说那晚大约十一点上床睡觉。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}She said she went to bed about eleven o'clock that night.
Dialogue: 0,1:22:06.05,1:22:09.55,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}她的床靠窗，躺着就能往外看\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Her bed was next to the window, and she could look out while lying down
Dialogue: 0,1:22:09.72,1:22:12.89,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}直接看到街对面男孩的房间。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}and see directly into the boy's room across the street.
Dialogue: 0,1:22:13.80,1:22:16.39,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}她翻来覆去一个多小时，睡不着。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}She tossed and turned for over an hour, unable to sleep.
Dialogue: 0,1:22:16.56,1:22:20.69,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}最后，大约十二点十分，她转向窗户\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Finally, she turned toward the window at about ten minutes after 12:00
Dialogue: 0,1:22:20.85,1:22:22.31,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}往外看时，\N{\rEN\blur0.8}and, as she looked out,
Dialogue: 0,1:22:22.48,1:22:25.36,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}透过一辆驶过的高架列车车窗，她看见了凶杀。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}she saw the killing through the windows of a passing EL train.
Dialogue: 0,1:22:26.07,1:22:28.65,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}她说凶杀发生后灯马上就灭了\N{\rEN\blur0.8}She said the lights went out immediately after the killing
Dialogue: 0,1:22:28.82,1:22:33.66,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}但她清楚地看见了男孩刺向他父亲的那一幕。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}but that she got a good look at the boy in the act of stabbing his father.
Dialogue: 0,1:22:34.58,1:22:38.33,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}在我看来，这是不可动摇的证词。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}As far as I can see it, this is unshakable testimony.
Dialogue: 0,1:22:39.25,1:22:42.00,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-嗯，这就是整个案子。  -你怎么想？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Well, that's the whole case.   -What do you think?
Dialogue: 0,1:22:47.09,1:22:48.26,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你呢？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}How about you?
Dialogue: 0,1:22:50.38,1:22:52.09,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我……我不知道。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I... I don't know.
Dialogue: 0,1:22:53.09,1:22:54.55,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}要筛选的证据太多了。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}So much evidence to sift.
Dialogue: 0,1:22:55.05,1:22:56.89,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}这事相当复杂。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}This is a pretty complicated business.
Dialogue: 0,1:22:57.06,1:23:00.10,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}坦白说，我不明白你们怎么能投无罪。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Frankly, I don't see how you can vote for acquittal.
Dialogue: 0,1:23:01.23,1:23:03.52,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}要把所有证据理清可不容易。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}It's not so easy to arrange all the evidence in order.
Dialogue: 0,1:23:03.69,1:23:05.35,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你可以把所有其他证据都扔掉！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You can throw out all the other evidence!
Dialogue: 0,1:23:05.52,1:23:07.98,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那女人看见他干的！你还想要什么？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}The woman saw him do itt! What else do you want?
Dialogue: 0,1:23:09.19,1:23:10.74,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-是啊，也许吧—— -我们投票吧。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Yeah, well, maybe-- -Let's vote on it.
Dialogue: 0,1:23:11.24,1:23:13.24,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}好，有人要求再投一次。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Okay, there's another vote called for.
Dialogue: 0,1:23:13.40,1:23:14.45,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}有人反对吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Anyone object?
Dialogue: 0,1:23:15.32,1:23:16.99,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}好吧，我改投。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}All right, I'm changing my vote.
Dialogue: 0,1:23:17.70,1:23:19.54,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-他有罪。  -还有别人吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-He's guilty.   -Anybody else?
Dialogue: 0,1:23:19.70,1:23:20.87,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}投票结果是八比四。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}The vote is eight to four.
Dialogue: 0,1:23:21.04,1:23:24.67,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}这一票为什么让你这么得意？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Why is this such a personal triumph for you, this one vote?
Dialogue: 0,1:23:24.83,1:23:28.17,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}好，我认为我们无法达成一致。我们该告诉法官。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Okay, I say we're a hung jury. I say we take it in to the judge.
Dialogue: 0,1:23:28.34,1:23:30.09,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}怎么样？我想听听理由。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}How about it? I wanna hear arguments.
Dialogue: 0,1:23:31.22,1:23:33.26,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你，你是这事的领头人。你说呢？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You, you're the leader of the cause. What about it?
Dialogue: 0,1:23:35.89,1:23:37.01,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我们再过一遍。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Let's go over it again.
Dialogue: 0,1:23:37.72,1:23:39.56,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我们已经过一遍了！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}We've been over it again!
Dialogue: 0,1:23:39.72,1:23:41.48,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}这位穿灰法兰绒西装的男孩\N{\rEN\blur0.8}The boy in the gray flannel suit here
Dialogue: 0,1:23:41.64,1:23:44.44,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}像网球一样来回弹。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}is bouncin' backwards and forwards like a tennis ball.
Dialogue: 0,1:23:44.60,1:23:48.31,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}没必要恶语相向，把它变成比赛。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}No point in getting nasty and trying to turn this into a contest.
Dialogue: 0,1:23:50.53,1:23:51.86,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}好吧。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Okay.
Dialogue: 0,1:23:52.03,1:23:54.40,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}也许我们可以商量设个时间限制。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Maybe we can talk about setting some kind of time limit.
Dialogue: 0,1:23:55.03,1:23:57.07,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}对，每人再说一轮，怎么样？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Yeah, once around for the deal, huh?
Dialogue: 0,1:23:57.99,1:24:01.16,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}现在是……6点15分。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}It's a... quarter after 6:00.
Dialogue: 0,1:24:01.87,1:24:03.87,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}之前有人提到7点。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Someone before mentioned seven o'clock.
Dialogue: 0,1:24:04.04,1:24:06.00,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我想到时候我们可以开始讨论\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I think that's a point at which we might begin to discuss
Dialogue: 0,1:24:06.17,1:24:08.25,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我们是否无法达成一致的问题。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}the question of whether we're a hung jury or not.
Dialogue: 0,1:24:09.71,1:24:11.17,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你不舒服吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Don't you feel well?
Dialogue: 0,1:24:12.71,1:24:14.51,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我很好，谢谢。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I feel perfectly well, thank you.
Dialogue: 0,1:24:14.68,1:24:17.51,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我刚说7点是个合理的时间——\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I was saying that seven o'clock would be a reasonable time--
Dialogue: 0,1:24:17.68,1:24:19.80,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我问这个是因为……\N{\rEN\blur0.8}The reason I asked about that was because...
Dialogue: 0,1:24:20.56,1:24:21.97,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你在搓鼻子，像……\N{\rEN\blur0.8}you were rubbing your nose like...
Dialogue: 0,1:24:22.14,1:24:24.89,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}哦，抱歉打断你，\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Oh, I'm sorry for interrupting,
Dialogue: 0,1:24:25.06,1:24:28.10,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}但你做了个动作让我想起一件事。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}but you made a gesture that reminded me of something.
Dialogue: 0,1:24:28.27,1:24:30.23,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我正想搞清楚点事。你介意吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I'm trying to settle something here. Do you mind?
Dialogue: 0,1:24:30.40,1:24:31.86,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我觉得这很重要。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Well, I think this is important.
Dialogue: 0,1:24:33.57,1:24:34.57,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}谢谢。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,1:24:35.32,1:24:37.99,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那么，请原谅我问这个\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Now then, I'm sure you'll pardon me for this
Dialogue: 0,1:24:38.16,1:24:40.99,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我想知道你为什么要那样搓鼻子？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}but I was wondering why you rub your nose like that?
Dialogue: 0,1:24:41.16,1:24:42.62,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}哦，别这样，行吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Oh, come on, will you?
Dialogue: 0,1:24:42.79,1:24:46.00,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}现在我是在跟你旁边这位先生说话！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}At this point, I happen to be talking to the gentleman sitting next to you!
Dialogue: 0,1:24:47.08,1:24:50.00,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你为什么那样搓鼻子呢？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Now, why were you rubbing your nose like that?
Dialogue: 0,1:24:50.67,1:24:52.25,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}好吧，既然你非要知道，\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Well, if it's any of your business,
Dialogue: 0,1:24:52.42,1:24:54.34,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我搓它是因为它有点不舒服。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I was rubbing it because it bothers me a little.
Dialogue: 0,1:24:54.51,1:24:55.97,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}哦，抱歉。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Oh, I'm sorry.
Dialogue: 0,1:24:56.13,1:24:59.39,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-是因为眼镜吗？  -是的。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Is it because of your eyeglasses?   -It is.
Dialogue: 0,1:24:59.97,1:25:01.85,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}现在能谈别的了吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Now can we get on to something else?
Dialogue: 0,1:25:02.01,1:25:06.64,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你的眼镜在你鼻子两侧留下两道深印。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Your eyeglasses made those two deep impressions on the sides of your nose.
Dialogue: 0,1:25:06.81,1:25:08.40,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我之前没注意到。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I hadn't noticed that before.
Dialogue: 0,1:25:08.98,1:25:12.40,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-那一定很烦人。  -非常烦人。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-That must be annoying.   -It is very annoying.
Dialogue: 0,1:25:12.57,1:25:14.28,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}这我倒不知道。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Well, I wouldn't know about that.
Dialogue: 0,1:25:14.44,1:25:16.15,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我从没戴过眼镜。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I've never worn eyeglasses.
Dialogue: 0,1:25:16.94,1:25:18.07,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}视力2.0。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Twenty-twenty.
Dialogue: 0,1:25:18.24,1:25:20.66,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}听着，你能不能别再说验光师那套了？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Listen, will you come on already with the optometrist bit?
Dialogue: 0,1:25:22.41,1:25:25.45,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那个作证说看到凶案的女人\N{\rEN\blur0.8}The woman who testified that she saw the killing
Dialogue: 0,1:25:26.04,1:25:29.58,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}她鼻子两侧也有同样的印子。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}had those same marks on the sides of her nose.
Dialogue: 0,1:25:30.58,1:25:31.67,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}天哪！他说得对。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Holy smokes! You know, he's right.
Dialogue: 0,1:25:31.84,1:25:34.21,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-拜托。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}- Please.
Dialogue: 0,1:25:34.38,1:25:37.63,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}给我一分钟，我就说完了。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Just give me a minute, and I'll be finished.
Dialogue: 0,1:25:38.55,1:25:40.84,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}不知道别人有没有注意到她这点。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I don't know if anyone else noticed that about her.
Dialogue: 0,1:25:41.51,1:25:45.35,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我当时没想到，但我一直在回想她的脸……\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I didn't think of it then, but I've been going over her face...
Dialogue: 0,1:25:46.31,1:25:47.60,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}在脑子里。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}in my mind.
Dialogue: 0,1:25:48.48,1:25:50.60,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}她也有同样的印子。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}She had those same marks.
Dialogue: 0,1:25:51.48,1:25:55.65,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-她在法庭上一直搓。  -他说得对！她确实老那样。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-She kept rubbing them in court.   -He's right! Now, she did do that a lot.
Dialogue: 0,1:25:56.69,1:26:00.66,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}这女人大约……大约45岁。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}This woman was about... about 45 years old.
Dialogue: 0,1:26:01.45,1:26:05.12,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}她极力想让自己看起来像35岁\N{\rEN\blur0.8}She was making a tremendous effort to look 35
Dialogue: 0,1:26:05.66,1:26:07.41,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}为了她第一次公开露面。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}for her first public appearance.
Dialogue: 0,1:26:08.04,1:26:10.67,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}浓妆、染发\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Heavy makeup, dyed hair
Dialogue: 0,1:26:11.21,1:26:14.59,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}崭新的衣服，本该穿在更年轻的女人身上。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}brand-new clothes that should have been worn by a younger woman.
Dialogue: 0,1:26:15.21,1:26:17.96,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}没戴眼镜。不，女人都这样。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}No glasses. No, women do that.
Dialogue: 0,1:26:18.84,1:26:21.01,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你们能想象出来吗。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}See if you can get the mental picture of it.
Dialogue: 0,1:26:21.18,1:26:22.72,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你说没戴眼镜是什么意思？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}What do you mean, no glasses?
Dialogue: 0,1:26:23.26,1:26:26.18,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你怎么知道她戴没戴眼镜？就因为她搓鼻子？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}How do you know whether she wore glasses? Just 'cause she was rubbing her nose?
Dialogue: 0,1:26:26.35,1:26:28.23,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}她有那些印子。我看到了。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Now, she had those marks. I saw 'em.
Dialogue: 0,1:26:28.39,1:26:30.06,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那又怎样？你觉得这能说明什么？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}So what? What do you think that means?
Dialogue: 0,1:26:30.23,1:26:31.77,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}听着，我受够了你在这儿大喊大叫！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Listen, I'm getting so sick of your yelling in here!
Dialogue: 0,1:26:31.94,1:26:33.31,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}行了，算了吧。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Come on. Forget it.
Dialogue: 0,1:26:33.48,1:26:36.44,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}嘿，听着。听着，他……他说得对。我也看到了。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Hey, listen. Listen, he's... he's right. I saw them too.
Dialogue: 0,1:26:36.61,1:26:37.98,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我当时离她最近。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I was the closest one to her.
Dialogue: 0,1:26:38.15,1:26:39.82,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}她鼻子两侧有……这些东西。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}She had these... these things on the side of her nose.
Dialogue: 0,1:26:39.99,1:26:42.99,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-鼻子两侧那个叫什么？  -你到底想说明什么？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-What do you call those on the side?   -Well, what point are you making here?
Dialogue: 0,1:26:43.16,1:26:46.95,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}她染了发，鼻子上有印子。那又怎么样？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}She had dyed hair, marks on her nose. Well, what does that mean?
Dialogue: 0,1:26:47.12,1:26:51.25,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那些印子除了眼镜还能是别的什么弄的吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Could those marks be made by anything other than eyeglasses?
Dialogue: 0,1:26:54.79,1:26:56.59,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}不可能。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}No, they couldn't.
Dialogue: 0,1:26:57.30,1:26:59.09,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我没看到什么印子！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I didn't see any marks!
Dialogue: 0,1:27:00.84,1:27:01.88,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我看到了。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I did.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:02.63,1:27:04.59,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}奇怪，我之前没想到。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Strange, but I didn't think about it before.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:05.34,1:27:07.72,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那律师呢？他怎么没提？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Well, what about the lawyer? Why didn't he say something?
Dialogue: 0,1:27:07.89,1:27:10.56,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}这里有12个人在专心研究这案子。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}There are 12 people in here concentrating on this case.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:10.73,1:27:12.64,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我们11个人也没想到。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Eleven of us didn't think of it either.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:12.81,1:27:15.81,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那地方检察官呢？你觉得他会耍这种花招？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Well, what about the district attorney? Do you think he'd pull a trick like that?
Dialogue: 0,1:27:15.98,1:27:17.90,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}让她不戴眼镜作证？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Have her testify without her glasses?
Dialogue: 0,1:27:18.07,1:27:19.65,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你见过哪个女人必须戴眼镜\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Did you ever see a woman who had to wear glasses
Dialogue: 0,1:27:19.82,1:27:22.20,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}却因为觉得影响容貌而不愿戴？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}and didn't want to because she thinks they spoil her looks?
Dialogue: 0,1:27:22.36,1:27:25.57,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}好。她鼻子上有印子。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Okay. She had marks on her nose.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:25.74,1:27:28.70,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}这点我认。是眼镜弄的，对吧？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I'm giving you that. From glasses, right?
Dialogue: 0,1:27:29.49,1:27:30.83,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}她不想戴着它们出门\N{\rEN\blur0.8}She didn't want to wear 'em out of the house
Dialogue: 0,1:27:31.00,1:27:32.79,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}好让人觉得她漂亮。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}so people would think she's gorgeous.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:33.83,1:27:37.71,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}但她看到这男孩杀他父亲时，她独自在家。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}But when she saw this kid killing his father, she was in the house alone.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:38.38,1:27:39.50,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}就这样。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}That's all.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:40.67,1:27:44.59,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-你睡觉戴眼镜吗？  -不戴。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Do you wear glasses when you go to bed?   -No, I don't.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:46.34,1:27:48.18,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}没人睡觉戴眼镜。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}No one wears eyeglasses to bed.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:48.35,1:27:51.02,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}按理说她躺在床上时没戴眼镜\N{\rEN\blur0.8}It's logical to assume that she wasn't wearing them when she was in bed
Dialogue: 0,1:27:51.18,1:27:52.98,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}辗转反侧想入睡。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}tossing and turning, trying to fall asleep.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:53.14,1:27:55.44,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-你怎么知道？  -我不知道！我猜的。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-How do you know?   -I don't know! I'm guessing.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:55.60,1:27:58.11,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我还猜她很可能没戴眼镜\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I'm also guessing that she probably didn't put her glasses on
Dialogue: 0,1:27:58.27,1:28:00.11,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}当她转头随意往窗外看的时候。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}when she turned to look casually out of the window.
Dialogue: 0,1:28:00.28,1:28:03.32,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}而且她自己作证说，她往外看时凶案正好发生。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}And she herself testified the killing took place just as she looked out.
Dialogue: 0,1:28:03.49,1:28:04.74,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}灯在一瞬间后就灭了。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}The lights went off a split second later.
Dialogue: 0,1:28:04.90,1:28:06.07,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那她根本来不及戴上眼镜。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}She couldn't have had time to put them on then.
Dialogue: 0,1:28:06.24,1:28:07.82,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-等等。  -再猜一个。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Wait a second.   -Here's another guess.
Dialogue: 0,1:28:07.99,1:28:10.45,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}也许她真以为自己看到那男孩杀了他父亲。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Maybe she honestly thought she saw the boy kill his father.
Dialogue: 0,1:28:10.62,1:28:12.12,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我说她只看到一团模糊的影子。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I say she only saw a blur.
Dialogue: 0,1:28:12.29,1:28:15.33,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你怎么知道她看到了什么？他怎么知道这些？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}How do you know what she saw? How does he know all that?
Dialogue: 0,1:28:15.96,1:28:17.58,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你怎么知道她戴的是什么眼镜？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}How do you know what kind of glasses she wore?
Dialogue: 0,1:28:17.75,1:28:20.34,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}也许是墨镜。也许她是远视。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Maybe they were sunglasses. Maybe she was farsighted.
Dialogue: 0,1:28:20.50,1:28:21.67,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你懂什么？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}What do you know about it?
Dialogue: 0,1:28:21.84,1:28:24.76,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我只知道这女人的视力现在有问题。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I only know the woman's eyesight is in question now.
Dialogue: 0,1:28:24.92,1:28:30.85,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}她得在夜里不戴眼镜认出六十英尺外的人。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}She had to be able to identify a person 60 feet away, at night, without glasses.
Dialogue: 0,1:28:31.01,1:28:33.64,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}不能凭这种证据送人去死。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You can't send someone off to die on evidence like that.
Dialogue: 0,1:28:33.81,1:28:35.60,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}哦，少来这套。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Oh, don't give me that.
Dialogue: 0,1:28:35.77,1:28:37.77,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你不觉得那女人可能弄错了吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Don't you think the woman might have made a mistake?
Dialogue: 0,1:28:37.94,1:28:40.23,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-不。  -不可能吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-No.   -It's not possible?
Dialogue: 0,1:28:40.40,1:28:41.86,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}不，不可能。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}No, it's not possible.
Dialogue: 0,1:28:44.99,1:28:46.28,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}有可能吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Is it possible?
Dialogue: 0,1:28:48.03,1:28:49.20,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}无罪。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Not guilty.
Dialogue: 0,1:28:53.79,1:28:55.08,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你觉得他有罪吗？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Do you think he's guilty?
Dialogue: 0,1:28:56.50,1:28:58.00,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我觉得他有罪。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I think he's guilty.
Dialogue: 0,1:29:01.21,1:29:02.42,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你呢？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Do you?
Dialogue: 0,1:29:05.80,1:29:08.51,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}不。我确信他无罪。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}No. I'm convinced.
Dialogue: 0,1:29:09.22,1:29:11.80,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-无罪。  -你怎么了？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-Not guilty.   -What's the matter with you?
Dialogue: 0,1:29:12.47,1:29:14.31,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我现在有合理怀疑了。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I have a reasonable doubt now.
Dialogue: 0,1:29:14.47,1:29:15.89,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}十一比一。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Eleven to one.
Dialogue: 0,1:29:16.06,1:29:19.06,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那其他证据呢？那些东西呢？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Well, what about all the other evidence? What about all that stuff?
Dialogue: 0,1:29:19.23,1:29:21.23,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那……那把刀，所有的事！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}The... the knife, the whole business!
Dialogue: 0,1:29:21.40,1:29:23.69,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你不是说其他证据都可以抛开吗。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Well, you said we could throw out all the other evidence.
Dialogue: 0,1:29:29.91,1:29:31.87,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那现在怎么办？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Well, what do we do now?
Dialogue: 0,1:29:35.20,1:29:36.41,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}就你一个人。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You're alone.
Dialogue: 0,1:29:37.33,1:29:39.33,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我不在乎是不是只有我一个！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I don't care whether I'm alone or not!
Dialogue: 0,1:29:39.50,1:29:40.62,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}这是我的权利。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}It's my right.
Dialogue: 0,1:29:43.88,1:29:45.17,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}这是你的权利。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}It's your right.
Dialogue: 0,1:29:55.22,1:29:57.31,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那你们想怎样？我说他有罪。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Well, what do you want? I say he's guilty.
Dialogue: 0,1:29:59.31,1:30:02.86,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-我们想听你的理由。  -我已经说过理由了。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-We want to hear your arguments.   -I gave you my arguments.
Dialogue: 0,1:30:03.82,1:30:05.23,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我们没被说服。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}We're not convinced.
Dialogue: 0,1:30:05.90,1:30:07.28,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我们想再听一遍。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}We want to hear them again.
Dialogue: 0,1:30:08.61,1:30:10.49,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我们有的是时间。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}We have as much time as it takes.
Dialogue: 0,1:30:16.29,1:30:17.54,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}所有的一切。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Everything.
Dialogue: 0,1:30:17.70,1:30:21.04,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}法庭上发生的每一件事，\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Every single thing that took place in that courtroom,
Dialogue: 0,1:30:21.21,1:30:22.88,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我是说每一件事，都说明他有罪。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}but I mean everything, says he's guilty.
Dialogue: 0,1:30:23.04,1:30:24.92,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你们以为我是白痴还是什么？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}What do you think, I'm an idiot or something?
Dialogue: 0,1:30:27.05,1:30:29.13,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你们怎么不谈谈那个老头的事？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Why don't you take that stuff about the old man?
Dialogue: 0,1:30:29.30,1:30:32.30,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}住在那儿、什么都听见了的老头！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}The old man who lived there and heard everything!
Dialogue: 0,1:30:34.10,1:30:35.39,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}还有那把刀的事。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Or this business about the knife.
Dialogue: 0,1:30:35.56,1:30:37.68,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}什么？就因为他找到一把一模一样的？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}What? 'Cause he found another one exactly like it?
Dialogue: 0,1:30:37.85,1:30:40.89,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那老头看见他就在楼梯那儿！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}The old man saw him right there on the stairs!
Dialogue: 0,1:30:41.44,1:30:43.60,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}差几秒钟又有什么区别？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}What's the difference how many seconds it was?
Dialogue: 0,1:30:45.27,1:30:47.15,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}每一件事。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Every single thing.
Dialogue: 0,1:30:48.61,1:30:51.57,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}刀从他口袋的破洞掉出来。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}The knife falling through a hole in his pocket.
Dialogue: 0,1:30:52.11,1:30:54.57,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你没法证明他没走到门口。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You can't prove he didn't get to the door.
Dialogue: 0,1:30:55.53,1:30:57.87,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}当然，你可以慢慢来，在房间里一瘸一拐地走。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Sure, you can take all the time, hobble around the room.
Dialogue: 0,1:30:58.04,1:30:59.91,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}但你证明不了！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}But you can't prove it!
Dialogue: 0,1:31:02.87,1:31:06.04,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}还有那高架列车和电影的事？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}And what about this business of the EL and the movies?
Dialogue: 0,1:31:06.21,1:31:08.59,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我从来没听过这么假的说法。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}There's a phony deal if I ever heard one.
Dialogue: 0,1:31:09.30,1:31:13.47,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我跟你赌五千块，我肯定记得自己看过什么电影。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I'll bet you 5,000 dollars I'd remember the movies I saw.
Dialogue: 0,1:31:13.64,1:31:19.06,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我跟你们说，发生的一切都被扭曲了！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I'm telling you, everything that's gone on has been twisted and turned!
Dialogue: 0,1:31:19.77,1:31:21.77,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}还有眼镜这档子事？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}This business with the glasses?
Dialogue: 0,1:31:21.94,1:31:26.36,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你怎么知道她没戴？这女人可是在公开法庭上作证的！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}How do you know she didn't have them on? This woman testified in open court!
Dialogue: 0,1:31:27.73,1:31:30.94,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}还有听见那孩子喊叫的事呢？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}And what about hearing the kid yell, huh?
Dialogue: 0,1:31:31.70,1:31:34.61,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我跟你们说，所有事实都在这儿。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I'm telling you, I've got all the facts here.
Dialogue: 0,1:31:36.07,1:31:38.20,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}这儿。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Here.
Dialogue: 0,1:31:40.24,1:31:42.41,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}好了，就这些！整个案子就这样。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Well, that's it! That's the whole case.
Dialogue: 0,1:31:50.05,1:31:51.21,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}怎么样？\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Well?
Dialogue: 0,1:31:53.97,1:31:55.26,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}说句话啊！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Say something!
Dialogue: 0,1:32:01.02,1:32:04.73,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你们这帮烂好人。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You lousy bunch of bleeding hearts.
Dialogue: 0,1:32:05.23,1:32:07.23,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}你们吓不倒我。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}You're not gonna intimidate me.
Dialogue: 0,1:32:07.40,1:32:09.40,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我有权坚持自己的看法。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I'm entitled to my opinion.
Dialogue: 0,1:32:13.19,1:32:17.03,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}臭小子。你一辈子辛辛苦苦！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Rotten kids. You work your life out!
Dialogue: 0,1:32:22.16,1:32:23.83,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我没法再……\N{\rEN\blur0.8}I can't keep...
Dialogue: 0,1:32:28.88,1:32:30.00,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}不。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}No.
Dialogue: 0,1:32:34.59,1:32:35.88,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}无罪。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Not guilty.
Dialogue: 0,1:32:39.72,1:32:40.93,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}无罪。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Not guilty.
Dialogue: 0,1:32:44.43,1:32:45.56,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}不……\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Not...
Dialogue: 0,1:32:56.57,1:32:58.28,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我们准备好了。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}We're ready now.
Dialogue: 0,1:32:58.45,1:33:00.66,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}是\N{\rEN\blur0.8}IS
Dialogue: 0,1:33:29.81,1:33:32.11,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}J\N{\rEN\blur0.8}J
Dialogue: 0,1:34:52.27,1:34:53.48,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}嘿！\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Hey!
Dialogue: 0,1:34:58.40,1:35:00.94,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}-你叫什么名字？  -戴维斯。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}-What's your name?   -Davis.
Dialogue: 0,1:35:01.61,1:35:03.07,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}我叫麦卡德尔。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}My name's McCardle.
Dialogue: 0,1:35:05.99,1:35:07.45,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}那，再见了。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}Well, so long.
Dialogue: 0,1:35:07.62,1:35:08.62,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}再见。\N{\rEN\blur0.8}So long.
Dialogue: 0,1:35:11.83,1:35:14.17,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\rZH\blur0.8}ff\N{\rEN\blur0.8}ff
